      "subject": "fix(cli): accept JSON files for web capture and screenshot comparisons (#1397)",
      "body": "fix(cli): accept JSON files for web capture and screenshot comparisons (#1397)\n\ncompare-web-captures and compare-web-screenshots parsed their arguments as\ninline JSON only, unlike every other JSON-input command. Screenshot\nartifacts and scenario captures embed base64 PNG bytes, so a typical\nviewport screenshot exceeds the command-line length limit (128 KiB per\nargument on Linux, 1 MiB total on macOS) and could not be compared from\nthe CLI at all, while MCP accepts it. A file path was reported as\nmalformed JSON, and screenshot schema failures returned no issues.\n\nEach argument now accepts inline JSON or a JSON file path through\nparseCliJsonInput; file failures keep its path diagnostics, malformed\ninline JSON keeps the field issue, and screenshot validation reports\nprojected schema issues. The tests share one CLI JSON process fixture.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
