      "subject": "perf(evidence): stop copying normalized results into raw_result (#1402)",
      "body": "perf(evidence): stop copying normalized results into raw_result (#1402)\n\ncreateAnalysisExecution defaulted an omitted rawResult to a second\ncomplete copy of the result. Every caller that had no distinct provider\nrepresentation therefore doubled its Evidence: decode_interface_builder,\ninspect_keyed_archive, inspect_asset_catalog, trace_dylib_resolution,\ninspect_native_dispatch_metadata, observe_native_calls,\nobserve_native_ui/capture_native_ui_scenario (including screenshots), and\nsmall Ghidra/IDA lifecycle records. Sibling operations of the same\nproviders already recorded null.\n\nAn omitted rawResult now records null. Normalized results are unchanged.\nMCP responses repeat Evidence in text and structured content, so each\nresponse and its share of the 10 MiB transport budget shrink by the same\nhalf; e.g. trace_dylib_resolution on a real app bundle drops from\n3,217,119 to 1,612,524 bytes per representation.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
