    {
      "sha": "e10c934d5a756c1a4c7b547ebd02c403ddfde7b8",
      "subject": "fix(ghidra): keep the cross-format branch callee multi-block",
      "body": "fix(ghidra): keep the cross-format branch callee multi-block\n\nThe cross-format oracle requires a callee whose recovered control flow\nhas more than one basic block, and rea_cross_branch provided it through\na symmetric if/else of tail calls. Clang 21 folds that shape into a\nconditional negate plus one tail branch, a single basic block, so the\nlane rejected a correct Ghidra analysis of the fixture.\n\nGive the branch a loop whose trip count depends on a volatile global:\nno compiler can eliminate the backedge, and the callee stays multi-block\nat every optimization level on every toolchain.\n",
      "parents": ["08ec2bf82fa88f5e8caa2b7da9093636731dc55c"],
