    {
      "sha": "e4a8e0b728154fe0bf181684ccd0d73df45cf4bf",
      "subject": "fix(javascript): recognize Electron APIs through renamed bindings",
      "body": "fix(javascript): recognize Electron APIs through renamed bindings\n\nElectron recognition matched callee spellings, so a bundler rename such as\nesbuild's `import { ipcMain as ipcMain2 } from \"electron\"`, or a destructured\n`const { contextBridge: bridge } = require(\"electron\")`, hid every IPC\nhandler, BrowserWindow, contextBridge and utility process behind it.\n\nResolve each call and construction root lexically to its Electron import or\nrequire origin, and classify the callee under that export's name. Shadowed\nlocals keep their own meaning.\n\nOn Hermes Desktop v0.21.6, whose main process is one esbuild ESM bundle,\nrecognized main IPC handlers rise from 1 to 204, BrowserWindow constructions\nfrom 0 to 11, and paired renderer transmissions from 1 to 201.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01XPY2GmufMNGQKoEgRUx1pd\n",
