      "body": "fix(javascript): stop replaying earlier writes for each object property write\n\nRepeated property writes to one object made member-mutation collection\ncubic. Each write evaluated its target binding to rule out a primitive,\nand every evaluation folded all earlier mutation paths, copying every\nslot once per path. 2,000 writes to one object took 27 s and 4,000 took\n203 s.\n\n- A recorded write always leaves a non-primitive binding value, so only\n  the first write to a binding needs the primitive check.\n- Apply mutation paths per slot in one pass with the same ordering\n  semantics instead of one full slot copy per path.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: N0zoM1z0 <161784452+N0zoM1z0@users.noreply.github.com>",
