      "sha": "2781cad20125ff3a210b795f60620b048e1bbe9b",
      "subject": "perf(process): stop padding rendered terminal lines to full width (#1450)",
      "body": "perf(process): stop padding rendered terminal lines to full width (#1450)\n\nRendered frames padded every visible row with trailing spaces to the\nterminal width. Blank rows cost a full row each and every frame repeats\nthem, so the padding made up 14-39% of capture Evidence (2 KB of sparse\noutput produced 228 KB). The padding carried no information: columns is\nrecorded and serialized_state keeps the exact terminal state.\n\nLines are now trimmed after normalization, so line.padEnd(columns)\nrestores the previous value. The comparison contract commits\nrendered_line_format so older padded captures do not compare as the\nsame contract.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
