      "sha": "ef96657d6ba0c1f22ebdb1e6bd4d9a6ac9335002",
      "subject": "perf(javascript): hash each semantic evidence context once (#1457)",
      "body": "perf(javascript): hash each semantic evidence context once (#1457)\n\nThe semantic graph's evidence-context registry canonicalized the full\nprovenance context three times for every node, relation, unknown and\nfingerprint: once to hash its ID and twice more to compare against the\nstored row. A file has only a few distinct contexts, so nearly all of\nthat work repeated a known answer.\n\nInterning now keys contexts by their canonical text. Each fact\ncanonicalizes once, and only a new context is hashed and checked for a\ndigest collision. IDs and output are unchanged; Obsidian's 334 MB\nEvidence is byte-identical and analysis drops from about 47.0 s to\n44.4 s.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
