      "subject": "perf(javascript)!: stop repeating the semantic identifier strategy per fact (#1474)",
      "body": "perf(javascript)!: stop repeating the semantic identifier strategy per fact (#1474)\n\nEvery semantic graph node and relation carried an identifier_strategy\nobject whose schema admits exactly one value per record type. The\nconstant made up about 9% of analyze_javascript_application output\n(Obsidian app.asar: 12.04 MB to 10.96 MB), and semantic traces repeated\nit on every returned fact.\n\nThe node_id and relation_id schema descriptions now state how each\nidentifier is derived.\n\nBREAKING CHANGE: Semantic graph nodes and relations no longer include\nidentifier_strategy, and relation IDs no longer hash that constant.\nEvidence recorded by earlier versions does not validate against the new\nsemantic graph schema.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
