      "subject": "perf(mcp): stop advertising placeholder input descriptions (#1479)",
      "body": "perf(mcp): stop advertising placeholder input descriptions (#1479)\n\nInput schema presentation gave every undescribed property a generic\n\"Value for <name>.\" sentence. That only restates the property name, yet\nit covered 1,958 properties: 70 KB of the 522 KB of advertised input\nschemas that clients load into model context. Authored descriptions,\nreferenced descriptions, and the name-pattern sentences that add meaning\n(maximums, digests, paths, Evidence IDs) remain; other properties now\nadvertise no description.\n\nThe schema validity test now rejects placeholder descriptions instead of\nrequiring a description on every property.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
