      "sha": "f970b886aace516383caaa6d974f9df63faff340",
      "subject": "feat: add Hermes as a supported MCP client (#1403)",
      "body": "feat: add Hermes as a supported MCP client (#1403)\n\n* feat: add Hermes as a supported MCP client\n\nHermes Agent reads stdio MCP servers from `mcp_servers.<name>` in\n`config.yaml`. REA had no Hermes client, so setup could not register it and\nHermes users had to wire the server up by hand.\n\n- SupportedClients: add the `hermes` format and client definition, resolving\n  the config path from HERMES_HOME, else the platform default that Hermes's own\n  resolver uses (LOCALAPPDATA/hermes on Windows, ~/.hermes elsewhere), including\n  HERMES_DATA_DIR_SUFFIX.\n- ClientConfigurationDocument: parse and serialize Hermes YAML, upserting the\n  rea entry into the parsed document so user comments and unrelated settings are\n  preserved; emit `enabled: true` since Hermes connects entries unless disabled.\n- ClientRegistrationStatus: forward the Hermes location variables so status\n  checks resolve the same path as setup.\n- Tests: cover path resolution on both platforms and the register/read/uninstall\n  round trip, and clear the Hermes location variables between tests.\n\n- delilah 🌸\n\n* docs: document the Hermes client and its config path\n\n- delilah 🌸\n\n* refactor(setup): resolve skill destinations per client\n\n* fix(setup): install Hermes skills in the active profile\n\n* fix(setup): identify each client skill action uniquely\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: morluto <76467478+morluto@users.noreply.github.com>",
