      "sha": "9e22da845bf8b447f81539e0ba57d5deb59e9103",
      "subject": "feat(setup): add native Pi client support (#1376)",
      "body": "feat(setup): add native Pi client support (#1376)\n\n* feat(setup): add native Pi client support\n\n* fix(setup): isolate invalid Pi agent directory overrides\n\nKeep malformed Pi path evidence on its client entry so unrelated selected clients can complete setup and doctor. Preserve explicit Pi rejection and block filesystem operations rather than falling back to another directory.\n\n* fix(setup): parse Pi configuration as strict JSON\n\nPi's installed MCP loader reads mcp.json with a bare JSON.parse and no\nBOM tolerance, so comments, trailing commas, a BOM, or an empty existing\nfile yield loader errors and no servers. Parsing the Pi dialect with\nobjectSchema.parse(JSON.parse(text)) before the shared empty/JSONC\nshortcut rejects those files at every mutation boundary instead of\nreporting configured registrations Pi cannot load. A missing file still\ninitializes a fresh strict-JSON document, other dialects keep their\nJSONC/BOM/empty tolerance, and malformed files are never rewritten.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: morluto <76467478+morluto@users.noreply.github.com>",
