      "sha": "983b070d4d5c6179526f3b24e20c9d344388b786",
      "subject": "fix(artifacts): record each case collision once at its diverging segment (#1505)",
      "body": "fix(artifacts): record each case collision once at its diverging segment (#1505)\n\nInventory paired every path under one case spelling with every path under\neach other spelling and listed all of them on each occurrence. An archive\nwith Foo/ and foo/ subtrees of N files each produced N-entry lists on 2N\noccurrences: 4,000 such ZIP members yielded a 120 MB inspect_artifact\nresult and close to 1 GB of memory. The trie walks also recursed once per\npath component, so a ZIP name with tens of thousands of components threw\nRangeError.\n\nA collision is now recorded at the segment where spellings diverge and\nshared down that subtree by an iterative walk. Each occurrence names the\ncolliding prefix and the first other spelling, plus a count of further\nspellings, each of which is its own occurrence.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
