    {
      "sha": "93ca276921cb6bd1ebfa0431369633c0a428bde5",
      "subject": "fix(browser): accept HAR files that begin with a byte-order mark (#1509)",
      "body": "fix(browser): accept HAR files that begin with a byte-order mark (#1509)\n\nHAR 1.2 lets writers emit a UTF-8 byte-order mark and requires readers to\nignore it. The decoder passed ignoreBOM: true to TextDecoder, which keeps\nthe mark in the decoded text, so a BOM-prefixed export failed as \"HAR is\nmalformed JSON.\" Decoding now uses the default, which skips one leading\nmark. The artifact digest still covers the selected file bytes.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
