    {
      "sha": "a936303723939478cbc8ebd7068ce32ef6eb1028",
      "subject": "fix(json): name a leading byte-order mark in rejected JSON input (#1510)",
      "body": "fix(json): name a leading byte-order mark in rejected JSON input (#1510)\n\nStrict JSON file inputs reject a leading UTF-8 byte-order mark, but the\ndiagnostic was the parser's own message, which quotes the invisible U+FEFF\nas the unexpected token: Unexpected token '', \"{\"invento\"... is not\nvalid JSON. Editors such as Windows PowerShell 5.1 write that mark by\ndefault, and nothing in the message showed it.\n\nCLI JSON files (whole and streamed), Evidence and snapshot JSON files, and\nprocess scenario files now report that the input begins with a UTF-8\nbyte-order mark and how to save it. Acceptance is unchanged.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
