      "sha": "2bf812772d7209e31e15198bc3383243ad879f39",
      "subject": "fix(apple): bound binary plist expansion before decoding keyed archives (#1515)",
      "body": "fix(apple): bound binary plist expansion before decoding keyed archives (#1515)\n\ninspect_keyed_archive passed caller-selected binary plists straight to\nplist.parseBinary, which recurses on every object reference and copies\nshared containers. A 484-byte archive of forty nested [next, next] arrays\ngrew the process past 4 GB until it died with no result, which would also\nend an MCP server. A 125-byte self-referencing array overflowed the stack\nand was reported as an artifact too large to process.\n\nThe iterative reference walk that already guards decode_interface_builder\nnow runs first, with an 8x keyed-archive decode budget. Over-budget depth\nor expansion is a limit; a reference cycle is a malformed archive. Its\n\"decoder\" bounds admit the same layouts plist.parseBinary reads, so\naccepted archives stay accepted. Interface Builder behavior is unchanged.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
