      "sha": "f51503ef1c4b0b7e8b00bf413d5a4436c8bc1d87",
      "subject": "fix(process): normalize scenario replacements literally",
      "body": "fix(process): normalize scenario replacements literally\n\ncapture_process_scenario declares normalization patterns as literal text, but\\nreplaceAll expands \\$&\\, \\$\\`, and \\$1\\ in the replacement as a replacement\\npattern. A caller normalizing text that contains a dollar sign silently gets\\nduplicated, spliced, or dropped content in the recorded Evidence instead of\\nthe requested literal replacement.\\n\\nUse split/join, which is literal on both sides and is already the idiom used\\nfor exact-literal scenario rules in browserScenarioNormalization.ts.\n",
