      "sha": "b4db35f092d7166aebdf4387b48f7652b1d1c3b6",
      "subject": "fix: bind identity and coverage to the producing rule (#1513)",
      "body": "fix: bind identity and coverage to the producing rule (#1513)\n\n* fix: bind identity and coverage to the producing rule\n\nLogical paths, container families, examined bytes, path-segment conventions, destination collisions, file-id leases, Mach-O CPU selection, and firmware cleanup now follow the observation that owns each rule.\n\n* fix: fail unmatched Mach-O slices and keep firmware roots independent\n\nA fat target whose architecture lipo did not list now stops before slice tools run. Chained fixups still count unread LC_DYLD_INFO rebase bytes, and a firmware cleanup failure no longer blocks the next workspace.\n\n* test: cover path identity and runtime families at the projection boundary\n\nNFC joins and segment conventions are now asserted by the path resolver, the Apple projection, and a real APK inventory instead of helper unit tests.\n\n* test: expect unread dyld rebase bytes in the Apple dispatch fixture\n\nThe legacy LC_DYLD_INFO fixture keeps a rebase range this reader does not decode, so the public CLI and MCP check now requires that partial coverage beside the bind opcodes.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>",
