      "sha": "46c9cba03a52b8ec382a686cd70ded6128225db8",
      "subject": "fix(javascript): expand an escaped receiver's methods once (#1495) (#1517)",
      "body": "fix(javascript): expand an escaped receiver's methods once (#1495) (#1517)\n\nSince #1471, escaping an object also escapes every method's results. Each\ncall through the object escapes it as the receiver, and each escape\nre-expanded all of its methods. N methods returning one shared object,\neach called once, did N times N work: 2,000 calls took 3.0 s of semantic\nanalysis and 4,000 took 12 s.\n\nExpansion below references depends only on syntax, so escapes now reuse\nit per expression and path. Identifiers that resolve to the same binding\nand path collapse to one, because the escape walk treats them alike.\nEvery escape site is still recorded. The semantic IR is byte-identical\non 50 sources, and the issue's case takes 253 ms at 2,000 and 638 ms at\n4,000.\n\nCloses #1495\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
