      "sha": "5fdb0636b4734cabfa3147e8fcc94976c3bd8aa4",
      "subject": "fix(javascript): yield during per-file projection and graph construction (#1525)",
      "body": "fix(javascript): yield during per-file projection and graph construction (#1525)\n\nanalyze_javascript_application ran several long phases with no event-loop\nturn, so MCP ping and cancellation waited: each file's parse, analysis and\nsemantic projection; building every application node and relationship\nbefore the application graph's first sealing step; and whole-graph schema\nparses inside both immutable graph factories.\n\n- Each file runs as steps (parse, static analysis, semantic analysis, then\n  each projection pass), driven by the existing time-sliced checkpoint.\n- Application graph input construction yields between phases, per module\n  link and per file of findings.\n- The pipeline transfers its privately built graph inputs to new sealing\n  steps that validate the graph's own fields synchronously and elements,\n  content checks and the digest in steps. The public copying factories\n  keep their synchronous capture.\n\nResults are unchanged: graph IDs and the complete result digest match main\non five inputs including Obsidian's 23 MB obsidian.asar. On the issue's\n1,200-function fixture the longest event-loop block falls from about\n290 ms to 90 ms, and ping after abort from up to 286 ms to at most 56 ms.\nOn obsidian.asar it falls from 10.9 s to 5.4 s; the rest is one analyzer\nstage of a single very large file.\n\nRefs #1462\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: N0zoM1z0 <161784452+N0zoM1z0@users.noreply.github.com>",
