      "sha": "ca7ef69c0ceed367470cb2d8e867a33e61706b02",
      "subject": "fix(javascript): yield inside semantic analysis and large projection passes (#1542)",
      "body": "fix(javascript): yield inside semantic analysis and large projection passes (#1542)\n\n* fix(javascript): yield inside semantic analysis and large projection passes\n\nAfter #1525 the longest event-loop blocks were single stages on very large\nfiles: semantic analysis of Obsidian's 3.7 MB app.js ran 5.8 s in one piece,\nand its object projection 1.8 s.\n\n- analyzeParsedJavaScriptSemanticsSteps yields between the analysis phases\n  and between the eight derived collectors; the synchronous function drains\n  it, so results are unchanged.\n- Per-file analysis yields between open-receiver classification and static\n  analysis and drives the semantic steps.\n- Semantic node creation, definitions and references, and the object and\n  frontier passes yield every 64 items. Node creation keeps source order,\n  which the per-file node budget depends on.\n\nOn obsidian.asar the longest block falls from 5,355 ms to 907 ms with the\nsame total time (40.6 s to 39.5 s). Graph IDs and complete result digests\nmatch main on five inputs. Remaining blocks up to about 0.9 s are single\nAST traversal passes inside the analyzers.\n\nRefs #1462\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(javascript): drop the unused synchronous derived-semantics wrapper\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
