      "sha": "4b985e5021f578e6ef0bc2a412abe9cba6bdaca1",
      "subject": "fix(artifacts): take nested container families from bytes (#1553)",
      "body": "fix(artifacts): take nested container families from bytes (#1553)\n\nInventory gave nested members a ZIP or ASAR family from their path\nsuffix. Byte classification replaced it only for ZIP magic, so text named\n`.apk` or `.asar` stayed a container, and encrypted entries and symlinks\nkept the suffix guess. A filesystem `.asar` without an ASAR header failed\nthe whole inventory as a malformed archive.\n\nNested ZIP families now follow ZIP magic and ASAR follows its header\npickle, shared with root classification. An unread member named like a\ncontainer has an unknown format and a limitation naming the suffix. ASAR\nexpansion requires the header.\n\nThe Android projection adds a limitation when no root AndroidManifest.xml\nwas observed, and its rejection names the observed root format.\n\nFixes #1491\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
