      "sha": "0e19db9fce74af2081144102f5787cf90a450244",
      "subject": "fix(javascript): unify package resolution and resolve exact exports subpaths (#1424)",
      "body": "fix(javascript): unify package resolution and resolve exact exports subpaths (#1424)\n\n* fix(javascript): resolve exact package export subpaths\n\nBare module specifiers with subpaths now resolve against the selected\npackage's exports map instead of staying external. An exact subpath key\nselects its target through the existing condition, array, and null\nsemantics, and the selected target resolves as one exact file with no\nextension or index fallback. A declared exports map encapsulates every\nother subpath lookup, and packages without an exports map keep legacy\nfile and directory-index resolution.\n\nPackage-private import aliases remain external pending a separate\nincrement (#1365).\n\nVerification: npm run check:fast; focused and full\nsrc/application/javascript source tests on Windows;\nverify:test-discovery; docs:check. Four pre-existing failures in\nJavaScriptFileUrlPaths and JavaScriptModuleSpecifierPaths reproduce on\nunmodified main on Windows because their fixtures write file names\ncontaining '?'.\n\n* fix(javascript): unify package path resolution\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: morluto <76467478+morluto@users.noreply.github.com>",
