      "sha": "de619bd33450a9869395eaeb25fe5c4d6e034e36",
      "subject": "fix(ida): canonicalize the headless workspace root before opening (#1481)",
      "body": "fix(ida): canonicalize the headless workspace root before opening (#1481)\n\nOn macOS the default workspace root is os.tmpdir() under /var/folders,\nand /var is a symlink to /private/var. idalib-mcp reports the canonical\ninput path from idb_open/idb_list, while REA compared it against the\nuncanonicalized private copy with normalize(), so every headless IDA\nanalysis failed its identity check (surfacing as unreadable_output) and\nthe spawned idalib worker was never released.\n\nResolve the workspace root with realpath() when allocating the private\nworkspace so the input path REA sends already matches what upstream\nreports.\n\nCo-authored-by: Xingchuan Ma <xingchuan.ma@msn.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
