    {
      "sha": "649661dc8baa6976bbd8385c65ef0f21aa5745de",
      "subject": "fix(javascript): stop reading media preload attributes as Electron preloads",
      "body": "fix(javascript): stop reading media preload attributes as Electron preloads\n\nHTML audio and video elements have their own `preload` attribute (\"none\",\n\"metadata\", \"auto\"). A React renderer compiles `<audio preload=\"metadata\">`\nto `jsx(\"audio\", { preload: \"metadata\" })`, and the `property:preload`\nheuristic reported it as an Electron preload script named `metadata`.\n\nSkip `preload` properties in the props object of a call whose first\nargument is the static tag `audio` or `video`. The callee is not checked,\nbecause minified element factories have arbitrary names.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01XPY2GmufMNGQKoEgRUx1pd\n",
