    {
      "sha": "c19e15a2b3f09b3f693d7eab5263d83f4d2d1cd4",
      "subject": "feat(javascript): return a retained summary view on request (#1568)",
      "body": "feat(javascript): return a retained summary view on request (#1568)\n\nanalyze_javascript_application returns the complete application graph\ninline, which repeats tens of kilobytes even for a few source lines and\nexceeds the default 10 MiB MCP frame for a 300-function source file.\n\nThe new optional detail input keeps complete delivery by default. With\ndetail \"summary\" the server records the complete analysis Evidence in\nthe session and returns its inspect_analysis_view summary, whose\nparent_evidence_id lets callers page modules, select items, or pass the\nretained reference to application workflows. A server without Evidence\nretention refuses summary detail with capability_unavailable rather\nthan returning a summary whose analysis cannot be reached.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
