    {
      "sha": "fef6f730643dd60a80a109fc9751e1782b79ab4a",
      "subject": "feat(adb): complete ADB device support for Android reverse engineering (#1552)",
      "body": "feat(adb): complete ADB device support for Android reverse engineering (#1552)\n\n* feat(adb): acquire installed APK sets from connected Android devices\n\nAdd a read-only ADB device-acquisition family over the caller's adb binary:\ninspect_adb_client, list_adb_devices, inspect_adb_device, list_adb_packages,\nand pull_adb_package, exposed through the CLI and MCP with shared admission,\nEvidence provenance (binary, version, serial, transport), and fixed argv\nvectors that never reach a shell.\n\npull_adb_package acquires the complete split set reported by pm path into a\npackage-named directory that must not exist, digesting every file with\nSHA-256 and keeping per-file failure reasons and partial coverage. Device\nkind is reported as an inference with its basis; getprop whitelisting keeps\nbuild identity bounded. REA installs nothing and never manages devices or\nemulators; the first device query may start the caller's local adb server,\nrecorded when observed.\n\nVerified against adb 34.0.5 on Linux with an Android 14 (API 34) x86_64\nemulator: full 224-package inventory, a real two-APK split set pulled with\nbyte-exact digests, and a 73.9 MB system-package pull. npm run verify:adb\nrecords the lane; parser goldens come from the same device. READMEs carry\nthe new row in every supported language.\n\n* feat(adb): complete the adb surface with observation, transfer, and lifecycle tools\n\nExtend the ADB family from five to twenty-four operations, all through\nfixed adb argument vectors with no shell exposure:\n\nObservation: read_adb_logcat (bounded dump, count/buffer/pid), inspect_adb_package\n(dumpsys package projection), list_adb_processes (ps -A), list_adb_directory\n(ls -la with kinds and symlink targets), list_adb_features (hex GL versions),\nlist_adb_services (AIDL slash-suffixed names), inspect_adb_display (wm size and\ndensity), inspect_adb_window (focus declarations), read_adb_setting (device-side\nnulls reported as such), capture_adb_screen (exec-out screencap with PNG\ndimensions), collect_adb_bugreport (digested device archive).\n\nTransfer and search: pull_adb_file and push_adb_file (device-side sha256sum\nverification, explicit overwrite authority), resolve_adb_packages (substring\npackage search with exact-match flag — the find step of an easy get).\n\nLifecycle for dynamic analysis, each declaring mutatesTarget:\ninstall_adb_package and uninstall_adb_package preserving the device's\nSuccess/Failure verdict, start_adb_app (resolve-activity then am start -W),\nstart_adb_activity (typed extras as --es/--ez/--ei/--el/--ef), and stop_adb_app\n(am force-stop).\n\nVerified end-to-end against adb 34.0.5 on Linux with an Android 14 (API 34)\nx86_64 emulator: 287 services, 92 features, split-set pulls with byte-exact\ndigests, verified push/pull roundtrip, sized screen capture, and the full\ninstall → resolve → start → observe-in-ps → force-stop → uninstall lifecycle.\nFixed a v-mode regex incompatibility in the settings key pattern and added\nargument descriptions required by the CLI catalog audit.\n\n* fix(adb): quote remote shell operands and protect captured output\n\n* test(adb): cover bugreport destinations containing spaces\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: REA Contributor <contributor@rea.tools>\nCo-authored-by: morluto <76467478+morluto@users.noreply.github.com>",
