      "sha": "162f9bf7ffd559e871c83778c7a247b7afd4e5df",
      "subject": "fix(ghidra): clear wrong no-return flags before serving a session (#1419)",
      "body": "fix(ghidra): clear wrong no-return flags before serving a session (#1419)\n\n* fix(ghidra): clear wrong no-return flags before serving a session\n\nAuto-analysis can flag ordinary functions as no-return (stream readers,\n__cxa_guard_acquire, ...). Their callers then end at the call and the\ndecompiler truncates them. Run a postScript before the bridge that clears the\nflag on functions containing a real RET and re-disassembles the call sites that\nwere terminators.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(ghidra): refit in place and scope no-return call-site repair\n\nKeep function types by refitting the owning functions with fixupFunctionBody\ninstead of removing and recreating them. Only redo call sites whose callee was\nactually cleared (including thunks to it), skip sites followed by a function\nstart or x86 padding so real end calls do not run on, and always log the result.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(ghidra): constrain no-return repair to admitted return evidence\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: morluto <76467478+morluto@users.noreply.github.com>",
