      "sha": "4d8d76b2534275c6df1d62c9437d52f52a1d9d96",
      "subject": "fix(electron): support packaged app.asar pages and rewritten unpacked companions (#1400)",
      "body": "fix(electron): support packaged app.asar pages and rewritten unpacked companions (#1400)\n\n* fix(electron): resolve pages served from inside app.asar\n\nPackaged Electron applications load their renderer pages from file URLs\ninside app.asar. The host filesystem cannot stat those paths, so\nlist_electron_targets excluded every such page as unsupported_url and\ninspect_electron_page could not select it.\n\nResolve these URLs the way Electron's file protocol does: the first .asar\npath component that is a regular file is the archive, and the remainder\nmust name a regular file in its header. Directories, links, and missing\nmembers stay rejected. Parsed headers are cached by archive identity.\n\n* fix(artifacts): extract and explain rewritten ASAR unpacked companions\n\nPackaging tools commonly sign or strip .asar.unpacked native binaries after\nwriting the archive header, so their declared hashes no longer match.\nanalyze_javascript_application already accepts integrity_policy, but\nextract_artifact did not, and inspect_artifact and extract_artifact still\ntold callers to \"get a fresh copy\", which cannot help for a shipped app.\n\n- Accept integrity_policy on extract_artifact (MCP and CLI). The default\n  still fails closed; record-and-continue writes the observed bytes and\n  returns the extracted files' integrity_contradictions records.\n- Name the unpacked entry and the post-packaging cause in integrity\n  failures, and point every operation that accepts integrity_policy at\n  record-and-continue.\n- Report an active unpacked entry whose companion file is absent as\n  unavailable with its logical path instead of a format failure.\n- Share one integrity_policy schema across the inventory, extraction, and\n  JavaScript application inputs.\n\n* fix(electron): bound ASAR headers before allocation\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: morluto <76467478+morluto@users.noreply.github.com>",
