      "sha": "f6009d007713ef335189934d0c6d52a56818c525",
      "subject": "fix(browser): keep the first DOM attribute when the name is repeated (#1516)",
      "body": "fix(browser): keep the first DOM attribute when the name is repeated (#1516)\n\n* fix(browser): keep the first DOM attribute when the name is repeated\n\nWhen an element in a captured DOM tree carries duplicate attribute\ndeclarations (e.g. repeated href, action, or src), domMetadata folded\nthe attributes into a Map using pairs.set(), overwriting earlier\ndeclarations with the last one.\n\nHTML specifies that the first declaration is kept when an attribute\nname is repeated. This aligns domMetadata and attribute_names to retain\nthe first occurrence case-insensitively, matching HTML and ensuring that\nattribute_names and dom_urls reflect the same attributes.\n\nFixes #1496\n\n* fix(browser): preserve case-sensitive DOM attribute names\n\n* test(browser): align repeated attribute coverage with deduplication\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: taljeri <318237806+taljeri@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: morluto <76467478+morluto@users.noreply.github.com>",
