    {
      "sha": "ded59689cebad45d2d7af7685266b9e9a1985593",
      "subject": "fix(javascript): accept the Wakaru 1.x release line and verify 1.14.0 (#1540)",
      "body": "fix(javascript): accept the Wakaru 1.x release line and verify 1.14.0 (#1540)\n\n* fix(javascript): accept the Wakaru 1.x release line and verify 1.14.0\n\nExact --version equality rejected every Wakaru build except 1.13.0, and\nstrict report schemas rejected any added field, so each upstream release\nbroke recovery until REA re-pinned. Wakaru now documents that --version,\n--json and provenance.json change only by addition within a major version.\n\nAdmit ^1.13.0 with the verified/compatible split used for Binwalk and\nUnblob, report the observed version instead of the pinned constant, and\nadd a limitation for unverified releases. Parse reports with loose\nobjects and keep the reported module status as a string; path, identity,\nrange and file-set checks stay exact.\n\nMove the audited pin, submodule, CI binary and verifier to 1.14.0, and\ndocument where to get the binary from the refusal message.\n\n* fix(javascript): project known Wakaru warning fields\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: morluto <76467478+morluto@users.noreply.github.com>",
