    {
      "sha": "749e58772a0b1dd72fbfc938a5135ba2a1c11538",
      "subject": "feat(jeb): add JEB engine provider over its MCP interface (#1536)",
      "body": "feat(jeb): add JEB engine provider over its MCP interface (#1536)\n\n* feat(jeb): add JEB engine provider over its MCP interface\n\nAdd a bring-your-own JEB provider that serves project, unit, and\ndecompilation inspection from a caller-started JEB client speaking MCP\n(streamable HTTP, selected with REA_JEB_MCP_URL). Expose four provider-neutral\noperations through shared CLI/MCP workflows: inspect_jeb_client,\nopen_jeb_project, list_jeb_units, and decompile_jeb_item, each returning\nEvidence with engine identity, endpoint, and preserved refusal reasons.\n\nThe adapter keeps JEB's envelope semantics: success fields are parsed\nformat-aware at the boundary, message-only refusals become unsupported-target\nerrors with the engine's own reason, transport failures become availability\nfailures with recovery guidance, and unit pagination derives coverage from the\nengine's 100-item page cap. Explicit unknowns (implicitly selected unit,\nomitted filters) are reported instead of guessed.\n\nVerified against a real JEB 5.48.0 licensed build serving jeb-mcp-server 1.3.0\nheadless: client inspection, unit listing, and method decompilation were\nexercised through the CLI, MCP boundary, and scripts/verify-jeb.mjs.\nJEB 5.48.0 headless instances do not advertise open_project; the refusal is\npreserved and documented.\n\n* fix(jeb): verify against a real signed APK and fix CLI option surface\n\nVerify the provider against a locally built, v1/v2/v3-signed probe APK\n(binary manifest, classes.dex with a launcher activity) on JEB 5.48.0: the\nfull unit tree (apk, manifest, three certificate units, dex bytecode,\ndecompiler), wildcard-filtered and paginated unit listing with derived\ncoverage, parent-restricted listing, and launcher-activity method\ndecompilation through both CLI and MCP, including dexdec's inline\nconstant folding of the probe's obfuscated tag.\n\nMove list-jeb-units filter/pagination and decompile-jeb-item unit selection\nfrom positional arguments to options; the MCP schemas are unchanged.\n\n* fix(jeb): preserve engine refusals through the real MCP boundary\n\nTesting against the published Signal 8.30.3 universal APK exposed a boundary\nbug the scripted provider tests missed: decodeJebToolResult raised a protocol\nerror for isError results before the provider could map JEB's\n{success:false, message} envelope, so real engine refusals surfaced as\nunreadable output instead of the engine's own reason. Decode refusal\nenvelopes like any structured result and let the provider preserve the\nreason; cover the decoder directly, including contentless and unparseable\nresults.\n\nSignal verification: full 109 MB R8/Kotlin/Compose APK with four signature\nschemes and native arm64 ELF units parsed; MainActivity.onCreate and R8\nsynthetic lambdas decompiled through CLI and MCP; paginated, filtered, and\nparent-restricted unit listing; refusal path confirmed on the live engine.\n\n* docs(jeb): record Flutter Gallery verification on the real-engine lane\n\nVerify the provider against the official Flutter Gallery 2.9.2 release APK\n(112 MB): per-ABI libapp.so Dart AOT snapshot images analyzed as native code\nwith 75k methods on arm64, snapshot internals and wrapper methods decompiled\nthrough both CLI and MCP with explicit unit selection, decoded manifest, and\nfiltered native-library unit discovery. Note that JEB 5.48.0 headless does\nnot expose the dedicated Dart snapshot processor or run_script; both remain\nGUI-only engine surfaces.\n\n* docs(jeb): translate the README JEB row for every supported language\n\nThe JEB row was inserted in English across all translated READMEs; each now\ncarries its own label, capability summary, requirements, and guide link\nfollowing that language's Android-row conventions.\n\n* fix(jeb): enforce local endpoints and preserve cancellation\n\n* fix(jeb): refuse redirects across the local MCP boundary\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: REA Contributor <contributor@rea.tools>\nCo-authored-by: morluto <76467478+morluto@users.noreply.github.com>",
