    {
      "sha": "96fd98cce06e1f93b027487d38048e56c05181bd",
      "subject": "feat(apktool): decode Android resource tables through a caller-supplied launcher (#1556)",
      "body": "feat(apktool): decode Android resource tables through a caller-supplied launcher (#1556)\n\n* feat(apktool): decode Android resource tables through a caller-supplied launcher\n\nAdd an Apktool family with two operations over the caller's apktool\nlauncher (REA_APKTOOL_COMMAND, absolute, or apktool on PATH):\n\n- inspect_apktool_client: resolved launcher, selection source, and\n  version; decodes nothing.\n- decode_android_resources: apktool d --no-src in a provider-owned\n  workspace that is removed before the result returns. Projects the\n  decoded AndroidManifest.xml (bounded at 512 KiB), apktool.yml version\n  and SDK facts exactly as printed, string resources verbatim (default or\n  one locale, bounded at 2000 entries, nested-markup entries counted as\n  unparsed), available string locales, and the decoded file count with a\n  hard cap. The target APK is digested with SHA-256 before decoding so\n  Evidence binds the observation to the exact input.\n\nSmali production is skipped by design: Java-source recovery belongs to\nthe JADX family. Workspace cleanup happens before results return; an\nunremovable workspace is named in the limitations instead of abandoned.\n\nVerified against apktool 2.7.0-dirty (Debian packaging) on Linux with\nOpenJDK 25 against a signed aapt2-built probe APK with two resource\nlocales: launcher version, on-disk digest agreement, metadata projection,\nmanifest package agreement, and both string tables (default and de).\nParser goldens come from the same decode. READMEs carry the new\n'Android resources' row in every supported language.\n\n* fix(apktool): own snapshots and bound decoded resource reads\n\n* docs(apktool): describe owned resources and bounded projection\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: REA Contributor <contributor@rea.tools>\nCo-authored-by: morluto <76467478+morluto@users.noreply.github.com>",
