    {
      "sha": "bddddccdee3129d0b1b11e32b751be2b6d501c23",
      "subject": "feat(native): admit bounded MIPS ELF analysis through Ghidra (#1362)",
      "body": "feat(native): admit bounded MIPS ELF analysis through Ghidra (#1362)\n\n* feat(native): admit bounded MIPS ELF analysis through Ghidra\n\nRetain MIPS ELF identity and interpretation through Evidence and snapshots.\nKeep provider admission bounded to ELF32 ET_EXEC o32 MIPS32r2, without\nimplicitly widening Hopper, IDA or Windows P0 coverage. Add source-owned\nfixtures and an optional real-provider verifier; real Ghidra verification\nremains pending in this contribution environment.\n\nRefs #718\n\n* fix(ghidra): bound MIPS floating-point mode admission\n\nReject explicit EF_MIPS_FP64 and EF_MIPS_NAN2008 declarations until their\nsemantics have a real-provider verification lane. Add PSP PRX/Allegrex,\no64/EABI and floating-point-mode refusal regressions. Document that the\nheader gate is not a full .MIPS.abiflags check and advance the profile lane\nidentity to invalidate older interpretation bindings.\n\nValidation: 24 standalone checks against the transpiled production profile\nmodule passed; the two new flag cases failed before this change. Clang 17\nand LLD compiled the source-owned fixture for both endian targets. The\ncomplete Vitest/typecheck suite and real Ghidra verification remain pending.\n\nRefs morluto/rea#718; PSP support remains follow-up morluto/rea#1330.\n\n* fix(native): validate MIPS ABI records before Ghidra admission\n\nRead bounded ELF32 PT_MIPS_ABIFLAGS and SHT_MIPS_ABIFLAGS records through\nthe already-open target handle. Preserve declared ABI fields, reject\nconflicting/duplicate/truncated records, and keep missing records unknown.\nWire inspection into target resolution before provider selection. Require\ncompatible declarations for the deliberately narrow Ghidra lane and bind\nall ABI fields into profile identity (v3) for snapshot invalidation.\n\nClang 17 produced eight source-owned fixtures spanning both byte orders\nand FPXX/FP32/FP64/soft-float modes with identical ELF header flags. The\nnew reader and policy distinguish them. 24 focused regression test bodies\npassed after TypeScript transpilation using node:test in place of Vitest;\nstrict isolated TypeScript checking of the reader and target/result types\npassed. These are limited checks, not full Vitest/project typechecking or\nreal-Ghidra verification, which remain pending.\n\nAdvances morluto/rea#718. PSP/Allegrex remains morluto/rea#1330 follow-up.\n\n* fix(native): repair MIPS integration boundaries and test resolver behavior\n\nKeep ELF targets out of Hopper Mach-O preparation and scope existing PE fixture types correctly. Move ABI tests into the filesystem boundary lane, use shared cleanup, add resolver regressions, apply the pinned formatter, and register the real MIPS verifier through the existing package-command pattern. Validated with repository-pinned Node/npm, check:ci, actual focused Vitest, discovery and docs:check. Real Ghidra conformance remains pending.\n\n* fix(test): honor caller-selected JDK in real MIPS verification\n\n* test(native): strengthen MIPS Ghidra conformance\n\nCross-check the source-owned fixture with bounded GNU readelf inspection, compare production ELF/ABI interpretation and independent symbol addresses, and verify effective Ghidra language/compiler identity through existing public operations. Add a source-owned fixed-encoding probe for immediate and conditional branch checks plus global/string byte assertions.\n\nAdd 16 assertion/producer-boundary regression cases without widening production admission, changing provider contracts, or introducing proprietary dependencies. Local focused suite: 99 passed, one existing root-permission test skipped. Typecheck, lint/module boundaries, formatting and 700-file discovery pass; full hosted checks and real Ghidra verification remain pending for this checkpoint.\n\n* fix(ghidra): preserve native-tool architecture checks after MIPS integration\n\nThe conflict-free upstream merge failed TypeScript compilation because includes on the union of MIPS-only and other architecture arrays requires never. Use equality-based membership without casts or changing accepted native hosts. Extend the existing native-decompiler rejection table with a MIPS executable at a Linux x64 tool path; retain upstream FAT and unknown-header behavior. Hosted verification follows this commit; no success is claimed yet.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>",
