      "sha": "c7345512eae285158ea035be619ef6c8deb09adf",
      "subject": "perf(native): index admitted value-trace nodes",
      "body": "perf(native): index admitted value-trace nodes\n\nReplace a graph-wide node scan for each parameter use with membership in the set of admitted node IDs. Preserve node-budget omission, pagination, and existing ID-collision behavior.\n\nFlameox profiles identify the eliminated scan. Six-run medians on a bounded synthetic four-procedure workload improved from 2538.17 ms to 220.32 ms (11.52x); full JSON responses have identical SHA-256 4071fc7ec17be01e6a23d53814a47b3b1bb0ebd80099d21ef8431da487801725. This measures production trace composition with a synthetic provider, not real Ghidra target speed.\n\nExternal design research through DeepWiki was checked against Ghidra 12.1.4 DataGraph: https://github.com/NationalSecurityAgency/ghidra/blob/8b6bbb857accdfa20dc5b2f5dea471178c2e9fbc/Ghidra/Features/CodeCompare/src/main/java/ghidra/features/codecompare/graphanalysis/DataGraph.java\n",
