      "sha": "926c2d6ba7975522d63a8dbb0d448f5b9d1514d4",
      "subject": "test(ghidra): preserve metadata in interior-label fixture",
      "body": "test(ghidra): preserve metadata in interior-label fixture\n\nPlace the imported control label inside a valid multi-byte NOP instead of suppressing Mach-O function-start metadata. Encode the supported ARM64 and x86-64 instructions explicitly and retain the load dependency so the control remains past the function entry. Assert that Ghidra imports a label and no procedure at the control address before checking name rejection and address containment.\n\nTwo real arm64 Ghidra 12.1.4 imports confirmed both fixture strategies produce labels; only default linking retains LC_FUNCTION_STARTS. The full native-value CLI/MCP verifier passed with 349 successful and 52 expected rejected boundary calls, including imported aliases, complete exports, and startup cancellation cleanup. Host ARM64 and Apple x86-64 fixture compilation passed; x86 provider execution remains unverified.\n",
