      "subject": "fix(browser): fold loopback spellings into one attach admission key (#1604)",
      "body": "fix(browser): fold loopback spellings into one attach admission key (#1604)\n\nA CDP endpoint serves every loopback stack on one port, but the attach\nadmission key was built from the endpoint origin string, so scenarios\nattaching through http://127.0.0.1:PORT and http://[::1]:PORT produced\ntwo lease keys, passed admission in parallel and the browser rejected\nthe second client. Collapse literal loopback hostnames to one identity\nin the lease key (port and target still partition it) without touching\nendpoint validation.\n\nValidation: npx vitest run src/browser/PlaywrightScenarioBrowser.test.ts (9 passed; the two new loopback tests failed before the fix), npx vitest run src/browser src/domain (1745 passed, 2 failed, both failing on pristine main), npm run test:fast (3896 passed, 12 failed, 7 skipped; the failure set is identical on pristine main at 3894 passed), plus typecheck, oxlint, oxfmt and resolved module-boundary verification.",
