      "sha": "3a7a3074e30d842bb0a0c7837a46d45d66565342",
      "subject": "feat(javascript): recognize tRPC procedures and GraphQL operations (#1670)",
      "body": "feat(javascript): recognize tRPC procedures and GraphQL operations (#1670)\n\n* feat(javascript): recognize tRPC procedures and GraphQL operations\n\nRecord RPC client syntax as network endpoint candidates in both\nanalyze_javascript_application and analyze_web_bundle, distinguished by\nmechanism:\n\n- trpc:procedure:<method> keeps the static member path of\n  root.<path>.<method>(...), which tRPC proxies preserve through\n  identifier minification. React hooks and TanStack option factories are\n  recognized directly. Vanilla query/mutate need a root bound to\n  createTRPCClient/createTRPCProxyClient, or a tRPC source marker with a\n  router path of at least two segments; subscribe needs the marker and a\n  tRPC observer argument. `this` roots, browser globals and RTK Query\n  `endpoints` chains are never procedures; cache-key helpers are excluded.\n- trpc:link:<link> records the literal url of documented HTTP links.\n- graphql:<type> records named operations from string and cooked template\n  literals with a valid operation header, and from precompiled\n  OperationDefinition objects; a graphql-tag loc.source.body copy is not\n  reported twice.\n\nMethod, callback and factory names follow @trpc/client and React/TanStack\nintegration sources and documentation for 11.19. Carrier segments before\nthe router path, useUtils helpers and minifier-renamed links remain\ndocumented limitations.\n\nValidation: typecheck; domain tests for recognition and false positives\n(Apollo, RxJS, stores, RTK Query, browser globals, prose); web bundle\nanalyzer test; end-to-end analysis of a minified fixture through the\nbuilt MCP server on Windows 11.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(javascript): preserve RPC binding identity and bundled calls\n\n* style(reference-source): fix CI formatting\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: morluto <76467478+morluto@users.noreply.github.com>",
