      "sha": "fe574c0c9f64d13de9223862a90921e5060abed5",
      "subject": "fix(javascript): recover Electron APIs through default imports and optional calls (#1673)",
      "body": "fix(javascript): recover Electron APIs through default imports and optional calls (#1673)\n\n`import electron from \"electron\"` bound the module with a leading `default`\nexport segment, so `electron.ipcMain.handle(...)`, `new\nelectron.BrowserWindow(...)` and destructuring from that binding matched no\nElectron API. Electron's CommonJS exports define no `default` member, so the\nsegment can only denote the module object; drop it when classifying\nElectron bindings.\n\nThe binding classifier already recorded optional-call roots, but the IPC,\ncontext-bridge, utility-process and sender-validation visitors accepted only\nplain calls. `ipcMain?.handle(...)`, `contextBridge?.exposeInMainWorld(...)`\nand the common `event.senderFrame?.url.startsWith(...)` check were dropped\nwithout a limitation.\n\nRefs #1656\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
