      "sha": "b212e92f9be972fae2093a323d76473918d09fcb",
      "subject": "ci: select semantic tests and fixture lanes for their guarded inputs (#1675)",
      "body": "ci: select semantic tests and fixture lanes for their guarded inputs (#1675)\n\nEdits to `release.yml` or `real-ghidra-windows.yml` selected only the\nworkflow lane, so the shards holding releaseWorkflow, releaseCheckpoint\nand realGhidraWindowsWorkflow tests were skipped. Actionlint checks\nsyntax only, so a PR could drop the package-before-publish gate, the\nregistry canary or the default-branch-only self-hosted runner restriction\nwithout CI noticing.\n\nConformance fixture sources under tests/ set only the code lane, so the\nconformance-fixtures and reconstruction-readiness jobs, the only callers\nof `verify:fixtures` and `verify:readiness`, never ran for them. Route\nthe directories that build-conformance-fixtures.mjs compiles to both\nlanes, and readiness applications to the readiness lane.\n\nBoth were raised by the Codex review of #1660 after it merged.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
