    {
      "sha": "76296c5a3868ba3b54be6ed3896719283d6de5f8",
      "subject": "fix(native): bind NativeAOT metadata to declared PE section extents",
      "body": "fix(native): bind NativeAOT metadata to declared PE section extents\n\nSection headers distinguish the declared virtual extent from the on-disk raw extent, which may include alignment padding. Resource RVA ownership and overlap use VirtualSize, falling back to SizeOfRawData when VirtualSize is zero, and payload reads still require file-backed bytes.\n\nThe NativeAOT snapshot reader applies the same range rule to RVA reads, metadata scans, executable targets, and derived overlay bounds. Page-rounded loader mappings may expose tail bytes, but those bytes lie outside the declared section range used by these parsers.\n",
