  "commits": [
    {
      "sha": "0ecf3f2438ec96a6b543942869808018e8d84452",
      "subject": "perf(mcp): keep Playwright and type-only imports off MCP startup (#1691)",
      "body": "perf(mcp): keep Playwright and type-only imports off MCP startup (#1691)\n\n* fix(build): emit no runtime imports for type-only bindings\n\nUnder verbatimModuleSyntax, an import whose specifiers all carry inline\n`type` modifiers compiles to `import {} from \"...\"`, a side-effect import\nthat still resolves and evaluates the module. 78 compiled modules carried\none, including `import {} from \"playwright-core\"` in the browser scenario\nsession, which loaded Playwright's module graph at MCP startup.\n\nUse top-level `import type` for these bindings and enable oxlint's\ntypescript/no-import-type-side-effects rule so the pattern cannot return.\n\nRefs #1685\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* perf(mcp): load Playwright when a scenario launches, not at startup\n\nThe browser scenario and Electron active providers are constructed before\nthe stdio server serves, and both bound Playwright's launchers at module\nload. Resolve `chromium` and `_electron` from playwright-core when a\ncapture opens instead, as the web module resolver already does.\n\nMCP startup now resolves 1,312 modules (4,902 resolutions) instead of\n1,598 (6,076) before reading the first request, and no longer loads\nplaywright-core. Provider construction, the tool catalog, and capability\ninventory are unchanged.\n\nA boundary test spawns the stdio server, initializes, lists tools, and\nasserts playwright-core and isomorphic-git were not resolved; the CLI\nprobe now exercises the real launch path to prove detection.\n\nCloses #1685\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
