      "sha": "ae95e68ba5fa95cf2ec0453b50ffd217cabf5359",
      "subject": "fix(apktool): run Windows batch launchers through cmd.exe (#1777)",
      "body": "fix(apktool): run Windows batch launchers through cmd.exe (#1777)\n\nOn Windows, Node refuses to spawn .bat and .cmd files without a shell\n(CVE-2024-27980), so REA_APKTOOL_COMMAND pointing at Chocolatey's\napktool.bat or a java -jar wrapper failed its version probe with EINVAL,\nreported as \"did not report a usable version\".\n\nMove Ghidra's conservative cmd.exe invocation (no AutoRun, no delayed\nexpansion, every token quoted, interpreter metacharacters rejected) into\nsrc/process/WindowsBatchCommand.ts. Ghidra keeps its error type, wording\nand length limit. apktool now uses it for both the version probe and the\ndecode run when the launcher is a batch file on Windows. A launcher that\ncmd.exe would reinterpret reports launcher_unsupported (not_configured)\nwith remediation instead of version_unresolved.\n\nFixes #1774\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
