      "sha": "e4027e4afccc6316cd9cfc27c7b0427e66ceb91f",
      "subject": "feat(update): update Bun global installations (#1735)",
      "body": "feat(update): update Bun global installations (#1735)\n\n* feat(update): update Bun global installations\n\n`rea update` only recognized npm global installations and looked up\nreleases with `npm view`, so a `bun add --global rea-agents` install on a\nmachine without npm failed with `spawn npm ENOENT`.\n\nDetect the running package inside Bun's global directory\n(BUN_INSTALL_GLOBAL_DIR, $BUN_INSTALL/install/global,\n$XDG_CACHE_HOME/.bun/install/global, ~/.bun/install/global), resolve the\nlatest release with `bun info`, install with\n`bun add --global --ignore-scripts`, then verify the installed entry point\nand plan integration maintenance exactly as for npm.\n\nBun commands run inside the owning global directory with\nBUN_INSTALL_GLOBAL_DIR pinned, so the caller's current project is never\nselected. A global directory without package.json is not treated as an\nowned installation: Bun then installs into the nearest ancestor project.\nnpm installations keep their existing commands and messages.\n\n* fix(update): gate Bun self-updates on supported CLI versions\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: morluto <76467478+morluto@users.noreply.github.com>",
