    {
      "sha": "12c416005f9d2abf438f4df4447972424d781b65",
      "subject": "feat(javascript): recover code-split bundles from multiple inputs (#1686)",
      "body": "feat(javascript): recover code-split bundles from multiple inputs (#1686)\n\n* feat(javascript): recover code-split bundles from multiple inputs\n\nrecover_javascript_sources accepted a single path, and\nvalidateModuleSet bound every module's provenance to that one snapshot.\nA code-split app (runtime + chunks, or an Electron main/preload/renderer\nset) had to be recovered one file per call, and modules recovered alone\ncould not resolve imports across chunks: cross-chunk require(id)\nreferences stayed as numeric ids with property reads.\n\nAdd an optional additional_paths input. The listed files are\nconcatenated, in order after path, into the single engine snapshot, so\none Wakaru run sees every module and cross-chunk imports resolve.\nvalidateModuleSet's single-snapshot binding is unchanged. Module\nprovenance is attributed back to the input file its first extraction\nrange starts in, with byte ranges rebased to that file's own offsets;\na module whose ranges cross an input boundary keeps the concatenated\nsnapshot identity and offsets, recorded as an explicit limitation.\nSingle-path behavior is byte-for-byte unchanged (one segment,\noffset 0).\n\nFixes #1605\n\n* fix(javascript): preserve source identity in multi-input recovery\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: JingHao-Leon <w15909130000@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: morluto <76467478+morluto@users.noreply.github.com>",
