      "body": "fix(native): raise default PE resource entry budget to 16384 (#1703)\n\ninspect-pe-resources rejected stock Windows resource images because their\ntables exceed the 4096-entry default. Windows 11 25H2 SystemResources\nmeasures imageres.dll.mun at 6476 examined entries, shell32.dll.mun at 5903\nand wmploc.DLL.mun at 5440, so the default budget now admits each of them\nwith headroom while the maximum stays 65536. The independent 8 MiB metadata\nbudget still bounds allocation, and exceeding any budget still fails without\npartial results.\n\nThe stable filesystem boundary test now emits a 6476-entry table through a\nlarger fixture section and asserts that the default budgets report complete\ncoverage, covering stock-image scale without a real Windows file.",
