      "sha": "f2150eb9a7ed76748238009ca6666efa52de5271",
      "subject": "feat(harmony): project HarmonyOS package inventory evidence (#1447)",
      "body": "feat(harmony): project HarmonyOS package inventory evidence (#1447)\n\n* feat(harmony): project HarmonyOS package inventory evidence\n\nFirst HarmonyOS increment from #1431: HAP, HSP, and App Pack roots are\nclassified through the hardened ZIP reader and projected into an\nexecution-free application graph with packaging-model hints, exact\ncomponent paths and hashes, App Pack children by path, runtime-family\nhints, and path-based N-API bridge hypotheses. HarmonyOS .har stays\nunclassified by suffix because .har also names HTTP Archive JSON.\n\nAdds the project_harmony_application_graph tool (CLI and MCP), synthetic\ncomposition coverage, a pinned real-package verify lane, and docs.\n\n* refactor(domain): share application graph projection scaffolding\n\nThe HarmonyOS projection mirrors the Android and Apple projections by\ndesign, which pushed jscpd duplication over its 2.5 percent budget.\nExtract the identical pieces (inventory input schema, projected\ncomponent schema and occurrence flattening, bridge candidate schema\nfactory, coverage assembly, comparator, canonical digest) into\ndomain/mobileApplicationGraphProjection.ts and route all three\nprojections plus the composition fixtures through it. Duplication drops\nfrom 2.52 to 2.49 percent with no behavior change: projection ids,\nclassifications, and limitations are byte-identical.\n\n* fix(harmony): address review, stable app-pack roots, and rotated fixture\n\n- rebased onto main; the shared projection scaffolding now keeps main's\n  nativeRuntimeConvention loop and the harmony runtime families adopt the\n  same react-native/flutter/unity path conventions\n- the .app App Pack suffix is now a root-input rule only (verified ZIP\n  magic in classifyRootFormat and BinaryTargetResolver); nested .app ZIP\n  members inside other packages keep the generic zip classification, with\n  a regression test, so existing inventories do not change\n- the signing limitation now states that an empty signing list does not\n  mean unsigned because packaging-tool signatures live in the ZIP signing\n  block, and the app-pack root rule is disclosed as suffix-based\n- repinned the real-package fixture to the current VHome 2.6.14-beta asset\n  after the upstream deleted v5.0.111-beta and replaced the v2.6.14-beta\n  asset within hours; the pin records both observed digests\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: morluto <76467478+morluto@users.noreply.github.com>",
