    {
      "sha": "30787297d49bf93e67f62a9ec42f896188d57a20",
      "subject": "fix(managed): charge retained member facts instead of decoding bounds (#1768)",
      "body": "fix(managed): charge retained member facts instead of decoding bounds (#1768)\n\n* fix(managed): charge retained member facts instead of decoding bounds\n\ninspect_managed_members returned no types or methods for ordinary\nassemblies: Newtonsoft.Json 13.0.3 (netstandard2.0, 705 KB) exceeded\nthe 64 MiB representation budget. Each method body reserved 256 bytes\nper IL byte and each signature 256 bytes per blob byte before decoding,\nand those worst-case bounds were never returned, so the budget scaled\nwith total IL size rather than with the retained output. The final\nprojection admission also charged every decoded string at six bytes per\ncharacter and every scalar at 32 bytes, about eight times its JSON size.\n\nBound IL, exception-clause and signature decoding with a transient\nadmission that does not consume capacity, then reserve the decoded body\nor signature that is actually retained. Projection admission now\ncharges the exact UTF-8 JSON bytes of decoded strings, keys and scalars;\nescaped and multibyte text still counts at its encoded size.\n\nNewtonsoft.Json now yields 496 types, 4185 methods and 18846 call\nedges. Assemblies whose retained facts exceed the budget, such as the\n2.3 MB System.Private.ServiceModel 4.7.0, remain unavailable.\n\n* fix(managed): bound concurrent decoding and count JSON bytes in place\n\nReview follow-up. A method's IL bound and its exception-section bounds\nwere each checked against the same remaining capacity although their\nbookkeeping is live at the same time, so 40 MiB of IL plus 40 MiB of\nexception clauses passed a 64 MiB budget. Transient admissions now\naccumulate until the method body or signature is built, and reserve\nrespects bounds that are still live.\n\nProjection admission also serialized each decoded string to measure it,\nwhich could allocate about six times a near-limit string before the\ncheck. It now counts the exact escaped UTF-8 bytes without building the\nJSON text.\n\n* fix(managed): admit derived call and field edges as they are built\n\nReview follow-up. Released IL bounds no longer stand in for the call and field-access records that edges() derives from anchors. Each record is now admitted before the graph grows further, so a crafted assembly cannot materialize the whole derived graph before the representation guard fails.\n\n* fix(managed): admit derived caller names before building them\n\nReview follow-up. The caller name of call and field-access records was interpolated per anchor before any admission saw it. It is now built once per method, after its exact JSON size, counted from the type and member names, has been admitted.",
      "parents": ["f2150eb9a7ed76748238009ca6666efa52de5271"],
      "authors": [
