      "sha": "91f843bf38b0e4ec8576f41f3140488b4ee8ff32",
      "subject": "fix(artifacts): mark Windows host executables by extension (#1823)",
      "body": "fix(artifacts): mark Windows host executables by extension (#1823)\n\nWindows has no POSIX execute bit; Node reports file modes from the\nread-only attribute alone, so every host file, including PE images,\nreported `executable: false` while the same occurrence reported\n`artifact_kind: executable`. Derive the host executable marking once:\nPOSIX permission bits stay authoritative, and Windows marks regular\nfiles with the CreateProcess/cmd launchable extensions.\n\nFixes #1819\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
