      "sha": "6ac5c36503492d3b6da4fcf2a5dee87aff60fc8c",
      "subject": "fix(javascript): follow bundler namespace interop for Electron APIs (#1827)",
      "body": "fix(javascript): follow bundler namespace interop for Electron APIs (#1827)\n\n* fix(javascript): follow bundler namespace interop for Electron APIs\n\nRolldown/tsdown emit `let electron = require(\"electron\"); electron =\n__toESM(electron);` and esbuild/tsc emit `__toESM(require(\"electron\"))`\nor `__importStar(require(\"electron\"))` for namespace imports. The\nreassignment or the helper call hid the Electron origin, so bundled\nmain processes reported zero BrowserWindows and preloads.\n\nLocally declared, never reassigned interop helpers recognized by name\nnow pass the module through, and a binding's rewrap of its own value is\nnot treated as a reassignment. Other writes stay unresolved.\n\nFixes #1802\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(javascript): require emitted interop helper definitions\n\nOnly trust an interop helper name when it has a single program-scope\nfunction definition, and state that helper bodies are not evaluated.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
