      "sha": "ed1519ddee02739f57136e356786f64c7f74fed0",
      "subject": "fix(managed): report ExportedType rows in managed member inspection (#1828)",
      "body": "fix(managed): report ExportedType rows in managed member inspection (#1828)\n\n* fix(managed): report ExportedType rows in managed member inspection\n\nFacade assemblies such as System.Runtime.dll provide their types only\nthrough ExportedType rows (type forwarders), which member inspection\nnever read, so they reported complete coverage with no types. Report\neach row as declared with its flags, forwarder bit, TypeDefId hint, and\nimplementation token, and record invalid or null implementation coded\nindexes as partial coverage. Comparisons now state that exported types\nare not compared when either side has them.\n\nFixes #1812\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(managed): read earlier member Evidence without exported types\n\nMember Evidence recorded before ExportedType rows were read omits the\nfield. Parse it as null (not examined) instead of rejecting it, and\nstate in comparisons that such an observation's exported types are\nunknown.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(managed): leave exported types unknown when metadata is unavailable\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
