      "sha": "1f531fc257f71731624cbd6b595208adacf59108",
      "subject": "fix(managed): decode generic, array, fnptr, and modifier signatures (#1835)",
      "body": "fix(managed): decode generic, array, fnptr, and modifier signatures (#1835)\n\n* fix(managed): decode generic, array, fnptr, and modifier signatures\n\nMember signatures using GENERICINST, ARRAY, FNPTR, CMOD_REQD/CMOD_OPT,\nor TYPEDBYREF were reported as unsupported, leaving their types unknown\nand turning otherwise complete inspections partial. Decode them with an\nexplicit stack so nested signatures stay recursion-free, keep encoded\nTypeDefOrRefOrSpec values, and report malformed shapes as malformed.\n\nFixes #1832\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(managed): bound array rank before rendering dimensions\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(managed): keep modifier order and reject non-method fnptr headers\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(managed): reject corrupt fnptr flags and misplaced typed references\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(managed): decode signature elements by grammar position\n\nTrack whether each element is a field type, return type, parameter,\nnested Type, or pointee. VOID is valid only as a return type or\npointee, TYPEDBYREF only as a return type or parameter, and BYREF only\nat the top of a return type, parameter, or ref field; other placements\nare malformed. Function pointer items are parsed as a return type then\nparameters, and generic arguments as Types.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
