      "body": "fix(errors): stop recommending retries for non-retryable failures (#1869)\n\n* fix(errors): stop recommending retries for non-retryable failures\n\nUnreadable output and provider adapter failures project retryable=false,\nbut their standard message and remediation said \"Retry once\", so a\nfirmware run whose expected report was never published told callers to\nrepeat a non-retryable operation. Point those failures at `rea doctor`\nand the reported details instead, leaving retryability decided once by\nthe projected error code.\n\nFixes #1855\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(errors): align Hopper remote failure guidance with retryability\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
