      "sha": "499ac180115de7c9de3f1adc55159ffa6e9bb40e",
      "subject": "fix(web): reject NUL bytes in web tool local path inputs",
      "body": "fix(web): reject NUL bytes in web tool local path inputs\n\nFour web tools accepted caller-selected local paths as plain strings, so\na NUL byte passed contract validation and reached filesystem calls. The\nservices only checked isAbsolute, and isAbsolute admits a NUL, so the\nfailure surfaced later as a raw ERR_INVALID_ARG_VALUE instead of a named\ninput constraint. Every other local-input tool already refuses NUL through\nthe shared local-path schema, and the existing OS-invalid-local-input\nharness covers those but not these web tools.\n\ninspect_web_network_capture.capture_path, export_web_scripts.capture_path\nand output_directory, trace_web_source_location.manifest_path and\nsource_map.path, and trace_web_module_imports.manifest_path and\nimport_map.path now use localPathStringSchema. Each field already required\na nonempty string, so the advertised pattern and minLength stay the same\nand only the NUL refusal is added.\n\nValidation: a new schema test rejects NUL in all seven fields while\naccepting ordinary absolute paths; the four tools are added to the\nOS-invalid-local-input harness and reject NUL through the real advertised\nMCP contracts; typecheck, oxlint, oxfmt, and toolSchemaValidity with a\nregenerated catalog. Two webScriptExport boundary cases fail identically\nwith and without this change on this Windows host (symlink EPERM and\nprivate-runtime-root authority), so they are environmental.\n",
