      "sha": "176941700118cc33c86e07373cd6950f30548386",
      "subject": "fix(firmware): name missing extractor dependencies in partial extraction (#1879)",
      "body": "fix(firmware): name missing extractor dependencies in partial extraction (#1879)\n\nUnblob reports a missing external extractor as an\nExtractorDependencyNotFoundReport nested inside a chunk or multi-file\nreport, and normalizeUnblobReport forwarded that value verbatim into\ndiagnostics as { input_path, report }. A caller that reached partial\ncoverage therefore had to decode the raw producer report to learn which\nextractor was absent and at which stage, even though the report already\nnames the dependencies.\n\nExtraction diagnostics now normalize those entries: the named\ndependencies are collected from the report and any nested value, the\nproducing handler is recorded as the stage, and the original report stays\nretained for provenance. Entries without a dependency report keep their\nprevious shape.\n\nValidation: FirmwareReports unit cases cover the chunk-nested and\nmulti-file-nested dependency reports and the retained raw report;\nfirmware suite passes; typecheck, oxlint and oxfmt on changed files. Real\nUnblob extraction is unverified here because it needs the external\nextractor stack.",
