    {
      "sha": "9b3e59804db71072ed023f109342f96063c57b45",
      "subject": "fix(javascript): prove namespace interop before attributing Electron APIs (#1857)",
      "body": "fix(javascript): prove namespace interop before attributing Electron APIs (#1857)\n\n* fix(javascript): prove Electron module namespace conversion\n\n* refactor(javascript): share AST child field metadata\n\nCo-authored-by: factory-droid[bot] <138933559+factory-droid[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Kaoru0822 <208281322+kaoru0822-kitauji@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix(javascript): retain destructured intrinsic writes\n\nShare one pattern-target walker across lexical definitions, member mutation\ntracking and Electron identity writes. Keep overwritten globals unresolved\nwithout treating property keys or shadowed locals as global replacements.\n\nCo-authored-by: factory-droid[bot] <138933559+factory-droid[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Kaoru0822 <208281322+kaoru0822-kitauji@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix(javascript): preserve intrinsic projections and fresh target identity\n\nResolve known mutators through static binding projections and prove stable\nidentifier chains to fresh literals before widening unknown mutation targets.\nKeep reassigned, uninitialized and member-projected targets conservative.\nCover both review regressions through source tests and inert CLI/MCP fixtures.\n\nCo-authored-by: factory-droid[bot] <138933559+factory-droid[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Kaoru0822 <208281322+kaoru0822-kitauji@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix(javascript): retain fresh function and class target identity\n\nRecognize stable local function, undecorated class and RegExp targets before\nwidening intrinsic mutations. Keep decorated classes opaque because their\nbinding value can be replaced, and preserve class-initialization writes.\nCover fresh targets and replacement decorators in inert CLI/MCP fixtures.\n\nCo-authored-by: factory-droid[bot] <138933559+factory-droid[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Kaoru0822 <208281322+kaoru0822-kitauji@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix(javascript): preserve intrinsic alias capture timing\n\nValidate each alias read after initialization and retain the original function capture across copies. Share declaration initializer facts with RPC and Electron analysis, including class declarations used for fresh-target identity. Accept single-statement control blocks while keeping lexical roles and added operations checked. Cover the capture regressions through inert source and public CLI/MCP workflows.\n\n* fix(javascript): respect hoisted fresh function declarations\n\nFunction declarations provide fresh targets before their textual position. Retain initialization-order checks for variable and class values, including aliases. Cover the reviewed regression with source controls and the public CLI/MCP fixture.\n\n* fix(javascript): preserve proven interop result projections\n\n* fix(javascript): retain stable declarations and bound intrinsic writes\n\nKeep repeated variable declarations with one unconditional initializer while\nrejecting assignments, conditional initialization and multiple values.\nNormalize known intrinsic calls, aliases and bound argument prefixes at the\nsemantic owner, retaining opaque targets without tainting unused bindings or\nfresh local objects. Cover both regressions through source and CLI/MCP tests.\n\nCo-authored-by: factory-droid[bot] <138933559+factory-droid[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Kaoru0822 <208281322+kaoru0822-kitauji@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix(javascript): retain bound intrinsic mutation effects\n\n* fix(javascript): preserve bound receivers for intrinsic invocation\n\n* fix(javascript): prove generic binding and invocation effects\n\n* fix(javascript): retain Reflect set receiver effects\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: factory-droid[bot] <138933559+factory-droid[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Kaoru0822 <208281322+kaoru0822-kitauji@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: morluto <76467478+morluto@users.noreply.github.com>",
