    {
      "sha": "0b7fc40eeef03b06de08d886572c2862331d8947",
      "subject": "fix(contracts): mark foreign execution and device mutation destructive (#1904)",
      "body": "fix(contracts): mark foreign execution and device mutation destructive (#1904)\n\nMCP annotations derived destructiveHint only from mayDiscardData, so tools\nthat run the analysis target or a caller-selected executable\n(capture_process_scenario, observe_native_calls) and tools that change an\nattached Android device (install/uninstall/push/start/stop) advertised\ndestructiveHint: false.\n\nAdd explicit executesForeignCode and mutatesDevice effect flags, audit them\nacross all 170 tool effect records, and derive\ndestructiveHint = mayDiscardData || executesForeignCode || mutatesDevice.\nreadOnlyHint semantics are unchanged.\n\nHopper/Ghidra metadata writers (set_address_name, set_addresses_names,\nset_bookmark, set_comment, set_inline_comment, annotate_native_function)\ncan replace or clear existing analyst names and comments, so they now\ndeclare mayDiscardData as well.\n\nA contract test pins the destructive set and requires every tool whose\ndescription mentions running, launching, executing, starting, installing or\nuninstalling to declare one of the new flags or carry a reasoned exception,\nso wording and effects cannot silently drift. The binary_session effects\noutput schema carries the new flags.",
