    {
      "sha": "e4ac7bbfc2f8c631ba1c60f507d85253e122d4c8",
      "subject": "fix: order remaining outputs independently of host locale (#1867)",
      "body": "fix: order remaining outputs independently of host locale (#1867)\n\n* fix: order remaining outputs independently of host locale\n\nString.prototype.localeCompare without a pinned collation follows the\nhost's ICU default locale, so the same input could be ordered differently\non different machines. 614fb768 moved canonical domain projections to\ncompareUnicodeCodePoints; provider, application, catalog, and setup\norderings still used locale collation.\n\nOrder every remaining source site by Unicode code point, including Mach-O\nsymbols, firmware extraction paths, ASAR entries (previously pinned to\n\"en\" collation), evidence ID sets, browser and Electron target, script,\nand resource inventories, reconstruction obligations, capability and\nprovider listings, and setup environment details.\n\nThe current tool and prompt catalog names order identically under both\ncomparators, so the catalog identity digest is unchanged.\n\n* fix(artifacts): order ASAR entries by their portable path\n\n@electron/asar lists host-spelled paths, so code-point order over the raw\nspelling still differed by host: \"a\\b\" sorts after \"a0\" on Windows while\n\"a/b\" sorts before it on POSIX. Pair each listing with its portable\narchive path once, order by that path, and keep the host spelling for\n@electron/asar calls and adapter keys.",
