    {
      "sha": "e8491e023a255f790ae9850225084d7495e9ade0",
      "subject": "fix(artifacts): mark Windows launchable files as host executables (#1824)",
      "body": "fix(artifacts): mark Windows launchable files as host executables (#1824)\n\nHost-file occurrences derived `executable` from POSIX execute bits, which\nWindows never reports, so every Windows host file (including PE .exe\nimages classified as executable) reported `executable: false`.\n\nDerive the fact once through hostExecutable: POSIX hosts keep the execute\nbits; Windows marks regular files with the extensions it launches directly\n(.exe, .com, .bat, .cmd), without reading the ambient PATHEXT.\n\nFixes #1819\n\nCo-authored-by: morluto <76467478+morluto@users.noreply.github.com>",
