      "body": "feat(javascript): resolve exact package import aliases (#1862)\n\n* feat(javascript): resolve exact package import aliases\n\nResolve exact #alias specifiers against the importer's enclosing\npackage.json imports map using the shared condition, array, and null\ntarget selection. Nested packages keep their own maps; missing keys,\nexplicit nulls, and out-of-scope aliases report a precise reason.\nWildcard, recursive, and external-package import targets remain\nunresolved.\n\n* fix(javascript): keep nested import aliases in CLI graphs\n\nBound nested #alias requires produce application-graph require edges\nfrom the enclosing package. Node reports MODULE_NOT_FOUND when a nested\npackage.json has no imports field, without inheriting the ancestor map.\n\n* fix(javascript): resolve literal package import keys before path admission\n\n* fix(javascript): preserve import keys and invalid-target fallback\n\n* fix(javascript): preserve unmatched package target arrays\n\n* fix(javascript): retain package target refusal evidence\n\n* test(browser): match real verifier startup budget\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: morluto <76467478+morluto@users.noreply.github.com>",
