    {
      "sha": "72489a9445299f695d793f004fed88e1bac0a557",
      "subject": "fix(javascript): report available parent result budget in coverage limits (#1915)",
      "body": "fix(javascript): report available parent result budget in coverage limits (#1915)\n\n* fix(javascript): size the future static reserve by remaining sources\n\nThe parent reserved 80% of its result budget for future static facts\nwhenever any source remained, so one tiny later file could discard an\nearlier file's completed semantic graph. Reserve at most one bounded\nstatic checkpoint's retained size per remaining source, within the same\nshared pool, so many remaining sources keep the previous protection.\nParent-budget rejections now report the effective admission budget and\nexplain that the CLI/MCP process heap, not max_heap_mb, bounds them.\n\nRefs #1911\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(javascript): make parent budget remediation and its test runtime-aware\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(javascript): suggest a concrete parent heap size in remediation\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(javascript): let parent budget rejections state their retained facts\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
      "parents": ["b6651cb99fba8fec3fd3efcb6794ae32b8a1525d"],
