      "sha": "c2cf7dcb86e11350214f82e5c51de7ca6ee3d27a",
      "subject": "fix(managed): index attribute constructor owners once per layout (#1943)",
      "body": "fix(managed): index attribute constructor owners once per layout (#1943)\n\nEach CustomAttribute whose constructor is a local MethodDef scanned the\nTypeDef table to find the declaring type, so inspect_managed_artifact did\nO(attributes x types) row decoding. A 584 KB assembly with 16,000 types\nand 16,000 such attributes blocked for about 38 s.\n\nBuild a first-match owner index once per metadata layout. Already-owned\nlist positions are skipped, so overlapping malformed method lists keep\ntheir previous first-match owner in near-linear time. The index is\ncharged to the decode budget, and a build failure is cached like the\nmember pointer lookup.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
