      "sha": "1d4c4eb0308b4cb5761a91533edeb33fcfb442f2",
      "subject": "fix(adb): reject unsafe host file names when pulling one device file (#1962)",
      "body": "fix(adb): reject unsafe host file names when pulling one device file (#1962)\n\npull_adb_file derived its host file name from the last path segment of a\ncaller-supplied device path and joined it to the output directory without\nchecking that the name is usable on the host. A device path ending in a\nseparator, a dot segment, a control character, a Windows reserved device\nname, a trailing dot or space, or a ':' alternate-data-stream marker could\nresolve to an unexpected host path or fail opaquely after the transfer.\n\nThe single-file path now derives the name with POSIX semantics and refuses\nany non-portable segment as invalid_request before creating a directory or\nrunning adb pull. This matches the package path's pending host-name policy\nand never renames a device-reported file.\n\nCo-authored-by: morluto <76467478+morluto@users.noreply.github.com>",
