      "body": "feat(managed): select declaring types in inspect_managed_members\n\nSelect exact declaring types before managed signatures and CIL bodies are decoded, preserving caller choices in CLI/MCP Evidence. Keep unmatched names and selected coverage explicit; comparisons and graphs retain unknowns outside their observed scope. Reuse existing metadata ownership/accounting and advertise unique selections through the actual SDK Schema.\n\nValidated with 229 focused tests across 21 files, 11 managed conformance controls, fullstatic/docs checks and real Linux CLI and fresh MCP inspection of two unchanged DLLs. All 118 selected CIL hashes matched original PE-mapped bytes; result/caller-argument parity and unmatched controls passed. Full artifact/native-boundary metadata is complete; whole-assembly members retain the unchanged 64 MiB resource constraint. No target code executes.\n\nRefs #1878\n\nCo-authored-by: skared <190618464+skoodster@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Ysopwnable <161784452+N0zoM1z0@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: factory-droid[bot] <138933559+factory-droid[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Kaoru0822 <208281322+kaoru0822-kitauji@users.noreply.github.com>",
