      "sha": "43f9c39dfbdfaa6e5bc260b037a506cd1f56fe6d",
      "subject": "fix(setup): configure an empty Hermes config.yaml (#1983)",
      "body": "fix(setup): configure an empty Hermes config.yaml (#1983)\n\n* fix(setup): treat an empty Hermes config.yaml as a new document\n\nYAML parses an empty file to null, so Hermes configuration was checked\nas an object before the shared empty-file rule and rejected. Setup then\nfailed its readback gate for a zero-byte config.yaml, although a missing\nfile is configured and the Hermes serializer already writes a fresh\ndocument for empty original text. Apply the empty-file rule before the\nHermes YAML parse, as #1117 did for JSON clients.\n\n* test(setup): configure an empty Hermes config.yaml\n\nConfigure zero-byte and newline-only config.yaml files through the\nreal filesystem workflow, then read the registration back as aligned.",
