      "sha": "0d11f71e0dc5cf95d3bea093355f7edc09089a68",
      "subject": "fix(managed): admit ReadyToRun images built for non-Windows hosts (#1985)",
      "body": "fix(managed): admit ReadyToRun images built for non-Windows hosts (#1985)\n\nReadyToRun images compiled for Linux, macOS or the BSDs store the COFF machine XORed with IMAGE_FILE_MACHINE_NATIVE_OS_OVERRIDE (dotnet/runtime src/coreclr/inc/pedecoder.h). Every framework assembly in a Linux .NET install has machine 0xFD1D, so target admission and the managed PE reader rejected them as an unsupported architecture.\n\nDecode the PE machine once in src/domain/peMachine.ts, replacing the two duplicated switches, and accept an OS override only on images with a CLI directory.",
