      "sha": "1febc22907f1cc8035dd1450616233121bd7f19d",
      "subject": "fix(wasm): inspect modules whose custom section names contain NUL (#1981)",
      "body": "fix(wasm): inspect modules whose custom section names contain NUL (#1981)\n\n* fix(wasm): frame custom section names at their displayed NUL\n\nwasm-objdump prints a custom section name with printf's %.*s, so an\nembedded NUL ends the displayed name, as it does for module names.\nThe section row was compared with the complete name decoded from WAT,\nso a valid module whose custom section name contains U+0000 failed\ninspection with \"WABT custom-section header does not match decoded\nWAT\". Compare the row with the displayed prefix instead.\n\n* test(wasm): cover NUL-terminated custom section names\n\nFrame the real objdump golden with a decoded custom section name that\ncontinues after a NUL, and keep rejecting a displayed prefix that\ndiffers from the decoded name.\n\n* test(wasm): verify a NUL-containing custom section name with real WABT\n\nAdd a custom section named \"visible\\0hidden\" to the real-tool custom\nname fixture. WABT 1.0.42 decodes it as an escaped WAT name and\ndisplays \"visible\" in wasm-objdump, so the verifier expects that\ndescription through the compiled CLI and MCP.\n\n* refactor(wasm): share WABT's NUL-terminated name display\n\nModule-name preamble lines and custom-section rows each truncated the\ndecoded name at its first NUL. Keep that display rule in one helper so\nboth framings follow the same producer behavior. Output is unchanged.",
