      "sha": "adde8a80921b199ddd7105998f3760d345b468fc",
      "subject": "fix(native): reject required otool fields truncated before their value (#1995)",
      "body": "fix(native): reject required otool fields truncated before their value (#1995)\n\n* fix(native): reject required otool fields truncated before their value\n\n#1967 let requireUniqueField count a label at end of line so an empty\ndylib-use options row is present. That applied to every required field,\nso truncated output such as a bare vmaddr, vmsize, uuid or entryoff line\npassed the presence check while parseField dropped it, and the value\nsilently became null.\n\nLet parseField decide which labeled line carries a value: the single\nmatching line must parse as that field. The empty options row remains\nthe only valueless field parseField admits.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(native): admit the empty segname of Mach-O object files\n\nMH_OBJECT files put their sections in one segment whose name is empty,\nand otool -l prints it as a bare segname label. Requiring a value for\nevery scalar field rejected valid object-file output as unreadable.\n\nLet parseField admit an empty segname like the empty dylib-use options\nrow, and keep projecting an empty or absent segment name as \"unknown\",\nas main did.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(native): admit all-NUL Mach-O section names\n\nAn all-NUL section_64.sectname prints as a bare sectname label, like an\nempty segname. Admit it in parseField and keep projecting the empty name\nas \"unknown\", as main did.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
