      "subject": "fix(javascript): preserve execution and invocation provenance",
      "body": "fix(javascript): preserve execution and invocation provenance\n\nKeep direct empty bridge objects observed, reject unexecuted initializers,\ninvalidate modified bootstrap tables and Electron identities, and retain\nselection predicates through symbolic values and wrapper paths. Track lexical\nbinding identity and completed activation boundaries without leaking analysis\norder into earlier reads.\n\nSeparate wrapper invocation provenance from the underlying IPC source range\nso repeated registrations remain ambiguous through transfer and graph joins.\nUse the same offered transfer budget for module preflight and final writing.\n\nIndex static literal properties once instead of rescanning every member. Keep\nthe original 10,001-member capacity fixture; Flameox confirmed the repeated\nlookup cost and the optimized fixture completes in under one second locally.\nPrune the stale compact-schema tool inventory assertion and update the public\ncall-graph registration expectation to its declared result envelope.\n\nValidation: build, check, docs:check, 83 focused tests, 10 Electron identity\nacceptance cases, 2 full-scale finding-capacity cases, and 7 compact-schema\ntransport tests. No real Electron runtime execution is claimed.\n",
