    {
      "sha": "d9d2a173819ce8e2e7f09eb584ec6ff7b4ee3480",
      "subject": "feat(setup): register DeepSeek Harness through setup, doctor and uninstall (#1929)",
      "body": "feat(setup): register DeepSeek Harness through setup, doctor and uninstall (#1929)\n\n* feat(setup): register DeepSeek Harness through setup, doctor and uninstall\n\nDeepSeek Harness registers MCP clients through a Cordis YAML patch\nsequence in the home patch rather than a server table, so setup could\nnot configure it and users had to append the documented entry by hand.\n\nAdd a dsh client: the home patch $DSH_HOME/cordis.patch.yml\n(~/.dsh/cordis.patch.yml when unset) is parsed as a patch list, the REA\nentry owns the stable rea-mcp id, and setup appends or replaces exactly\nthat entry while preserving unrelated patches and comments in place.\nDoctor reports the registration through the same entry, and uninstall\nremoves it, dropping insert operations it emptied. Skill destinations\nfollow ~/.agents/skills ($DSH_AGENTS_HOME/skills when configured), the\nhome the rest of the client machinery already uses.\n\nFixes #1839\n\n* fix(setup): carry environment and identity validation into DSH registrations\n\nAddress review: the DSH entry discarded discovered provider overrides;\nconfig.env is now emitted and retained like the other dialects. An entry\ncarrying the rea-mcp id under a wrong or missing package name, or\nduplicated entries, reads back as absent so setup rewrites exactly one\ncanonical entry instead of reporting unchanged. Doctor now requires\nserverName rea and stdio transport before calling a DSH registration\naligned, and the Harness skill identifier in the docs matches the\ninstalled reverse-engineer-anything skill.\n\n* fix(setup): apply Cordis patch order and collapse DSH registrations\n\nAddress review: a later direct { id, config } operation replaces the\nrow's config under the native patch DSL, so the registration view now\napplies patches in order instead of only reading insert operations;\ndoctor reports the effective command rather than the inserted one.\nSetup rewrites exactly one canonical entry: duplicate id-matching rows\ncollapse to the first, direct patches to the entry are dropped from the\ndocument and from the edited YAML, and uninstall removes them with the\nentry. The client-location test fixture now clears DSH_HOME and\nDSH_AGENTS_HOME so a developer environment cannot point the suite at\nreal Harness homes.\n\n* fix(setup): repair direct-only registrations and preserve Cordis entry state\n\nSerialize now edits the first insertion carrying rea-mcp in place, so a\ngrouped entry keeps its scope, neighbors, and comments instead of moving\nto a fresh root-level insertion, and later carrying insertions and direct\npatches collapse away. Entry-level disabled state projects into the\nregistration the doctor and setup compare, so a disabled row reads as\nstale and the repair re-enables it. A direct-only registration no longer\nsuppresses the canonical insert append, and an update retains the\nregistration environment. Duplicate entries collapse across operations,\nnot only within one.\n\n* fix(setup): preserve Harness row state through identity and refresh repairs\n\nA wrong-package row still reads back as a server record carrying its\nenvironment and caller fields, projected with a package marker the\nalignment path treats as stale, instead of vanishing and dropping\nconfig.env from the repair. A direct Cordis patch without a preceding\ninsertion configures nothing, so a direct-only registration reads as\nabsent even when its config matches and the repair appends the insert.\nCaller-owned config fields beyond the REA-owned keys, such as the cwd\nthe native verifier sets, survive a refresh instead of being silently\ndropped.\n\n* fix(setup): preserve Cordis tags and collapse aligned Harness rows\n\nA refresh rebuilt Harness config from parsed values, so a caller !!js\nexpression was written back as a literal. Owned keys are now overlaid on\nthe winning config node and other nodes stay in place. Two already-aligned\nrea-mcp insertions read as stale, so setup collapses them to one row, and\nthe bundled skill lists dsh with the other clients.\n\n* fix(setup): drop the unused DSH configuration type\n\nKnip reports DshConfigurationFormat as an unused export. The format union\ndoes not depend on that alias.\n\n* fix(setup): keep Harness env tags and comment-only patches\n\nA refresh replaced the whole env map, so a caller !!js value was written\nback as a literal. Environment entries now stay in place unless the value\nchanged. A comment-only cordis.patch.yml parses as an empty patch list and\nkeeps those comments when the registration is appended. Docs describe\nplain rea uninstall, which scans supported clients and has no --client flag.\n\n* fix(setup): own Harness rows by entry id and expression state\n\nUninstall removes a rea-mcp row even when the launcher is stale or the\npatch never established a server record. A non-boolean disabled value,\nincluding a Cordis expression, reads as stale. Expression text on a known\nenvironment setting is not validated as a literal path, so a refresh can\nkeep the tag.\n\n* fix(setup): collapse aliased Harness insertions\n\nAn anchored insert followed by an alias parses as two rea-mcp rows, but\nthe YAML edit kept the alias, so readback stayed duplicated and setup\nrestored the file. Aliases that resolve to the owned entry are now\ndropped, including an alias of the entry inside one insert. Aliases of\nother patches stay.\n\n* fix(setup): resolve aliased Harness lists and config maps\n\nAn insert value that aliases another entry list still loaded a second\nrea-mcp row after the operation-level alias collapse. That alias is now\ndropped once the anchored list is rewritten. A config: *cfg map is\nresolved and cloned before the refresh, so a caller !!js field on the\naliased map is not rewritten as a plain literal.\n\n* fix(setup): follow Harness aliases for ids, lists, and env tags\n\nAn insert alias whose anchor is not another insert is copied so\nunrelated rows stay while the owned row is rewritten. An aliased\nentry id is resolved before ownership checks, and an environment alias\nof an unchanged !!js scalar is left in place.\n\n* fix(setup): keep aliased Harness env maps through uninstall\n\nAn env alias is cloned before a refresh so tagged values are not rebuilt\nas literals, and expression-key scans follow aliases before path checks.\nInsert aliases that carry REA are recorded before uninstall empties their\nanchor, so the later alias is dropped instead of dangling.\n\n* fix(setup): follow root Harness aliases and mark dsh as main-only\n\nWinning-config walks resolve a root alias before patch order, so a replayed direct config's !!js env is not validated as a literal path. Root aliases that own rea-mcp are recorded before uninstall empties their anchor. An insert whose only owned member is an external alias is cloned so Cordis tags survive. Docs state dsh is not in npm 6.4.0.\n\n* fix(setup): keep rows behind inert Harness aliases\n\nA root alias whose anchor is not a loaded operation is copied and only the owned row is edited, so unrelated rows stay active. Entry id aliases become a scalar before their anchor patch is dropped. Root-alias ownership follows insert-list aliases, so a replay is removed instead of dangling after uninstall.\n\n* refactor(setup): centralize Cordis source ownership\n\n* fix(javascript): share Electron mutation proof with wrapped calls\n\n* test(mcp): align graph and catalog checks with current contracts\n\n* fix(setup): separate Cordis ownership from editability\n\n* docs: clarify ownership and interpretation boundaries\n\n* fix(setup): preserve Cordis applicability and caller metadata\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>\nCo-authored-by: morluto <76467478+morluto@users.noreply.github.com>",
