      "sha": "d0249282c64882329a6acab8f3b477552da53499",
      "subject": "docs(install): explain Claude Code upfront tool loading on third-party endpoints (#2029)",
      "body": "docs(install): explain Claude Code upfront tool loading on third-party endpoints (#2029)\n\nClaude Code turns MCP tool search off when ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL points to a\nnon-first-party host, so every REA tool definition is sent with every\nrequest. On main at 04089d5be the forwarded names, descriptions and input\nschemas measure about 496 KB (~120k tokens) with the full profile and about\n290 KB (~68k tokens) with the compact profile. When Claude Code assumes a\nsmaller window than the model has, as with `deepseek-v4-flash` without the\n`[1m]` suffix, autocompact thrashes because compaction cannot remove tool\ndefinitions.\n\nDocument the window, tool-search and compact-profile remedies, and that\nDeepSeek's Anthropic API does not list `tool_reference` blocks.\n\nRefs #2019\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
