      "sha": "4f46eac453965efde3bc782aebfeec198551afc4",
      "subject": "ci: narrow native-host lane selection and reuse build caches (#2131)",
      "body": "ci: narrow native-host lane selection and reuse build caches (#2131)\n\n* ci: narrow native-host lane selection and reuse build caches\n\nUnowned src/ and bridge/ files no longer fall back to the full baseline.\nThey run the Linux suite plus the Linux x64 installed-package/Inspector\nbaseline. New apple and package scopes own the Apple artifact lane, the\npackage matrix and the Windows curated lane, including the test files those\nlanes invoke. Manual-only verifier entrypoints run static checks and the\nLinux suite. CHANGELOG, SECURITY, GitHub templates and the native Windows\nREADME are documentation-only.\n\nPull requests omit the macOS x64 package host unless labelled ci:full.\nThe Windows and Apple lanes restore the shared Turbo build cache, the\nWindows lane drops its duplicate typecheck, and the Linux suite uses six\nshards. Main pushes keep the full baseline.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* ci: match package script entrypoints against scope globs\n\nScript-only package.json edits resolved their entrypoint with literal\nequality, so glob-owned verifiers such as scripts/verify/apple/** and\nscripts/verify/inspector/** fell back to the full baseline instead of\nselecting their owning lane.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
