      "subject": "fix(managed): report malformed PE layouts as invalid input (#2194)",
      "body": "fix(managed): report malformed PE layouts as invalid input (#2194)\n\n* fix(managed): report malformed PE layouts as invalid input\n\nreadManagedPeLayout raises ManagedReaderFailure for DOS, COFF and section\nheader failures such as section data past EOF. Those escaped the managed\ninspectors, so ManagedStaticProvider wrapped them as ProviderAdapterError\nand the CLI and MCP reported execution_failure with advice to run rea\ndoctor. Map format failures to an invalid_format input issue carrying the\nreader's detail, as inspect-pe-resources and inspect-go-binary do.\n\nFixes #2191\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(managed): route unmappable PE layouts through one input error\n\ninspect-managed-native-boundaries caught a layout-level ManagedReaderFailure\nitself and returned an empty malformed inspection with exit 0, while the\nother managed operations now report the same bytes as invalid input. Let\nthe layout failure reach the provider's invalid_format mapping; metadata\nfailures after a readable layout still return malformed coverage.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
