      "sha": "d35035780a643e38301b8eaea03f01bb506e9df9",
      "subject": "fix(setup): remove emptied skill directories on uninstall (#2182)",
      "body": "fix(setup): remove emptied skill directories on uninstall (#2182)\n\n* fix(setup): remove emptied skill directories on uninstall\n\nUninstall removes only the managed skill files so user files survive,\nbut it left every emptied reverse-engineer-anything directory and its\nreferences/ subdirectory behind. After the ownership manifest is removed,\nremove the managed directories deepest first with a non-recursive rmdir,\nwhich keeps any directory that still holds user files.\n\nFixes #2159\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(setup): report emptied skill directories that cannot be removed\n\nOnly a directory that still holds user files, is already absent, or is no\nlonger a directory is kept silently. Any other rmdir failure, such as a\nparent that denies deletion, now fails the skill item with the directory\npath instead of reporting the skill as removed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
