      "subject": "fix(mcp): keep shared optional providers open across discarded probes (#2205)",
      "body": "fix(mcp): keep shared optional providers open across discarded probes (#2205)\n\nstartMcpTransport loads optional observation providers once per process\nand passes them to every server instance the SDK constructs. Each\ninstance's closeProviders also closed the shared browser scenario\nprovider, so when the SDK discarded a server/discover probe instance for a\nlegacy initialize, every later capture_browser_scenario call failed with\n\"Browser scenario provider is closing.\" Server instances no longer close\nthe caller-supplied provider; the transport returns\ncloseOptionalProviders and process shutdown closes it once.\n\nFixes #2195\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
