      "sha": "10400fdb57e4226c5ce15af17968a664f35498ce",
      "subject": "fix(ida): thin the selected FAT slice into the private headless input (#2201)",
      "body": "fix(ida): thin the selected FAT slice into the private headless input (#2201)\n\nUniversal Mach-O admission reported the selected slice architecture while the IDA provider's private input copy handed the whole FAT container to upstream idalib, which then picked its own slice (x86_64 for /bin/cat) while Evidence labeled the session arm64. FAT parsing now exports the selected slice's byte range as universalSlice, and the private input copy writes exactly those bytes: the whole source digest still anchors the copy against admission-time changes, and the thinned result anchors the post-operation identity check.\n\nThin targets keep the whole-file copy, and mach-o-universal remains the container format across Evidence, snapshots, and provider routing.\n\nValidation: typecheck, oxlint (no new warnings), oxfmt, and targeted vitest runs — ida adapters 12 files/116 tests, domain and services projects 60 files/736 tests, ghidra/hopper behavior 2 files/50 tests, filesystem and universal-extraction boundary 2 files/49 tests, native signature MCP 1 file/2 tests, plus a new thinning suite (5 tests, red before the fix: 3 failed). The thinned product was verified byte-identical to the `clang -arch arm64` input of a `lipo -create` universal fixture. Controlled fixtures only; no live IDA analysis was performed for this change.\n\nCloses #2139",
