      "sha": "7ae3c50a9d49c480035855de9fcc4484befacd92",
      "subject": "docs: correct drift and reorganize English guides (#2207)",
      "body": "docs: correct drift and reorganize English guides (#2207)\n\nPut setup, developer commands, MCP replies, and investigation recipes before\nclient details and implementation references. Preserve existing guide anchors,\nexamples, provenance, partial-result recovery, and provider restrictions.\n\nCorrect verified documentation drift, synchronize the Ghidra capability\nwording, and regenerate metadata for skill version 40. Keep uncertain platform\nand lifecycle findings unchanged. Refs #2156.\n\nValidation: 56 focused tests, check:fast, docs:check, VitePress production build,\nformat and link/example checks. Real isolated CLI/MCP probes cover Ghidra,\nNativeAOT, HAR, cancellation, Chrome, large ELF delivery, native type limits,\nand the new JS/managed/process/setup recipes. Heavy work uses two CPUs;\na resource-heavy DOM probe was stopped and replaced by a smaller real CDP\npayload-limit control. Windows, macOS GUI, ADB, and the full CI matrix were\nnot executed.\n\nCo-authored-by: factory-droid[bot] <138933559+factory-droid[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>",
