      "sha": "51d6c87cdbf5f11eaf3cb1862befe704a81827c5",
      "subject": "feat(clients): register ZCode during setup (#1564)",
      "body": "feat(clients): register ZCode during setup (#1564)\n\n* feat(clients): register ZCode during setup\n\n- SupportedClients: zcode definition (~/.zcode/cli/config.json, format\n  zcode, personal skills at ~/.zcode/skills)\n- ClientConfigurationDocument: zcode dialect reads/writes the nested\n  mcp.servers table; withClientServers now tolerates a missing outer\n  table for fresh documents\n- docs: add ZCode to the supported-clients table with configuration notes\n- tests: zcodeClientConfiguration.test.ts (path resolution, nested\n  upsert, fresh/empty configs, uninstall)\n\nVerified: tsc --noEmit clean; vitest run\ntests/boundary/filesystem/zcodeClientConfiguration.test.ts 6/6.\n\n* fix(clients): preserve ZCode fallback servers and honor enable flag\n\nReview follow-up (#1564), two integration gaps:\n\n- ZCode reads the user-scope ~/.agents/mcp.json fallback only while the\n  native .zcode config defines no servers at all, with no merging. Setup\n  now copies the fallback's mcpServers entries into the native table when\n  writing the first native server, so registrations that only live in\n  the fallback keep loading; the fallback file is left untouched. A\n  malformed fallback fails setup closed (configure and preflight)\n  instead of being silently suppressed.\n- ZCode disables a server with \"enable\": false on its entry, which the\n  generic status parsing (disabled/enabled) did not recognize: doctor\n  reported such a registration as aligned although ZCode never starts\n  it. The ZCode dialect now treats enable: false as disabled (state\n  stale) and setup rewrites the entry on rerun.\n\nDocs describe both behaviors; the bundled REA skill's supported client\nlist includes zcode.\n\nVerified: tsc --noEmit clean; vitest run\ntests/boundary/filesystem/zcodeClientConfiguration.test.ts 10/10;\nnpm run check:fast green; npm run verify:test-discovery 733 files.\n\n* fix(clients): reject non-regular ZCode fallback files before reading\n\nResolve the fallback through the client-config transaction path and the\nregular-file admission before parsing it, so a FIFO or other non-regular\nfile at ~/.agents/mcp.json fails setup closed instead of blocking the\nread indefinitely. Directory and FIFO fallback cases are covered in\ntests, and the preflight remediation names unreadable fallbacks too.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: morluto <76467478+morluto@users.noreply.github.com>",
