      "body": "feat(clients): register Qoder CLI during setup (#1572)\n\n* feat(clients): register Qoder CLI during setup\n\n- SupportedClients: qoder definition (~/.qoder/settings.json, format\n  json, QODER_CONFIG_DIR override honored)\n- Qoder CLI documents mcpServers as the user-scope server table with\n  command/args/env and stdio as the default transport; no personal\n  skills directory is documented, so setup skips the skill copy\n- tests: qoderClientConfiguration.test.ts (path resolution and\n  QODER_CONFIG_DIR override, upsert preserving unrelated settings,\n  fresh/empty configs, uninstall)\n\nVerified: tsc --noEmit clean; vitest run\ntests/boundary/filesystem/qoderClientConfiguration.test.ts 6/6.\n\n* fix(clients): install Qoder CLI's personal REA skill\n\nReview follow-up (#1572): the Qoder CLI Skills documentation lists\n~/.qoder/skills/{skill-name}/SKILL.md with automatic discovery, so the\ndefinition now carries skillPath following Qoder's configuration\nlocation (QODER_CONFIG_DIR honored) and setup installs the bundled\nskill copy there. The installation docs no longer claim Qoder has no\npersonal skills directory, and the bundled REA skill's supported\nclient list includes qoder.\n\nVerified: tsc --noEmit clean; vitest run\ntests/boundary/filesystem/qoderClientConfiguration.test.ts 7/7.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: morluto <76467478+morluto@users.noreply.github.com>",
