      "sha": "c9aecde580d26d4e7745c2623a4efa327a27367e",
      "subject": "fix(frida): reject an unreadable script file before starting a session (#2211)",
      "body": "fix(frida): reject an unreadable script file before starting a session (#2211)\n\n* fix(frida): reject an unreadable script file before starting a session\n\nThe shared instrument_with_frida workflow started the Frida session, which\nattaches or spawns the target, before the provider read a file script\nsource. A missing script file then failed loadScript with a bare\ninvalid_request, and session cleanup resumed the paused spawn, so the\ntarget ran without instrumentation. Check that the selected file is a\nreadable regular file first and report the path, or access_denied for\nEACCES/EPERM, before any device effect.\n\nFixes #2209\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(frida): let cancellation win over the script file check\n\nAn already-aborted request with an unreadable file source returned the\ninput or access-denied error instead of AnalysisCancelledError. Check the\nsignal before the script file preflight and again after it, so file\nsources keep the existing cancellation semantics.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(frida): keep the pre-start checks out of instrument\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
