      "sha": "7711b0000592aa80c7b0412004150313f78feabc",
      "subject": "fix(apple): preflight XML plist nesting before keyed archive decoding (#2161)",
      "body": "fix(apple): preflight XML plist nesting before keyed archive decoding (#2161)\n\n* fix(apple): preflight XML plist nesting before keyed archive decoding\n\ninspect_keyed_archive documented a 128-level nesting limit, but the XML\nplist path reached recursive decoding before any depth check: plist and\nthe prototype-key traversal in parseXmlPropertyList recurse once per\nnesting level, so a ~75 KiB, 3000-level XML plist exhausted the call\nstack and reported Maximum call stack size exceeded instead of the\nbounded-resource limit that shallower over-limit documents (129, 200)\nalready produced. The CLI classified both as truncated, so no crash or\nclassification bypass was involved; the diagnostic was the defect.\n\nReject excessive nesting in parseXmlPropertyList before any recursive\npass, using the projection's own limit (MAX_PLIST_DEPTH) so the error is\nidentical to the one projectPlistValue raises: callers keep the\nlimit/truncated classification with no error-handler translation. Depth\ncounts values the way the projection does - container members nest one\nlevel deeper, dictionary keys name members rather than nesting, and a\nself-closing element is the value at its own level - so the guard\nrejects exactly the documents the projection rejected, at the same\nboundary, and every in-limit document decodes unchanged. The guard sits\nat the shared decoder boundary, so Interface Builder, app Info.plist\nresolution and native inspect_plist gain the same deterministic limit;\nthe binary plist path keeps its existing expansion preflight.\n\nBinary plist behavior, ordinary XML decode, __proto__ omission counting,\nand archive digest/Evidence provenance are unchanged. OpenStep\nautodetection is untouched by this guard, as the existing Interface\nBuilder preflight also scopes its depth check to XML.\n\nRegression coverage: decoder unit tests at and just past the limit for\ndictionary and array nesting with self-closing and opaque markup,\nmodule tests through decodeKeyedArchiveBytes including a valid\nNSKeyedArchiver XML envelope at the limit, a production-boundary test\nthrough inspectBundleKeyedArchive, and the compiled public CLI\nreporting code truncated / reason limit for a 3000-level plist.\n\n* fix(apple): check XML nesting against parsed element structure\n\nReuse the iterative XML decoder document for depth preflight and prototype-key lookup. Bound recursive plist wrappers alongside dictionaries and arrays without interpreting markup inside attributes or DOCTYPE declarations as values.\n\nValidated with 104 focused tests including compiled CLI, MCP prototype-key, and Interface Builder coverage; npm run check and verify:test-discovery passed. No real-provider verification was run.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Zburgers <Zburgers@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: morluto <76467478+morluto@users.noreply.github.com>",
