      "sha": "fd985dbc5b9435918732c0cc1825060af2a3a47e",
      "subject": "fix(apple): join recognized keys from NIBArchive field maps (#2248)",
      "body": "fix(apple): join recognized keys from NIBArchive field maps (#2248)\n\n* fix(apple): join recognized keys from NIBArchive field maps\n\ninspect-asset-catalog returned no resource-key matches for a decoded\nNIBArchive resource whose recognized image key is present in the archive. The\nNIBArchive projection groups an object's decoded fields under the node's\nnibValues attribute beside the class, label and ID it derives from the same\narchive, while the AppKit keyed-archive parser flattens the same fields onto\nthe node. The catalog join read only the top level, so a recognized NSImageName\non a decoded resource produced no row, and the empty-catalog limitation still\nclaimed resource keys were reported as unmatched.\n\nRead an archive object's fields from both shapes, and give the namespace one\nowner by exporting NIB_VALUES_ATTRIBUTE from the projection that writes it.\nThe recognized-field set stays in the catalog analysis, which owns that\ncontract.\n\nVerified with 5 focused catalog tests, check:fast and verify:test-discovery on\nmacOS arm64, and through the public CLI against the reported NIBArchive\nfixture. The keyed-archive control keeps its existing row, and a NIBArchive\nwith only an unrecognized title still produces none. The ibtool-dependent\nnative hierarchy lane requires full Xcode and was unavailable here.\n\n* fix(apple): normalize resource keys at the NIBArchive producer\n\nFold the complementary implementation from #2256 into the earlier #2248 proposal, retaining the original contribution history.\n\nCo-authored-by: Thang Luu <76550342+thangldw@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix(apple): restrict catalog joins to parsed resource nodes\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: 吴佳浩 <wujiahao@supremind.com>\nCo-authored-by: morluto <76467478+morluto@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Thang Luu <76550342+thangldw@users.noreply.github.com>",
