      "subject": "feat(ida): support optional native IDA Free MCP in attached mode (#1544)",
      "body": "feat(ida): support optional native IDA Free MCP in attached mode (#1544)\n\nAdd an explicit attached native IDA MCP compatibility profile while preserving the legacy and headless workflows. Keep recorded input identity, complete source observations and the user's open GUI database. Batch unique callee lookups, conservatively prefilter literal strings, preserve Unicode matching and unavailable caller coverage, and require distinct-function switching in native verification.\n\nVerified with Windows IDA Pro 9.3 and the native MCP plugin built from c9d15d98e8a143fc74f6e14037c48f63889b6d6c with a loopback listener. Production CLI/MCP and an unchanged Windows whoami.exe passed. Windows IDA Free was not used. No personal paths or license registration information are included.\n\nValidation: 200 focused tests, static and documentation checks, architecture guards and discovery passed. Historical same-main warm task measurements improved from 675 to 317 ms; response token estimates fell from 16618 to 11509. Fresh-start, overall CPU and memory improvement were not established. Detailed scope is in experiments/analysis-efficiency/ida-native-windows.md.\n\nCo-authored-by: imissapixel <140405963+imissapixel@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: morluto <76467478+morluto@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: N0zoM1z0 <161784452+N0zoM1z0@users.noreply.github.com>",
