      "sha": "ea2f94d4de2241306158fecdd75f96cd34566694",
      "subject": "fix(wasm): stop appending WABT remediation to unrelated runtime-root failures (#2084)",
      "body": "fix(wasm): stop appending WABT remediation to unrelated runtime-root failures (#2084)\n\ninspect_wasm_artifact's configuration-phase error handler assumed every\nnon-OwnedCommandFailure thrown before the artifact phase was about WABT\ntool/directory resolution, and unconditionally appended \"Supply WABT 1.0.42\nvia absolute REA_WABT_BIN_DIRECTORY; REA does not install tools.\" to the\nreason. WabtArtifactProvider.inspect() also allocates its PrivateRuntimeRoot\nduring the configuration phase, so a PrivateRuntimeRootUnavailableError (the\nWindows native-authority capability, unrelated to WABT) got the same false\nremediation glued onto its own already-correct message, misdirecting anyone\ntroubleshooting a correctly-configured WABT install toward re-checking WABT\ninstead of the real blocker.\n\nClassify PrivateRuntimeRootUnavailableError before the generic\nconfiguration-phase branch, matching the existing convention already used\nin JavaScriptAnalysisWorker.ts and SourceMapCommand.ts: surface it as its\nown AnalysisCapabilityUnavailableError with no userMessage override, letting\nits own message stand.\n\nVerified against a real WABT 1.0.42 Windows release (hash-checked against\nGitHub release metadata) and a real compiled .wasm module: before the fix,\n`reason` read \"REA Windows native controls are unavailable: ENOENT: ...\nSupply WABT 1.0.42 ...\" even with a fully correct REA_WABT_BIN_DIRECTORY;\nafter, `reason` reports only the real cause.",
