      "sha": "5c2956587a1b0d431f72e10df07a1a6363fa066c",
      "subject": "fix(apple): preserve slice identity and macOS boundary diagnostics (#1772)",
      "body": "fix(apple): preserve slice identity and macOS boundary diagnostics (#1772)\n\n* fix(artifacts): name CPU_SUBTYPE_ARM64E_X1 Mach-O slices arm64e\n\nmacOS 27 system binaries such as /bin/ls carry a third FAT slice with\ncpusubtype 0x8000000c. The SDK defines subtype 12 as\nCPU_SUBTYPE_ARM64E_X1, and CPU_SUBTYPE_HAS_ARM64E puts it in the arm64e\nfamily. architectureName knew only subtype 2, so it named the slice\narm64, lipoNameMatches rejected lipo's arm64e.x1 name, and\ninspect-artifact /bin/ls failed with integrity_mismatch.\n\nThe arm64e.x1 test fixture now uses the real subtype. It fails without\nthis change.\n\nRefs #1168, #1765\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(artifacts): classify en-GB hdiutil verify refusals as format failures\n\nhdiutil follows AppleLanguages. With en-GB it writes \"image not\nrecognised\", and verifyFailureReason matched only the US spelling, so a\nfile that is not a disk image got the reason unavailable. Both spellings\nnow give format. Other languages still give unavailable.\n\nRefs #1765\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(process): read the full process table in the lifecycle cleanup check\n\nThe check ran ps -axo command= with the Node default maxBuffer of 1 MiB.\nOn a host with 1905 processes, the output is 1.52 MB, and the test failed\nwith \"stdout maxBuffer length exceeded\".\n\nRefs #1765\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(process): bound cleanup observations to sampled descendants\n\n* fix(apple): retain CPU subtype identity during dylib resolution\n\n* test(process): retain OS PIDs for descendant observations\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: David Lee <davidlee@Dav3Book-Pro-M4-Max.local>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: morluto <76467478+morluto@users.noreply.github.com>",
