      "sha": "3b0ea590fcc876fa017946f4cec009d653f02b38",
      "subject": "fix(native): honor Mach-O chained pointer locations and library ordinals (#1709)",
      "body": "fix(native): honor Mach-O chained pointer locations and library ordinals (#1709)\n\n* fix(native): honor Mach-O chained pointer locations and library ordinals\n\nWalk declared page starts and next links before decoding chained pointers,\npreserving plain pointers between fixups, zero-offset rebases, and known\nfacts in malformed chains. Interpret positive dylib ordinals with dyld's\nspecial-ordinal cutoff so valid dependency provenance is retained.\n\nGive the Swift verification fixture an explicit module name so link-mode\nfilenames do not produce invalid identifiers.\n\nValidation: 46 focused regressions; pre-fix reproductions in an isolated\ncopy; real macOS CLI/MCP verification of 10 compiled Objective-C/Swift,\narm64/arm64e, chained/legacy and symbols/stripped fixture variants.\n\n* perf(native): reuse parsed Mach-O chain membership\n\n* test(native): validate parsed-chain repair against local gates\n\n* test(native): pin chained fixup page failure provenance\n\n* fix(native): bound parsed chained page facts and metadata\n\n* test(server): pin shared partial Evidence provenance\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: baron <richstyles@gmail.com>",
