    {
      "sha": "653067d799591ce2b8fdc84e99c160ac17e2860f",
      "subject": "fix(javascript): resolve module-relative Worker URL references (#2104)",
      "body": "fix(javascript): resolve module-relative Worker URL references (#2104)\n\n* fix(javascript): resolve module-relative Worker URL references\n\n* fix(javascript): validate Worker URL paths independently of suffixes\n\n* fix(javascript): preserve directory-form Worker URL paths\n\n* fix(javascript): unwrap type assertions in Worker URL references\n\n* fix(javascript): validate Worker bindings before URL resolution\n\n* fix(javascript): leave drive-letter Worker URLs unresolved\n\nUse WHATWG file URL parsing before pathname decoding to detect drive-letter\nforms whose resource identity depends on the unmodeled source URL scheme.\nPreserve encoded and ordinary relative pipe paths, and cover false matches\nthrough the compiled CLI and resolver boundary tests.\n\n* fix(javascript): preserve Worker URL identity boundaries\n\nRecognize known Worker bindings before filtering callee spellings so ESM\naliases and transparent constructor wrappers reach URL analysis. Keep\nroot-relative module URLs unknown without a modeled runtime base root.\n\nIndex direct source-local global writes with the shared mutation collector\nbefore promoting URL and browser Worker constructors. Preserve lexical\nshadowing and unrelated property identities, and exercise all three review\nregressions through the compiled CLI.\n\n* fix(javascript): invalidate mutated import.meta URL bases\n\nTrack source-local import.meta writes alongside ambient global writes so\nWorker URL expressions keep an unknown base after a possible URL mutation.\nTag the identity roots independently and cover direct mutation and unrelated\nproperty cases through the compiled CLI.\n\n* fix(javascript): close Worker URL identity and pathname gaps\n\nResolve ambient object identities before appending written properties, and\nretain possible source-local aliases across rebinding. Reuse intrinsic\ninvocation handling for aliased and bound mutators, array spreads, and\ntransparent TypeScript wrappers while preserving Electron write semantics.\n\nKeep malformed-percent nested Worker URL pathnames unknown because the base\nscheme is unavailable and Node rejects these file URLs. Preserve tolerant\nHTML URL handling, valid escapes, and query/fragment evidence.\n\nCover the new cases and unrelated writes through the compiled CLI with\nexisting-file decoys. All 591 targeted tests and npm run check pass.\n\n* fix(javascript): bound alias expansion and classify Worker paths\n\nJoin ambient identity projections instead of enumerating alias histories.\nMemoize repeated value and provenance queries while preserving capture,\ndepth, and cycle-dependent uncertainty.\n\nKeep Node Worker string arguments unresolved without filesystem or cwd\ncontext, and admit qualified global URL constructors through identity checks.\n\nValidate three 40-level alias branch shapes through the compiled CLI,\n925 source tests, 25 CLI/boundary tests, and the full npm run check gate.\n\n* fix(server): preserve partial Evidence target-content provenance\n\nPass the exact named contract returnsTargetContent flag through the shared partial-Evidence error delivery path introduced by the shortlist integration.\n\nExercise successful and failed recording through in-memory MCP for marked and unmarked contracts, preserving source payload and original failures. Observe both shared-handler emission and wire delivery so the SDK error-marker fallback cannot hide omissions. Suppressing the flag fails exactly the two marked cases.\n\nValidation: check:fast, check, 736 semantic tests, 29 MCP transport/error tests and six compiled static Worker CLI journeys pass. No live target/provider execution or hosted publication.\n\n* fix(javascript): structurally share semantic dependency proofs\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: baron <richstyles@gmail.com>",
