      "sha": "7017c4d68cab49aed998283e09069d9d791e1b0b",
      "subject": "fix(artifacts): read every ZIP package family extraction is asked to open (#2493)",
      "body": "fix(artifacts): read every ZIP package family extraction is asked to open (#2493)\n\nextract_artifact carried its own copy of the ZIP package format list with five\nof the eight members the domain owner declares, and used it both as the guard\nthat refuses a format without an extraction reader and as the selector for the\nreader itself. A .hap, .hsp or App Pack target was therefore refused with\n\"Artifact format has no extraction reader\" even though the next branch builds a\nZipArtifactReader for exactly those formats, while inventory_artifact classifies\nthe same path through the owner and reads it.\n\nImport isZipPackageFormat from the domain owner and delete the duplicate list\nand its predicate, removing the second representation instead of reconciling it.\nThe reader branch now narrows to ZipPackageFormat, which is what the\nZipArtifactReader constructor already requires.\n\nVerified with 41 boundary extraction, ZIP integrity and detection tests,\ncheck:fast and verify:test-discovery on macOS arm64. Reverting only the source\nchange fails exactly the three added families and leaves the zip control green.\n\nCo-authored-by: 吴佳浩 <wujiahao@supremind.com>",
