      "sha": "d73ed6fce24f6d1372c80319cd41d29d66666159",
      "subject": "fix(domain): preserve retryable capability failures through redaction (#2494)",
      "body": "fix(domain): preserve retryable capability failures through redaction (#2494)\n\nredactExplicitFailure rebuilds each typed failure field by field so explicit\nliterals are removed while the projected code stays the same. The rebuild for\nAnalysisCapabilityUnavailableError carried providerId, operation, reason and\nuserMessage but not retryable, and the constructor defaults that field to false.\nRedacting a transient capability failure therefore made it permanent and changed\nthe remediation shown to the caller.\n\nPass the field through with the same conditional-spread shape used for\nuserMessage. The constructor recomputes retryable from cleanupIncomplete, and\ncleanup is already part of the reconstructed context, so a value that was true\nbefore redaction stays true and a false value stays absent.\n\nVerified with 66 error projection, access-denied, redaction and capture-failure\ntests, check:fast and verify:test-discovery on macOS arm64. The regression test\nfailed with \"expected false to be true\" before the change.\n\nCo-authored-by: 吴佳浩 <wujiahao@supremind.com>",
