      "sha": "2c6a4fac4ff3477ac14f3d780894c5b390880607",
      "subject": "fix(process): accept a trace identifier the comparison result can represent (#2488)",
      "body": "fix(process): accept a trace identifier the comparison result can represent (#2488)\n\nThe trace specification owns the declared identifier vocabulary and the\ncomparison result echoes those identifiers verbatim into raw_trace[].event_id,\nmatched_variant and diagnostic event_ids. The result module restated the shared\nIDENTIFIER_PATTERN by hand with a 64-character cap, so a specification with a\nlonger identifier validated and then its own comparison result failed to parse:\ncompareProcessTraces threw a raw ZodError at the caller instead of returning a\ncomparison.\n\nExport the identifier schema from the specification as the single owner and\nreuse it in the evaluation module, removing the capped copy. IDENTIFIER_PATTERN\nhas no length bound and every other consumer uses it unbounded, so the\nduplicate was the outlier. Removing the bound rather than adding one keeps the\nadvertised trace_spec input contract unchanged; identifiers of 64 characters or\nfewer behave exactly as before.\n\nVerified with 48 process tests, 24 boundary CLI/MCP trace tests, check:fast and\nverify:test-discovery on macOS arm64. The regression test failed with the\nZodError before the change and passes after it.\n\nCo-authored-by: 吴佳浩 <wujiahao@supremind.com>",
      "parents": ["c6acd19b6d842699ab807d9526dc762c743686f4"],
