    {
      "sha": "20f51d7286b1759e42f99c0512c73230052dda86",
      "subject": "fix(native): name the ownership helper prerequisite in command failures (#2506)",
      "body": "fix(native): name the ownership helper prerequisite in command failures (#2506)\n\n* fix(native): name the ownership helper prerequisite in command failures\n\nEvery supervised native command launch needs the Darwin process-ownership\nhelper. When that helper cannot be compiled (relative REA_DARWIN_SWIFTC_PATH,\nmissing SDKROOT, a missing compiler, or an SDK/compiler mismatch), the\nrunner reduced the typed DarwinProcessOwnershipInspectionError to a bare\n`io` failure. inspect_macho then reported `execution_failure` with no hint,\nand inspect_artifact on any universal Mach-O said only \"lipo could not\nenumerate universal Mach-O slices\".\n\nThe runner now keeps the inspection message as the failure's `detail` at\nthe launch boundary and carries it through xcrun resolution. The native\nprovider adds it to its diagnostics and the slice reader appends it to its\nmessage, matching what the SQLite and capture providers already report.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(native): cover the provider's ownership helper diagnostics\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
