    {
      "sha": "6a05248d464387c0ce4ec1577b4c1b24d3d355c7",
      "subject": "perf(frida): evict captured messages without copying the whole queue (#2628)",
      "body": "perf(frida): evict captured messages without copying the whole queue (#2628)\n\nOnce a Frida session reached its 16 MiB capture budget, every new message\nevicted the oldest one with Array#shift, re-serialized it to recover its\nbyte charge, and searched and spliced its per-script array. Each of\nthose is linear in the retained messages, so with about 188k small\nmessages retained the cost per message rose from 0.14 µs to 32 µs and\ncapped the main thread at roughly 31k messages per second, which a\nhooked hot function can exceed.\n\nKeep both queues as head-offset FIFOs that compact once half their slots\nare evicted, and record each message's charge when it is admitted.\nArrival order already makes the globally oldest message the oldest one\nof its script, so per-script eviction becomes a head check. Eviction is\nnow amortized O(1) at about 0.14 µs per message; retained messages,\ntheir order and the truncation flag are unchanged.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
