      "sha": "cd2ad1f24084e68910e4ceab4a33e1b88998ebe7",
      "subject": "fix(artifacts): report malformed ZIP archives as format failures (#2683)",
      "body": "fix(artifacts): report malformed ZIP archives as format failures (#2683)\n\n* fix(artifacts): report malformed ZIP archives as format failures\n\nzip.js signals archive faults (missing end-of-central-directory record,\nunrecognized format, overlapping members, corrupt member data,\nunsupported compression) as plain Errors. ZipArtifactReader passed them\nthrough untyped, so the artifact provider's fallback reported every one\nas `io` with no detail and told the caller to \"check file access\".\n\nType these faults at the ZIP reader boundary: structural and data\ncorruption become `format` failures and unsupported archive features\nbecome `unavailable`, each carrying the zip.js reason as detail. This\ncovers enumeration, the getData rejection, and the WritableStream abort\npath that delivers corrupt-data errors first.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(artifacts): share the ZIP inventory failure assertion\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
