      "sha": "ec4f4ddc588a564b75d69249b4ebbe4d4051c792",
      "subject": "fix(ghidra): read UTF-8 signed language definitions (#2772)",
      "body": "fix(ghidra): read UTF-8 signed language definitions (#2772)\n\nBuffer#toString kept a leading UTF-8 byte order mark as U+FEFF, so the\nstrict XML parser rejected a valid .ldefs file as content outside the root\nelement and aborted the whole language catalog read. XML 1.0 section 4.3.3\ndefines the mark as an encoding signature; decode with TextDecoder, which\nconsumes it. Malformed XML is still rejected.\n\nFixes #2533\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
