      "sha": "1ca5fd38b4833ac3fe6213a55e5abfd426228266",
      "subject": "fix(cli)!: keep a selected JSON null in --filter-output output (#2333)",
      "body": "fix(cli)!: keep a selected JSON null in --filter-output output (#2333)\n\ncreateCliResultOutput rendered an explicit null selected by\n--filter-output as the empty document {}, the same output it uses when\nthe selection has no value at all. On the streamed JSON/JSONL path,\na consumer could not distinguish a selected null from a missing field.\n\nWrite a selected null as null in streamed JSON and JSONL. This also\npreserves an unfiltered top-level null. The {} fallback stays for\nundefined, functions and symbols. The --full-output envelope already\ncarried data: null for a selected null. The --token-count path still\nhands results that fit the formatted-string limit back to Incur and\nprints 0 for a selected null. Other formats and Incur-owned result\npaths are unchanged.\n\nConsumers must accept JSON null for a present null and distinguish it\nfrom a missing selection. Use --full-output if an object envelope is\nrequired. Keeping the old shared {} representation would continue\nhiding this distinction.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019TTGAv6fe859ebbCLLfLHP\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
