      "sha": "d3a55720fc4aac8f9d2c5f5a4c9f20cdf5594d8e",
      "subject": "fix(setup): keep Hermes config numbers as written (#2368)",
      "body": "fix(setup): keep Hermes config numbers as written (#2368)\n\nSetup and uninstall re-printed every number in an existing Hermes\nconfig.yaml from a JavaScript number. Hermes reads the file as YAML 1.1\nwith exact integers, so a Discord channel ID lost its low digits, an\noctal mode such as 0600 became 600, and 0.0000001 became 1e-7, which\nYAML 1.1 does not define as a float. Two IDs that round to the same\ndouble were also rejected as duplicate keys, so setup could not\nregister at all.\n\nHermes YAML parsing and editing move to HermesConfigurationYaml. A parsed\nnumber is written with its source spelling while that spelling still\nreads as the node's value, the rule yaml's own boolean tag follows, and\ntwo keys are duplicates only when both their value and their spelling\nmatch. Parsed values stay JavaScript numbers.",
