      "sha": "0ca70e121c43db41d02c5afb6439e15cbf335289",
      "subject": "fix(ghidra): pre-create the launch-support config directory (#2470)",
      "body": "fix(ghidra): pre-create the launch-support config directory (#2470)\n\n* fix(ghidra): pre-create the launch-support config directory\n\nGhidra's launch support resolves its JDK before the headless run starts and\npersists that choice under `<config>/ghidra/<release directory>`. Inside REA's\nprivate runtime a child JVM cannot create those directories, so the first\nWindows Ghidra query aborted at ghidra.launch.AppConfig.saveJavaHome with:\n\n    java.io.IOException: Failed to create directory:\n    ...\\config\\ghidra\\ghidra_12.1.4_PUBLIC\n        at ghidra.launch.AppConfig.saveJavaHome(AppConfig.java:145)\n        at LaunchSupport.findJavaHome(LaunchSupport.java:210)\n\nLaunchSupport then fell back to its interactive prompt, read EOF, and reported\n\"JDK 21+ (64-bit) could not be found and must be manually chosen!\", so the\nprovider failed with \"Ghidra exited before bridge startup\" even though\n`rea doctor` reported a valid Ghidra installation and JDK.\n\nCreate the release directory while this process still owns the runtime, leaving\nGhidra only a file write inside it. The release coordinate comes from the\ninstallation's Ghidra/application.properties (application.version plus\napplication.release.name) with the extraction directory name as a fallback. On\nWindows each level goes through the native private-runtime owner, which opens\nevery existing component and creates only the final one.\n\nVerified on Windows x64 with Ghidra 12.1.4, a 64-bit Temurin JDK 21, and REA's\npackaged native addon: `rea inspect <x64 PE DLL> --provider ghidra` and the\nequivalent MCP `binary_overview` call both complete and report 21 segments,\n1436 procedures, and 2761 strings. Windows Ghidra remains read-only P0; this\nchange does not extend that boundary.\n\n* style(ghidra): format launch configuration regressions\n\n* fix(ghidra): reuse Java Properties parsing for launch release identity\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: AbdulAzizShanShi <441650742@QQ.COM>\nCo-authored-by: morluto <76467478+morluto@users.noreply.github.com>",
