      "sha": "8e6f37e2a0873ac21ebcc889c27839bfcb7552ca",
      "subject": "fix(formats): preserve high bits in remaining magic-byte checks (#2384)",
      "body": "fix(formats): preserve high bits in remaining magic-byte checks (#2384)\n\n* fix(formats): preserve high bits in remaining magic-byte checks\n\nNode's \"ascii\" decoder masks the high bit, so byte-for-byte signature\ncomparisons accepted lookalikes such as CD DA (\"MZ\" | 0x80) or a\nhigh-bit \"bplist00\"/\"NIBArchive\" header. ac57c88ef fixed this for the\nshared DOS/MZ reader; apply the same latin1 decoding to the remaining\nsignature checks: NativeAOT and Windows native loader MZ/PE, binary\nplist and NIBArchive detection, and PNG IHDR checks.\n\nDisplay-name decodes (section and metadata stream names) are unchanged.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* style(windows): format signature admission regressions\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: morluto <76467478+morluto@users.noreply.github.com>",
