    {
      "sha": "e0bd31c18c84fc406ad1c1fe412bc9018ede44ec",
      "subject": "fix(ghidra): bound the Java version probe output (#2361)",
      "body": "fix(ghidra): bound the Java version probe output (#2361)\n\nThe Java version probe captured its output with maxBuffer set to Infinity, so a\nchatty or hostile JVM selected as the Ghidra launcher could grow the captured\nstdout/stderr without limit and exhaust REA's memory during installation\ndiscovery. Bound the capture to 1 MiB, matching the budget already used for\nother Java listings. A probe that exceeds the budget yields no observation and\nis reported through the existing failed-probe path, the same one the Java check\nalready uses whenever the probe cannot produce an observation.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>",
