    {
      "sha": "5f8af4ee5f615e97f343d70d91a74568d0ec9fbd",
      "subject": "feat(ida): resolve containing procedures and report the admitted program as the document (#2374)",
      "body": "feat(ida): resolve containing procedures and report the admitted program as the document (#2374)\n\n* test(mcp): expect trace_feature to report references the provider truncated\n\nA provider that reports a capped xrefs read makes the trace truncated with a residual unknown for that target. An explicit complete report and a provider that reports nothing leave the trace as before.\n\n* fix(mcp): report references a provider truncated in trace_feature\n\nExecutions gain an optional flag for a capped xrefs read, set by the IDA adapter from the upstream cap. trace_feature marks the trace truncated with a residual unknown for that target only when the provider reports a truncation; a provider that reports nothing keeps its previous result. The trace_feature workflow profile is revised so earlier results are not replayed.\n\n* refactor(ida): report reference truncation whenever the runner observed an xrefs cap\n\n* test(mcp): cover session forwarding, per-target state, native reports and failures of the trace coverage\n\n* test(mcp): format the session forwarding test\n\n* test(ida): expect headless IDA to resolve containing procedures from lookups and segment facts\n\nCover positive and negative containment, segment boundaries including addresses above 2^53, failures of the lookup and of the segment survey, cancellation, input validation and the admitted program as the only document.\n\n* test(ida): expect feature tracing and address context to work on headless IDA\n\nRun trace_feature, including a capped reference read, and inspect_address_context with and without an explicit document through the IDA session client.\n\n* test(mcp): expect trace_feature availability to follow the search operations it calls\n\n* fix(mcp): derive trace_feature availability from the search operations it calls\n\n* feat(ida): resolve containing procedures and report the admitted program as the document\n\nThe modern headless profile resolves an address through the function lookup and, when no function contains it, tells a mapped address from an unmapped one using the database-scoped minimal survey. A survey that is missing, truncated or inconsistent fails the read. list_documents reports the single admitted program. The attached profiles do not declare either operation.\n\n* docs(ida): describe containing procedures, the admitted document and truncated feature traces\n\n* test(ida): verify containing procedures, the admitted document and feature tracing on real IDA\n\n* docs(testing): list the headless IDA workflows the real lane verifies\n\n* test(ida): make each survey failure case isolate a single defect\n\n* test(ida): pin large addresses, segment order, document identity, attached refusals and each trace_feature prerequisite\n\n* test(mcp): expect a repeated reference source to be resolved once in trace_feature\n\n* fix(mcp): resolve the containing procedure of a repeated reference source once\n\n* test(ida): trace the fixture procedure and derive probe addresses from its facts in the real lane\n\n* test(process): format processCaptureLifecycle.test.ts after the merge\n\n* test(ida): declare the alignment each synthetic universal slice offset satisfies\n\n* refactor(ida): move the real lane's feature trace assertions into a helper\n\n* test(ida): expect the real lane's feature trace check to accept references to every matched address\n\n* fix(ida): check each trace reference against its own matched address in the real lane\n\n* test(ida): pin that the new operations reject a document other than the admitted program\n\n* refactor(ida): move the real lane's mapped non-function probe into a helper\n\n* test(ida): expect the real lane's mapped data probe to skip strings inside functions\n\n* fix(ida): try the target's strings in order for the mapped non-function probe\n\n* test(ida): declare the real lane helper types for the verifier tests\n\n* test(ida): expect the real lane to reject a listed string that resolves as unmapped\n\n* fix(ida): fail the real lane when a listed string resolves as unmapped",
      "parents": ["e0bd31c18c84fc406ad1c1fe412bc9018ede44ec"],
      "authors": [
