      "sha": "97dc6581f45adfe5fcaa9c98e77e7dc6bc423a6e",
      "subject": "fix(dotnet): name the instruction when a CIL operand leaves the method body (#2697)",
      "body": "fix(dotnet): name the instruction when a CIL operand leaves the method body (#2697)\n\nThe decoder already reports \"Instruction X at IL offset N leaves method\nbody\" when an operand's computed end passes the IL body, but only after\nthe operand was read. Operand readers use Buffer reads, so an operand\ncut off by the body end threw a RangeError first. The catch-all stored\nNode's message (\"Attempt to access memory outside buffer bounds\" or an\noffset RangeError) as body.issue, dropping the instruction and offset.\nA body ending in a lone 0xFE two-byte opcode prefix failed the same way.\n\nTreat a RangeError from the operand read as the operand leaving the body\nso the existing diagnostic applies, and check the second opcode byte\nbefore reading it. Malformed status, partial coverage and earlier\ndecoded instructions are unchanged.\n\nFixes #2677\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
