      "sha": "e46bed73f190484984c42efcb6fae0ccc42da4ee",
      "subject": "fix(managed): decode the CIL no. prefix (#2241)",
      "body": "fix(managed): decode the CIL no. prefix (#2241)\n\nThe CIL opcode table held five of the six ECMA-335 prefix opcodes and\nomitted no. (FE 19 <unsigned int8>, III.2.2). A method body using it was\nreported as malformed with \"Unsupported CIL opcode 0xfe19\", losing its\ninstruction counts and normalized IL digest.\n\nDecode it with its one-byte check mask and treat it as a prefix, so it\nshares an instruction boundary with the opcode it modifies.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_012pRGskbPGjT444CgJfuhhj\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
