    {
      "sha": "c44d17fd3c4c71b86fcae401d9ff1088b4e27170",
      "subject": "fix(pwntools): let callers widen the artifact input bound (#2486)",
      "body": "fix(pwntools): let callers widen the artifact input bound (#2486)\n\n* fix(pwntools): let callers widen the artifact input bound\n\nThe pwntools adapters rejected every artifact over 32 MiB before any\nanalysis ran, and nothing in configuration, environment, CLI or MCP\ncould raise that bound, so real recorded core dumps stayed unanalyzable.\n\nResolve the bound from REA_PWNTOOLS_MAX_INPUT_BYTES in front of the\nshipped default. An absent value keeps 32 MiB, and a value outside\n1..1073741824 bytes is refused as unusable provider configuration before\nthe artifact is read instead of falling back silently.\n\n* fix(pwntools): name the bound variable in its own refusal\n\nAn unusable REA_PWNTOOLS_MAX_INPUT_BYTES travelled through the shared\nengine-absence helper, which always stamped configuration_key\nREA_PWNTOOLS_PYTHON, so a caller following that field was pointed at the\nPython executable instead of the bound it had just set. The guide also\ndescribed the refusal as an invalid request while the decoder reports\nprovider_unavailable.\n\nLet the failure context carry the key under review and pass the bound's\nown name at that call site, then state the code callers actually receive\nin the guide. Assert the key on the projected rejection so the engine\ndefault and the bound override each stay attributed to the right setting.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: morluto <76467478+morluto@users.noreply.github.com>",
