      "subject": "fix(go): classify JVM class files instead of universal Mach-O for CAFEBABE bytes (#2458)",
      "body": "fix(go): classify JVM class files instead of universal Mach-O for CAFEBABE bytes (#2458)\n\n* test(go): pin JVM class files as unsupported Go images\n\nThe regression fails on main: readGoBinaryImage(javaClassFile()) reports\n\"Universal/fat Mach-O containers require selecting a thin slice\" for a\nJVM class file whose bytes 4..7 are minor/major version, not nfat_arch.\n\n* fix(go): classify JVM class files instead of universal Mach-O\n\nRoute the four FAT magics through the shared readFatContainerHeader and\nclassifyFatContainerIdentity facts added for the same disambiguation in\nthe artifact and target lanes (921bb9575). Keep the thin-slice failure\nonly when the container identity is confirmed Mach-O; a JVM class file\nnow falls through to the generic only-ELF/PE/thin-Mach-O failure.\n\n* test(go): pin universal Mach-O thin-slice failure with FAT fixtures\n\nCover the kept behavior with the repository's own fatImage/machoImage\nbuilders (narrow and FAT64 tables) so the regression also proves real\nuniversal containers keep the slice-selection failure.\n\n* test(go): cover little-endian FAT magics in the universal container control\n\n* fix(go): require positive universal Mach-O identity\n\nRequire positive Mach-O identity before reporting a universal thin-slice remedy; malformed FAT-shaped bytes are not proof. Add the JVM constant-pool CPU lookalike to the existing fixture control.\n\nSource inspection and git diff --check; tests/builds/typechecks/CI reruns skipped at explicit user request.\n\n* fix(go): retain malformed FAT header diagnostics\n\nPreserve the owning FAT header parser reason for malformed headers while requiring positive Mach-O proof before the universal-slice remedy.\n\nSource inspection and git diff --check only. Tests, builds and typechecks skipped by explicit user request. GitHub review writes paused globally.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: morluto <76467478+morluto@users.noreply.github.com>",
