    {
      "sha": "c6503edfc4afdc0de6812ba3f7cd0909df5555f7",
      "subject": "ci: pin GitHub Actions to full commit SHAs (#1901)",
      "body": "ci: pin GitHub Actions to full commit SHAs (#1901)\n\n* ci: pin GitHub Actions to full commit SHAs\n\nReplace every third-party `uses: owner/repo@vN` reference in\n.github/workflows with the 40-character commit SHA that the tag\ncurrently resolves to, keeping the exact release as a trailing comment.\nEach pin was checked with `git ls-remote --tags`: the floating major tag\nand the commented release dereference to the same commit. Local\nreusable workflows are unchanged.\n\nRe-pin reactivecircus/android-emulator-runner from the SHA of the\nannotated `v2` tag object (4c44018e) to the commit it points to\n(a421e438, v2.38.0); Actions resolves both, but only the commit SHA is\nan immutable reference that tooling can compare with the release.\n\nUpdate the Windows Ghidra workflow trust-boundary test to require\nSHA-pinned setup-node and upload-artifact references instead of the\nprevious floating tags.\n\nValidation: actionlint v1.7.7 (-shellcheck= -pyflakes=, as in CI), YAML\nparse of all workflows, no remaining unpinned third-party `uses:`, and\nthe workflow boundary/conformance tests.\n\n* style(ci): format action identity assertion\n\nRetain formatting edits produced before the user stopped validation.\n\nSource inspection and git diff --check only. Tests, builds and typechecks skipped by explicit user request. GitHub review writes paused globally.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: morluto <76467478+morluto@users.noreply.github.com>",
