      "sha": "5d12a0b4b6137f025d9aa88cf001dc2a68c28b8a",
      "subject": "test(web): cover nullable HTTP captures through CDP and CLI (#1834)",
      "body": "test(web): cover nullable HTTP captures through CDP and CLI (#1834)\n\n* fix(browser): preserve unknown HTTP response comparison fields\n\n* fix(browser): retain proven request inventory changes\n\n* fix(javascript): preserve Electron identity and avoid quadratic property scans\n\nShare visible Electron mutations with wrapper expansion, index static object\nliteral properties once, and align MCP assertions with current contracts.\n\n* fix(javascript): track writes through symbolic Electron aliases\n\nResolve mutation targets through the same factories, module tables, containers,\nand conditional origins as call analysis. Share mutation coverage between\ndirect and wrapper scans while isolating origin caches and preserving exact\nproperty paths, local rebinding semantics, and analysis resource limits.\n\n* fix(javascript): preserve container slots and imported mutation origins\n\n* perf(javascript): defer container mutation replay until property reads\n\n* fix(javascript): preserve captured object identities and write order\n\n* fix(javascript): preserve ordered mutation origins\n\n* fix(javascript): honor property mutation constraints\n\n* test(web): narrow PR to HTTP and CLI comparison regressions\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: morluto <76467478+morluto@users.noreply.github.com>",
