      "sha": "23f72141d5befc6b14286ae7281c367d593f84bb",
      "subject": "fix(javascript): keep configuration setting reads out of endpoints (#2402)",
      "body": "fix(javascript): keep configuration setting reads out of endpoints (#2402)\n\n* fix(javascript): keep configuration setting reads out of endpoints\n\nStatic endpoint extraction reads the first literal argument of any call\nnamed get as an HTTP request path unless the receiver is a provable keyed\ncollection. VS Code extension bundles read settings through\n`workspace.getConfiguration(section).get(key)`, so every setting key\nbecame a network endpoint: the bundled Git extension's dist/main.js\nreported 173 network endpoints, nearly all of them setting names such as\n`autofetchPeriod` and `blame.statusBarItem.enabled`.\n\nThe lexical receiver classifier now records a `configuration` fact for a\n`.get` call whose receiver is a `getConfiguration(...)` call, inline or\nthrough a binding whose only visible write is one unconditional\ninitializer. Minifiers emit `let` for these bindings, so the proof relies\non the recorded writes rather than the declaration kind, as tRPC client\nroot resolution already does. Endpoint extraction skips non-URL literals\nfor that fact in both application and web bundle analysis. Reassigned,\nconditional, and shadowed receivers, URL or path literals, and other\nclients such as `api.get(\"users\")` keep their endpoints.\n\nThe receiver fact union was duplicated in three modules; consumers now\nimport the classifier's type.\n\nOn the Git extension bundle, network endpoints drop from 173 to 7 with\nunchanged analysis time (2.1 s).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(javascript): require the workspace host for configuration receivers\n\nA bare or differently scoped `getConfiguration(...)` may be an\napplication's own HTTP client factory, so `.get(\"users\")` on its result\nlost its endpoint. Only `workspace.getConfiguration(...)` and\n`<x>.workspace.getConfiguration(...)` now produce the configuration fact.\nMinifiers keep property names, so the bundled VS Code Git extension still\nreports 7 network endpoints instead of 173.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(javascript): recognize default VS Code namespace imports\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: morluto <76467478+morluto@users.noreply.github.com>",
