      "sha": "4c79127fcb31c5e85c4806f5a9522e00674f10e4",
      "subject": "fix(sqlite): classify a missing database path as an invalid value (#2775)",
      "body": "fix(sqlite): classify a missing database path as an invalid value (#2775)\n\n* fix(sqlite): classify a missing database path as an invalid value\n\nThe snapshot reported an absent selected database as an artifact path\nfailure, which the adapter projects as invalid_format alongside malformed\npaths and content. The snapshot owns the absence observation, so it now\nreturns an invalid_value input issue on path directly, matching the\nadapter's existing ENOENT/ENOTDIR classification.\n\nFixes #2614\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(sqlite): classify a missing database path as an invalid value\n\nThe snapshot reported an absent selected database as an artifact path\nfailure, which the adapter projects as invalid_format alongside malformed\npaths and content. The snapshot owns the absence observation, so it now\nreturns an invalid_value input issue on path directly, matching the\nadapter's existing ENOENT/ENOTDIR classification.\n\nFixes #2614\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: morluto <76467478+morluto@users.noreply.github.com>",
