    {
      "sha": "c22d7cd7567b52e6e6ba13f14df11c4a720c0c4e",
      "subject": "fix(browser): keep malformed Content-Length declarations unknown (#2773)",
      "body": "fix(browser): keep malformed Content-Length declarations unknown (#2773)\n\n* fix(browser): keep malformed Content-Length declarations unknown\n\nResponse metadata normalized Content-Length with Number(), truncation and\nclamping, so \"-5\", \"0x10\", \"1e3\" and \"+12\" became observed lengths 0, 16,\n1000 and 12. RFC 9110 section 8.6 defines the field as 1*DIGIT; any other\nspelling declares no length. Parse only decimal digits within the safe\ninteger range and keep every other value null.\n\nFixes #2596\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(browser): cover the largest accepted Content-Length\n\nPin the safe-integer boundary beside the overflow case so a future change\ncannot reject the largest representable declared length unnoticed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
