    {
      "sha": "46f51ee6cc45efc546369eae1691b76dfddc5825",
      "subject": "fix(flutter): name a missing or non-file APK selection (#2727)",
      "body": "fix(flutter): name a missing or non-file APK selection (#2727)\n\n* fix(flutter): name a missing or non-file APK selection\n\nidentify_flutter_build and inspect_dart_aot reported a missing path or a\ndirectory as \"The APK could not be read as a package: <path>: ENOENT ...\",\nwhich blames the package bytes for a selection mistake. Report\n\"Selected APK does not exist\" for ENOENT/ENOTDIR and \"Selected APK is not\na regular file\" for a non-regular selection, matching the SQLite\ninspector's wording. The issue path and invalid_format reason are\nunchanged; package format failures keep their existing message.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(filesystem): classify unopenable non-regular selections at admission\n\nA Unix socket cannot be opened at all: open() fails with ENXIO on Linux\nand EOPNOTSUPP on macOS (surfaced by libuv as \"Unknown system error\n-102\") before openRegularFile can stat the descriptor, so such a\nselection escaped NonRegularFileReadError and the Flutter provider still\nblamed the package bytes.\n\nWhen open fails, classify the path by its own metadata (lstat when\nsymlinks are rejected, stat otherwise): an existing non-regular file\nbecomes NonRegularFileReadError. Missing paths, permission failures,\nregular files, and the O_NOFOLLOW ELOOP rejection keep their original\nerrors. The Flutter selection test now covers a real Unix socket.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(filesystem): reclassify only unopenable file-type errors at admission\n\nChecking the path's metadata after any open failure turned EACCES on an\nunreadable directory into NonRegularFileReadError, so callers reported\ninvalid input instead of access_denied. Reclassify only errors that mean\nthe file type cannot be opened (ENXIO, EOPNOTSUPP, ENOTSUP, matched by\nerrno because libuv has no name for macOS EOPNOTSUPP 102); permission,\nsymlink-rejection and resource failures keep their original errors.\n\nRun the Unix socket selection check in its own test, skipped on Windows\nwhere listen() takes named pipes, and keep the missing-path and\ndirectory checks cross-platform.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(filesystem): keep cancellation that arrives during the non-regular probe\n\nA caller abort while the post-open metadata probe ran was replaced by\nNonRegularFileReadError, so callers such as parseBinaryTarget reported an\ninput-format error instead of cancellation. Recheck the signal before\nsubstituting the non-regular classification.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
