      "sha": "96d1f0f3fbc1a36664c62b66d7de8cc2f8837f52",
      "subject": "fix(cli): refuse scenario steps on passive native UI observation (#2712)",
      "body": "fix(cli): refuse scenario steps on passive native UI observation (#2712)\n\nobserve-native-ui and capture-native-ui-scenario were registered in one\nloop with a shared option schema and description. The passive command\ntherefore advertised `--steps` (\"Observe or run a scenario\"), accepted\nany value, and then dispatched observe_native_ui without it, so a\ncaller who selected the wrong command never learned that no scenario ran.\n\nRegister each command against its own contract. Observation declares\nonly the passive scope options, so `--steps` is rejected as an unknown\nflag; the scenario command keeps its JSON step decoding and validation.\nEach command now has its own description.\n\nFixes #2674\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
