      "sha": "ae9a7f34e17850eda3419102c4ddc24995653c64",
      "subject": "fix(process): report no remaining time after a provider deadline fires (#2720)",
      "body": "fix(process): report no remaining time after a provider deadline fires (#2720)\n\nNode timers can fire while performance.now() is still a fraction of a\nmillisecond short of the monotonic deadline. ProviderStartupDeadline then\nreported interruption \"timeout\" and an aborted signal while remainingMs()\nreturned ceil(0.x) = 1, so polling loops guarded by remainingMs() > 0\n(Hopper and Ghidra startup) could run past an elapsed deadline, and the\nreal-timer test \"aborts a bounded wait when its real monotonic deadline\nexpires\" failed intermittently in CI (expected 1 to be 0).\n\nOnce the deadline's own timer has classified a timeout, report zero\nremaining time. A deterministic regression test fires the timer with the\nmonotonic clock 0.4 ms short of the deadline.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
