      "sha": "ce748be2f30d5086e62106ca7d7d0d7b26b8fd28",
      "subject": "fix(process): order interaction differences by their dispatch time (#2739)",
      "body": "fix(process): order interaction differences by their dispatch time (#2739)\n\n* fix(process): order interaction differences by their dispatch time\n\nfirst_divergence ranks candidate differences by the earliest recorded\ntime of the differing observations, but eventTime read only `at_ms`.\nInteraction events record their time as `dispatched_at_ms`\n(and `scheduled_at_ms`), so a changed interaction always ranked as\nuntimed. An interaction outcome that differed at 6 ms therefore lost to\na process sample that differed at 500 ms.\n\nGive each comparison dimension its recorded time field. Interactions use\nthe dispatch time, when their outcome was observed; the other\ndimensions keep `at_ms`. An earlier process difference still wins.\n\nFixes #2645\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(process): require ordered interaction dispatch times in captures\n\nComparison ranks a changed interaction by its dispatch time, while\nfirstCollectionDivergence returns the first differing interaction by\nsequence. The capture parser checked only that interaction sequences are\ncontiguous, so an imported capture whose dispatch times decrease could\nmake that first-by-sequence difference later than another differing\ninteraction.\n\nInteractions are dispatched in sequence and their times come from the\nmonotonic capture clock, so require non-decreasing dispatch times at\nparsing, as frames, rendered frames, process samples and filesystem\ncheckpoints already require for their timestamps.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
