      "sha": "5996d8160f2429965b30070d04b26aba472af1db",
      "subject": "fix(native): bound captured output carried by native command failures (#2764)",
      "body": "fix(native): bound captured output carried by native command failures (#2764)\n\n* fix(native): bound captured output carried by native command failures\n\nThe native command runner retains up to 64 MiB of output because\nsuccessful analysis needs it complete, and failureCapture copied all of\nit into the failure. An inspect_plist whose plutil output exceeded the\nbudget therefore returned a 67 MB resource_constraint error whose\ndetails.captured_output.stdout repeated the whole retained output.\n\nKeep a 64 KiB UTF-8-safe excerpt per stream in failure diagnostics,\nmark them truncated, and keep the observed stdout/stderr byte totals.\nSuccessful captures are unchanged.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(native): bound codesign failures and cover excerpt cuts\n\ntranslateCodeSignExitFailure wrapped an accepted nonzero codesign capture\ninto a NativeCommandFailure by copying both complete streams, so\ninspect_signature failures still bypassed the diagnostic bound. Route it\nthrough the shared failureCapture builder; accepted output stays\ncomplete until the provider decides it is a failure.\n\nAdd a focused runner test for an ordinary nonzero exit with stdout and\nstderr just above the excerpt size and a two-byte character straddling\nthe cut, and a provider test for the codesign path.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(native): build excerpt test output inside the child process\n\nThe output strings embedded in one node -e argument totalled about 133\nKB, above Linux's 128 KiB per-argument limit, so spawn failed with E2BIG\non the CI runner. Generate the repeated output in the child instead.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
