      "sha": "fd65e278be4d802a06bbe176d997aaac0c4c9884",
      "subject": "fix(setup): resolve the configuration MSIX Claude Desktop reads (#2426)",
      "body": "fix(setup): resolve the configuration MSIX Claude Desktop reads (#2426)\n\n* fix(setup): resolve the configuration MSIX Claude Desktop reads\n\nOn Windows, setup, doctor and uninstall always used\n%APPDATA%\\Claude\\claude_desktop_config.json. The MSIX build of Claude\nDesktop (package family Claude_pzs8sxrjxfjjc) virtualizes AppData writes\nand reads its package-private copy under\n%LOCALAPPDATA%\\Packages\\<family>\\LocalCache\\Roaming\\Claude once it exists.\nSetup from an ordinary process therefore wrote a file the app never reads,\nand doctor reported that file healthy.\n\nResolve the Claude Desktop location once, in supportedClients(): the\nprivate copy when it exists, else the AppData file the package still\nreads, else a new private copy. An unrecognized Claude_* publisher or\nunreadable package storage is reported instead of falling back to AppData.\n\nCompare one of the package's private files with its AppData path through\nrealpath.native to learn whether the running package started this\nprocess. From that redirected view, or when no file can be compared,\nsetup and uninstall refuse to change Claude Desktop's configuration,\nbecause the running app rewrites it from memory. From a redirected view\nthey also refuse writes under %APPDATA% and %LOCALAPPDATA% for other\nclients and skills, which would land in the package's private storage.\n\nSetup refuses to register a launcher stored in any MSIX package's\nprivate storage, discloses which file the package reads, and tells the\nuser to quit Claude Desktop fully on every platform. Configuration fails\nwith target_changed if the package switched to its private copy after\nthe plan was shown. Uninstall removes REA from both files.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(setup): record the verified MSIX Claude Desktop registration\n\nOn the Windows 11 host with the MSIX build 2.31226.1.0, setup from an\nordinary terminal with the app quit wrote the package-private copy. After\nthe app restarted, the entry persisted, doctor reported it aligned, and\nClaude Desktop's MCP log showed REA starting and answering tools/list.\nUninstall against the real app remains unverified.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* style(setup): format MSIX review corrections\n\n* fix(setup): carry the admitted legacy path through uninstall removal\n\nclientRegistrationRemoval returned a removeLegacy boolean, and removeClient\nrecomputed the legacy path separately, so TypeScript could not prove the\npath existed when removeLegacy was true and `tsc --noEmit` failed in\nUninstall.ts. The decision now returns the admitted legacy path itself;\npreflight and removal consume that one value.\n\nThe alias regression matched new-destination children with a \"/\"\nseparator while building paths with path.join, so it failed on Windows.\nIt now uses path.sep.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(setup): split MSIX Claude Desktop lifecycle cases under the function length limit\n\nThe uninstall cases pushed the registration lifecycle describe past the 150-line lint limit. Group them separately, with the AppData registration case kept among the registration cases.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: morluto <76467478+morluto@users.noreply.github.com>",
