      "sha": "e3a012d6c98c60f3254e41e8b7d9c9f66e7cbe17",
      "subject": "fix(flutter): reject ambiguous ELF mappings and bound note reads (#2334)",
      "body": "fix(flutter): reject ambiguous ELF mappings and bound note reads (#2334)\n\n* fix(flutter): reject ambiguous mappings and bound ELF notes\n\nResolve PT_LOAD interpretations once for symbols and dynamic tables, including partial overlaps. Preserve equivalent mappings and leave conflicting or invalid alternate definitions unresolved.\n\nBound distinct nonempty ELF note ranges before retention and reads, deduplicate shared ranges, preserve observed build-ID candidates and report partial coverage on exhaustion. Correct shared verifier workspace ownership and structured Windows path assertions.\n\nAddresses the two post-merge review findings on PR #1582. Validation: 147 focused cases across Linux, macOS Sonoma 14.8.9 and non-administrator Windows 11 build 26300.9457; real Gallery CLI/MCP checks on all three hosts; six compiler-produced ELF32/ELF64 hash-layout cases; static, docs, discovery and duplication checks. Full string-pool projections remain explicitly bounded.\n\n* test(flutter): parse complete facts through named result schemas\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: me <me@medz.org>\nCo-authored-by: morluto <76467478+morluto@users.noreply.github.com>",
