      "sha": "5278835b534a9787a680f94ad2182c314f24c1e9",
      "subject": "fix(flutter): find snapshot headers that a read chunk boundary splits (#2804)",
      "body": "fix(flutter): find snapshot headers that a read chunk boundary splits (#2804)\n\n* fix(flutter): find snapshot headers that a read chunk boundary splits\n\nWithin one chunk the snapshot hash scanner resumes four bytes after each\nmagic, but across chunks it resumed after the whole 52-byte record and\ndropped the carried bytes. A magic starting 49-51 bytes after a rejected\n(non-hex) record was therefore lost when its four bytes straddled a read\nboundary, so the result depended on chunking and a conflicting hash could\nbe omitted while coverage stayed complete. Resume after the magic in both\ncases.\n\n* refactor(flutter): drop the snapshot scanner cursor the fix superseded\n\nAfter a complete record the carried tail is shorter than a magic, and a\npending magic has not been processed, so every push can rescan its carried\nbytes from the start without counting a record twice. Remove the absolute\ncursor and base offset, and cover sections 49-51 bytes after a rejected\nrecord with two-chunk and byte-at-a-time feeds.",
