      "sha": "21aa877e5ae3164cfbfab6f6db27967995ebc8c3",
      "subject": "fix(process): honor startup deadlines and add a CI audit skill (#2692)",
      "body": "fix(process): honor startup deadlines and add a CI audit skill (#2692)\n\n* docs(skills): add CI and test correctness auditing\n\nCo-authored-by: Kaoru0822 <208281322+kaoru0822-kitauji@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix(process): report no remaining time after a provider deadline fires\n\nNode timers can fire while performance.now() is still a fraction of a\nmillisecond short of the monotonic deadline. ProviderStartupDeadline then\nreported interruption \"timeout\" and an aborted signal while remainingMs()\nreturned ceil(0.x) = 1, so polling loops guarded by remainingMs() > 0\n(Hopper and Ghidra startup) could run past an elapsed deadline, and the\nreal-timer test \"aborts a bounded wait when its real monotonic deadline\nexpires\" failed intermittently in CI (expected 1 to be 0).\n\nOnce the deadline's own timer has classified a timeout, report zero\nremaining time. A deterministic regression test fires the timer with the\nmonotonic clock 0.4 ms short of the deadline.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(process): retain the monotonic startup deadline budget\n\nRecheck the absolute monotonic deadline when an early timer fires, and keep\npolling waits pending until their own target or the shared deadline arrives.\nPreserve caller cancellation, disposal and the unchanged real-timer assertion.\nThis replaces the earlier remainingMs workaround: an early callback must not\nclassify an unexpired deadline as a timeout.\n\nAdapt the production fix and regression cases from nosmile99 PR #2793 at\n546001693636f13700d86c6e93b6086abba2b7d6, including the independently reported\nboth-timers-early reproduction. Preserve the prior contributor's commit.\n\nFixes #2760\n\nCo-authored-by: nosmile99 <147114285+nosmile99@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Kaoru0822 <208281322+kaoru0822-kitauji@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* style(tests): format the Java class fixture signature\n\nThe captured main baseline has an unformatted helper signature. Apply the\nrepository formatter so the required style gate can run to completion.\n\nCo-authored-by: Kaoru0822 <208281322+kaoru0822-kitauji@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* test(ghidra): group expanded suites by their contracts\n\nSplit result-envelope and completeness checks, and Windows invocation and\nruntime checks, into named describe groups within the existing lint limit.\nPreserve every test, fixture, assertion and platform prerequisite.\n\nCo-authored-by: Kaoru0822 <208281322+kaoru0822-kitauji@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Kaoru0822 <208281322+kaoru0822-kitauji@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: morluto <76467478+morluto@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: nosmile99 <147114285+nosmile99@users.noreply.github.com>",
