      "sha": "9b08c2b1cbbd74631738db1ddb326592682326e8",
      "subject": "fix(native/windows): share FILE_SHARE_DELETE so owned objects can be marked delete-pending (#2445)",
      "body": "fix(native/windows): share FILE_SHARE_DELETE so owned objects can be marked delete-pending (#2445)\n\n* fix(native/windows): share FILE_SHARE_DELETE so owned objects can be marked delete-pending\n\nThe Windows native authority self-test (`binding.call(\"inspect\", [])`) fails\nclosed on stock Windows x64 with a non-admin user:\n\n    Delete owned object by handle failed (Win32 5): Access is denied.\n\nReproduced deterministically (15/15 failures) on Windows 11 x64, Node 22.22.2,\nnon-elevated account. Because `inspect` is a hard gate, every provider-backed\noperation is rejected and the whole native authority is unusable.\n\nRoot cause: Windows requires that every handle currently open on an object\ngrants FILE_SHARE_DELETE before that object can be marked delete-pending via\nSetFileInformationByHandle(FileDispositionInfo).\n\n`createRelative()` creates the runtime object with FILE_SHARE_READ only, and the\nreturned handle is retained for the lifetime of the runtime\n(`Runtime::directory`). `closeRuntime()` later needs to mark that same object\ndelete-pending, but the retained handle never shared DELETE, so the transition\nis denied (Win32 5).\n\nThe child handles opened by `closeRuntime()` for recursive cleanup have the same\ndefect: they request DELETE access while sharing only FILE_SHARE_READ, so the\nsubsequent `dispose()` call on those very handles is denied too.\n\nFix: add FILE_SHARE_DELETE to both share masks, keeping FILE_SHARE_READ and\ndeliberately not adding FILE_SHARE_WRITE, so the existing write-exclusion\nbehaviour of the retained leases is preserved while the delete-pending\ntransition the cleanup path depends on becomes possible.\n\nVerified end-to-end after the change: `inspect` passes, the full runtime\nlifecycle (`runtime_create` / `runtime_mkdir` / `runtime_write` / `runtime_open`\n/ `runtime_close`) completes with no residual directories, and a real 925 MB\napplication analysis (4396 files) runs through all stages.\n\n* fix(windows): anchor private runtime cleanup to directory handles\n\n* test(windows): assert cleanup sharing failure by code\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: maodns <311719211+maodns@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: morluto <76467478+morluto@users.noreply.github.com>",
