    {
      "sha": "edd99398797051f8910e777bf5bf94aea5756f4a",
      "subject": "fix(browser): give the DevToolsActivePort wait one deadline owner (#2265)",
      "body": "fix(browser): give the DevToolsActivePort wait one deadline owner (#2265)\n\n* Single owner for the Chrome DevToolsActivePort startup deadline\n\nCold Chrome startup tolerance was spelled three ways for one wait: the helper\nfell back to 15,000 ms, the runtime fixture lifecycle passed a literal 60,000,\nand the real-browser verifier kept a local 60,000 constant. A per-caller literal\nquietly changes how long a lane tolerates a cold browser before it fails, and\nthe failure reported only elapsed_ms, so a reader could not see which ceiling\nwas hit.\n\nExport BROWSER_DEVTOOLS_STARTUP_TIMEOUT_MS as the owner, use it for the helper\nfallback and both call sites, and report startup_timeout_ms in\nBrowserStartupError. A source guard keeps callers from restating the number.\n\n* Pin the DevToolsActivePort deadline guard to the startup call argument\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: morluto <76467478+morluto@users.noreply.github.com>",
