    {
      "sha": "94072364c7f8410b0e86e72c912c2611572b278f",
      "subject": "fix(sqlite): keep triggers whose declaration spells the table in another case (#2807)",
      "body": "fix(sqlite): keep triggers whose declaration spells the table in another case (#2807)\n\n* fix(sqlite): keep triggers whose declaration spells the table in another case\n\nSQLite stores a trigger's target in sqlite_schema.tbl_name exactly as\nwritten in CREATE TRIGGER and resolves it by ASCII case folding, while an\nindex stores the table's own name. The selected_table scope filtered\ntbl_name with COLLATE BINARY, so a trigger declared ON users for table\nUsers was omitted while the schema still reported complete. Match\ndependents with COLLATE NOCASE, and report each trigger's table as the\nstored table or view name so the selected-table contract still holds.\n\n* fix(sqlite): refuse an inexact table before the case-folded schema scan\n\nWith the NOCASE expansion, a selection such as users for table Users\nexpanded the stored table's declarations before readRows reported the\nmissing exact name, so large trigger definitions could surface as an\noutput-limit failure instead of the selection error. Check the exact\ntable name against PRAGMA table_list first and share the selection\nfailure with readRows.\n\n* fix(sqlite): fold dependent names only for a row-selectable table\n\nAn exact view, virtual or possible shadow table passed the exact-name\nguard, so the NOCASE scan could still expand a differently cased trigger\npast the reply budget before readRows refused the selection. Fold case\nonly when the selection is an ordinary table that is not a possible\nshadow table, and keep the exact filter otherwise so every refused\nselection fails as it did before the case-folding change.\n\n* fix(sqlite): resolve trigger tables without folding unrelated names\n\nThe stored-name lookup case-folded every PRAGMA table_list name up front,\nso a selected-table inspection of a tiny table paid for large unrelated\nidentifiers. A selected-table scan only returns the selected table's\ndependents, so report the selected name directly; other scopes use an\nexact stored name when one matches and fold the stored names once, only\nwhen a trigger spells its target differently.\n\n* perf(sqlite): fold each table name once when matching shadow parents\n\nThe extracted shadow-parent helper folded the table name inside the find\ncallback, once per unresolved virtual table, and the selected table was\nchecked both before and during the schema scan. Fold the name once per\ncall as before, and reuse the selected table's result in the scan.",
