      "sha": "e13da084e7c5967b80632ae5ad8d3d37bcf57469",
      "subject": "fix(apple): exclude AppleDouble sidecars from IPA components (#2838)",
      "body": "fix(apple): exclude AppleDouble sidecars from IPA components (#2838)\n\n* fix(apple): exclude AppleDouble sidecars from IPA components\n\nIPA projection returned every inventoried component before the AppleDouble\nsidecar filter applied to directory, ZIP and DMG roots, so ._* and\n__MACOSX/ metadata appeared as native libraries and frameworks while the\nresult reported that sidecars are excluded. Apply the sidecar exclusion\nfirst for every root format; IPA still keeps non-sidecar components\noutside Payload/.\n\nFixes #2546\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(apple): exercise the __MACOSX exclusion with a non-dotfile name\n\nThe IPA fixture's __MACOSX entry also started with \"._\", so the AppleDouble\nfilename rule excluded it and a broken __MACOSX check would go unnoticed.\nUse a library name that only the __MACOSX rule excludes; the native\nlibrary assertion now fails if that rule regresses.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
