    {
      "sha": "7dcd23c005ac40ae2523861ae8806e29cb1d74ed",
      "subject": "fix(setup): separate host support and stop skill checks after drift (#2073)",
      "body": "fix(setup): separate host support and stop skill checks after drift (#2073)\n\n* fix(host): separate REA host support from Hopper installer targets\n\nLinuxDistribution.supported carried two meanings at once: that the host runs\nREA, and that the automated Hopper installer is tested on it. The doctor read\nthe first meaning from the second, so Debian-derived hosts such as Kali\nreported unsupported_host while their providers worked normally.\n\nRename the field to hopperSetupSupported, which only the Hopper installer and\nsetup planning consume, and derive host support from the package family\nthrough supportsReaHost(). Any distribution with a recognized apt, dnf, or\npacman family is now a REA host. The tested Hopper installer list is\nunchanged, so Debian and Kali keep falling back to configuring an existing\nprovider instead of downloading an untested package.\n\nVerified on Kali 2026.3 (Debian testing, x86_64): rea doctor reports a healthy\nenvironment with Ghidra 12.1.4, and analyze_function decompiles an x86_64 ELF\nthrough the MCP server. npm run check, npm run docs:check, and the application\nand Ghidra suites pass. No Hopper or IDA host workflow was exercised.\n\n* fix(setup): stop skill checks after first drift\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: morluto <76467478+morluto@users.noreply.github.com>",
