    {
      "sha": "af142f656cf448120ad66ebb545bc92e77fd2401",
      "subject": "fix(mcp): report references a provider truncated in trace_feature (#2348)",
      "body": "fix(mcp): report references a provider truncated in trace_feature (#2348)\n\n* test(mcp): expect trace_feature to report references the provider truncated\n\nA provider that reports a capped xrefs read makes the trace truncated with a residual unknown for that target. An explicit complete report and a provider that reports nothing leave the trace as before.\n\n* fix(mcp): report references a provider truncated in trace_feature\n\nExecutions gain an optional flag for a capped xrefs read, set by the IDA adapter from the upstream cap. trace_feature marks the trace truncated with a residual unknown for that target only when the provider reports a truncation; a provider that reports nothing keeps its previous result. The trace_feature workflow profile is revised so earlier results are not replayed.\n\n* refactor(ida): report reference truncation whenever the runner observed an xrefs cap\n\n* test(mcp): cover session forwarding, per-target state, native reports and failures of the trace coverage\n\n* test(mcp): format the session forwarding test\n\n* test(process): format processCaptureLifecycle.test.ts after the merge\n\n* test(ida): declare the alignment each synthetic universal slice offset satisfies\n\n* fix(process): report no remaining time after a provider deadline fires\n\nNode timers can fire while performance.now() is still a fraction of a\nmillisecond short of the monotonic deadline. ProviderStartupDeadline then\nreported interruption \"timeout\" and an aborted signal while remainingMs()\nreturned ceil(0.x) = 1, so polling loops guarded by remainingMs() > 0\n(Hopper and Ghidra startup) could run past an elapsed deadline, and the\nreal-timer test \"aborts a bounded wait when its real monotonic deadline\nexpires\" failed intermittently in CI (expected 1 to be 0).\n\nOnce the deadline's own timer has classified a timeout, report zero\nremaining time. A deterministic regression test fires the timer with the\nmonotonic clock 0.4 ms short of the deadline.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n(cherry picked from commit dfdaa0ca74cc84a45dcb186422a0f51aa61bc427)\n\n* fix(process): keep monotonic deadline ownership after merge\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: morluto <76467478+morluto@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Kaoru0822 <208281322+kaoru0822-kitauji@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
