    {
      "sha": "2a78763e2070d71818a44bd419df549e13ce203c",
      "subject": "feat(native): search analyzed memory for masked byte patterns (#2341)",
      "body": "feat(native): search analyzed memory for masked byte patterns (#2341)\n\n* feat(native): search analyzed memory for masked byte patterns\n\nThe diff adds search_bytes to the CLI, the shared MCP contract, Ghidra\ninventory, and the headless bridge, and advertises the same operation on\nHopper as unavailable until that provider is verified. Patterns are\nhexadecimal byte pairs with optional ?? wildcards and an optional\nequal-length bit mask; the TypeScript boundary and the bridge both\nrequire a nonempty pattern, equal lengths, and at least one constrained\nbit. Ghidra walks initialized blocks in address order within inclusive\nbounds, keeps overlapping matches inside a single block, and returns\neach hit with its segment, unique source file offset, and containing\nprocedure, continuing through a cursor bound to the target, profile,\npattern, mask, and bounds. Each page reports the inclusive ranges\nexamined and the skipped uninitialized blocks; cancellation returns a\ntyped error and discards the active Ghidra database.\naddress_to_file_offset now uses the same unique-offset helper, which\nrejects a mapping that is missing, ambiguous, or larger than a safe\ninteger.\n\n* fix(native): limit unbounded byte search to loaded memory\n\nWithout start or end, search_bytes walked every Ghidra block, including\nnon-loaded file parts such as .symtab and overlay blocks, which the docs\ncall out of scope. Unbounded searches now skip those blocks and list them\nin searched.skipped_not_loaded; explicit bounds in their address space\nstill search them. Document that a match must end at or before end.\n\n* fix(native): preserve implicit address spaces in range consumers\n\n* fix(native): reject present malformed byte search state\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Matt Van Horn <455140+mvanhorn@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: morluto <76467478+morluto@users.noreply.github.com>",
