    {
      "sha": "af782dd5f56463fcd2a6a0af918569d70696551f",
      "subject": "fix(setup): treat empty DSH_HOME as unset (#2686)",
      "body": "fix(setup): treat empty DSH_HOME as unset (#2686)\n\n* fix(setup): treat empty DSH_HOME as unset (#2666)\n\nThe released `@deepseek-ai/dsh-home-paths` package explicitly treats an\nempty or whitespace-only `DSH_HOME` as unset and selects the default\nHarness home patch. `dshHomeDirectory` previously used nullish coalescing\n(`env.DSH_HOME ?? join(home, \".dsh\")`), so an empty override flowed\nstraight through `join(..., \"cordis.patch.yml\")` and produced a\ncwd-relative `cordis.patch.yml` outside the client-selected home.\n\nTreat empty and whitespace-only overrides as unset, matching the sibling\nOpenCode override resolver and the released DSH resolver. The patch now\nlands at `$DSH_HOME/cordis.patch.yml` for explicit overrides, the default\n`~/.dsh/cordis.patch.yml` for empty/unset, and trimmed whitespace for\npadded overrides.\n\nAdds `src/application/SupportedClients.test.ts` covering the empty,\nwhitespace-only, unset, padded, and explicit cases via the public\n`supportedClients(...)` entrypoint. Fixes #2666.\n\n* test(setup): remove superseded DSH path unit coverage\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: morluto <76467478+morluto@users.noreply.github.com>",
      "parents": ["d86d29c41108cc5d784e324c6cbe50beac70a543"],
