      "sha": "d4f0c5e664e26fe7ed1566dcc4b85ea9b57d52da",
      "subject": "fix(cli): start on Windows when USERPROFILE is empty (#2345)",
      "body": "fix(cli): start on Windows when USERPROFILE is empty (#2345)\n\n* fix(cli): start on Windows when USERPROFILE is empty\n\nNode's Windows home lookup throws ERR_SYSTEM_ERROR (uv_os_homedir ENOENT)\nfor an empty USERPROFILE instead of consulting the account profile. Incur\nresolves the home while it is imported, so every command, including\n`rea --version`, stopped with a raw stack trace before REA ran.\n\nTreat the empty selection as unset in the launcher, before any runtime\nimport, and cover startup with a compiled-CLI regression.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(process): report no remaining time after a provider deadline fires\n\nNode timers can fire while performance.now() is still a fraction of a\nmillisecond short of the monotonic deadline. ProviderStartupDeadline then\nreported interruption \"timeout\" and an aborted signal while remainingMs()\nreturned ceil(0.x) = 1, so polling loops guarded by remainingMs() > 0\n(Hopper and Ghidra startup) could run past an elapsed deadline, and the\nreal-timer test \"aborts a bounded wait when its real monotonic deadline\nexpires\" failed intermittently in CI (expected 1 to be 0).\n\nOnce the deadline's own timer has classified a timeout, report zero\nremaining time. A deterministic regression test fires the timer with the\nmonotonic clock 0.4 ms short of the deadline.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: morluto <76467478+morluto@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Kaoru0822 <208281322+kaoru0822-kitauji@users.noreply.github.com>",
