      "sha": "62c8b3da1b00260a5ef97d088737dafa0a7ea542",
      "subject": "feat(browser): attach passive tools to browsers without HTTP discovery (#2346)",
      "body": "feat(browser): attach passive tools to browsers without HTTP discovery (#2346)\n\n* feat(browser): attach passive tools to browsers without HTTP discovery\n\nAccept a literal loopback browser WebSocket,\nws://127.0.0.1:PORT/devtools/browser/ID, as the cdp_endpoint of the six\npassive browser tools. Discovery then reads Browser.getVersion and\nTarget.getTargets over that socket, and the target session adopts the\nsame socket, so a browser that asks for consent per connection prompts\nonce per call.\n\nThe socket identifier gates access, so Evidence records the endpoint as\nws://127.0.0.1:PORT/devtools/browser/[REDACTED], and runtime\nreconciliation accepts that recorded form. HTTP endpoints and their\nEvidence are unchanged. Electron, web runtime, scenario and Inspector\nendpoints stay HTTP-only.\n\nRefs #2288\n\n* test(browser): match browser-socket captures against HTTP discovery\n\nCheck in the real Chrome lane that DevToolsActivePort names the same\nbrowser socket as /json/version, and that inspecting the selected page\nthrough that socket leaves DOM structure and scripts unchanged compared\nwith an inspection through HTTP discovery.\n\nRefs #2288\n\n* fix(browser): bound browser-socket handshake and report discovery timeouts\n\nRun the browser-socket WebSocket handshake and both discovery commands\nunder one discovery deadline, so a port that accepts the connection but\nnever completes the upgrade times out instead of waiting forever.\n\nReport a reached deadline as a timeout without carrying the internal\nabort as its cause, so CLI and MCP project provider_timeout rather than\ncancelled. Caller cancellation is still reported as cancelled.\n\nRefs #2288",
      "parents": ["0c9ee56c2f819d122f12cb5872c5db76cfee1169"],
