    {
      "sha": "1d5f95dc4aff3ffadd06e922128606ea0fb669cc",
      "subject": "fix(native): parse renamed dyld_info re-exports (#2364)",
      "body": "fix(native): parse renamed dyld_info re-exports (#2364)\n\n* fix(native): parse renamed dyld_info re-exports\n\ndyld_info prints a re-export whose name differs from the source library's\nsymbol as `[re-export] _foo_renamed (_foo from libfoo)`. The export parser\nonly accepted `(from libfoo)`, so inspect_macho reported a nonexistent\nexport named `_foo_renamed (_foo from libfoo)` with no source, and the nm\nrow for `_foo_renamed` survived the name-based merge as a second export\nwith reexport null.\n\nAccept the optional source symbol, trying the plain `(from lib)` form\nfirst so a library name containing ` from ` keeps its text. The row now\nreports `_foo_renamed` re-exported from libfoo and replaces the nm\nduplicate. The export schema has no field for the source symbol name, so\nexports coverage records a limitation when a renamed re-export is present.\nThe golden fixture is a dyld_info capture of a synthetic dylib linked with\n-Wl,-alias,_foo,_foo_renamed.\n\n* fix(native): split dyld re-export suffix without nested quantifiers\n\nReplace the (?:(.+?)\\s+)??from lazy-optional group with a linear string\nscan so malformed lines cannot backtrack and a library path containing\n\" from \" still keeps its whole text via the plain-form-first check.\n\n* test(native): cover nested re-export library names\n\n* fix(native): retain reexports missing from nm inventory\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: morluto <76467478+morluto@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: morluto <17176810+morluto@users.noreply.github.com>",
