      "sha": "090b454350591f58d3349fa992109d55414f5294",
      "subject": "fix(javascript-semantics): keep emitted data out of dispatch listener fields (#2952)",
      "body": "fix(javascript-semantics): keep emitted data out of dispatch listener fields (#2952)\n\n* fix(javascript-semantics): keep emitted data out of dispatch listener fields\n\nThe EventEmitter operation collector read argument position 1 as the\nlistener for every event method, so a dispatch such as\nbus.emit(\"ready\", data) reported the data binding and its range as the\nlistener. Only registration and removal name a listener there; emit\npasses its remaining arguments to listeners that already exist. Read the\nlistener argument only for register and remove operations.\n\nFixes #2574\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(javascript-semantics): read listener arguments only for listener-taking methods\n\nremoveAllListeners accepts only an optional event name, so gating the\nlistener argument on operation kind still reported an ignored second\nargument as a listener. Gate on the methods whose argument position 1\nnames a listener instead: the registration methods, off, and\nremoveListener.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
