      "sha": "388b907c923133096a3387272367cbfb04ff1c04",
      "subject": "perf(javascript): defer ambiguity expansion in version comparisons (#2962)",
      "body": "perf(javascript): defer ambiguity expansion in version comparisons (#2962)\n\nperf(javascript): avoid quadratic temporary matching state\n\nRepeated source groups can allocate candidates that later identity matches\ndiscard. Retain the original ambiguous groups until all tiers finish, expand\nonly unmatched survivors, and append to locally owned key buckets in place.\n\nConstraint: Preserve matching priority, full ambiguity, and public output.\nDirective: Do not re-match residual groups that become unique after later tiers.\nTested: 59 relevant tests, npm run check, and test discovery on current main.\nTested: CLI benchmarks and full-suite failure comparison on the recorded base.\nNot-tested: Full suite on the updated main; native Linux and Windows workflows.",
