      "sha": "97268f40ea21b5f2d24b08c0c068a7ccf41459d4",
      "subject": "fix(dotnet): name the truncated instruction when an operand leaves the method body (#2704)",
      "body": "fix(dotnet): name the truncated instruction when an operand leaves the method body (#2704)\n\n* fix(dotnet): name the truncated instruction when an operand leaves the method body\n\nThe extent guard ran after the operand read, so a truncated operand threw a raw Buffer RangeError that replaced the intended diagnostic with the runtime message and lost the instruction identity.\n\nBound the operand extent before reading its value and carry the width beside each fixed reader so the two facts cannot drift.\n\nFixes #2677\n\n* test(dotnet): consolidate truncated operand coverage\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: morluto <76467478+morluto@users.noreply.github.com>",
