    {
      "sha": "729ca2ab6ae0644b5a466534f9287961bf7152db",
      "subject": "fix(ghidra): report unapplied PE CodeView PDB limitation (#2283)",
      "body": "fix(ghidra): report unapplied PE CodeView PDB limitation (#2283)\n\n* fix(ghidra): report unapplied PE CodeView PDB limitation (#2259)\n\nWhen Ghidra analyzes a PE target that references companion debug symbols\nin its CodeView (IMAGE_DEBUG_TYPE_CODEVIEW / RSDS or NB10) debug directory,\nGhidra's headless analyzer cannot automatically locate or apply the companion\nPDB from isolated runtime directories without companion admission. Procedure\nnames remain analysis-generated (FUN_<address>).\n\nParse CodeView debug metadata (RSDS GUID/age and NB10 age) during PE target\nresolution, and report an Evidence limitation informing callers and agents\nthat referenced debug symbols were not applied and procedure names are\nanalysis-generated.\n\nFixes #2259\n\n* test(pe): group CodeView header coverage separately\n\n* fix(ghidra): avoid contradictory PDB limitations\n\n* fix(android): make DEX descriptor pattern portable\n\n* fix(ci): isolate Linux Hopper process fixture inventory\n\n* fix(comparison): recheck historical calls-only changes (#2223)\n\n* fix(comparison): preserve incomplete function call evidence\n\nKeep missing, unknown, partial and unresolved call relationships unknown in function comparisons and reconstruction claims. Aggregate IDA caller and callee coverage without overwriting uncertainty.\n\nValidate with 144 focused tests, typecheck/lint, docs checks and test discovery. Real providers were not verified; the full headless IDA session suite requires unavailable Windows native controls.\n\n* fix(comparison): recheck historical calls-only changes\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: morluto <76467478+morluto@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* style: format identity comparison and IDA runner\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: morluto <76467478+morluto@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Lucien <164857476+dakjdakd@users.noreply.github.com>",
