    {
      "sha": "42667fc1a03ffae7ffea57a611f52162ea223a7c",
      "subject": "fix(wasm): report WABT output past its budget as a resource constraint (#2117)",
      "body": "fix(wasm): report WABT output past its budget as a resource constraint (#2117)\n\n* fix(wasm): report WABT output past its budget as a resource constraint\n\nA module whose WAT exceeds the 32 MiB output budget failed as\nunreadable_output, advised `rea doctor`, and echoed the full 32 MiB\ntruncated WAT prefix in details.captured_output. Map the owned-command\noutput-limit outcome during inspection to AnalysisResourceConstraintError\nnaming the budget, as the apktool and native macOS providers do, with a\nremediation that says the fixed budget will not change on retry.\n\nCaptured output for an output-limit failure keeps only the first 4,096\ncharacters of each stream, including on the cleanup-failure path. An\noversized --version probe keeps its configuration-phase mapping.\n\n* fix(wasm): keep observed sizes and whole code points in output-limit excerpts\n\nCut each stream's output-limit excerpt with boundedUtf8Text at 4,096\nUTF-8 bytes, so an astral character at the cut no longer leaves a lone\nsurrogate. Mark the output truncated when either excerpt was cut, and\nreport each stream's observed byte count.\n\nWord the remediation as a fact about the fixed budget. A flood of\ndiagnostics from any WABT tool reaches this path, so it no longer says\nthe module is too large.\n\nReplace the 32 MiB end-to-end test with a launcher seam that raises a\nsmall output-limit failure.\n\n* fix(wasm): match sibling captured-output fields for WABT output limits\n\nReport retained byte counts in stdout_bytes and stderr_bytes, as apktool\nand the firmware command do, and record exit_code and signal. Mark the\nexcerpt truncated outright, since the command raises output-limit only\nafter retention was truncated.\n\nWhen cleanup also fails, record the output limit and its budget as the\nprevious error instead of the generic command message. Document that\nthe two streams share the budget, so the excerpt holds up to 4,096 of\nthe bytes each stream retained.\n\n* docs(wasm): scope the output-budget error to inspection commands\n\n* docs(wasm): distinguish reported warm costs from unmeasured gaps\n\n* docs(wasm): clarify the scope of reported warm measurements\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: morluto <76467478+morluto@users.noreply.github.com>",
