      "sha": "64041e3072e968002e2085445217ccde1f36e5d7",
      "subject": "fix(session): reject an unknown configured provider before unbound routing (#2976)",
      "body": "fix(session): reject an unknown configured provider before unbound routing (#2976)\n\nWhen every registered deep provider rejected a target, select() returned\nan intentionally unbound success for any concrete environment selector,\nincluding one that names no registered provider. A misconfigured\nREA_ANALYSIS_PROVIDER therefore opened the target unbound, and the later\ndeep-operation diagnostic blamed target support instead of the unknown\nconfiguration. The same identifier requested explicitly already failed\nwith unknown_provider.\n\nTake the unbound shortcut only for a registered environment preference.\nAn unknown configured identifier now reaches concrete selection and fails\nwith unknown_provider, matching the explicit request. Registered\npreferences and auto still leave artifact-only targets unbound.\n\nFixes #2592",
