      "sha": "0c6c571a01f0c35aa56a0189fb8b8adfd0012c61",
      "subject": "perf(javascript): reuse semantic member-mutation lookups (#2941)",
      "body": "perf(javascript): reuse semantic member-mutation lookups (#2941)\n\nThe semantic member-mutation collector revisits the same nodes while it closes\nalias chains, and each visit re-derived results that cannot change within the\nphase:\n\n- resolveSemanticBindingState re-walked the scope chain for the same identifier\n  node. Definition collection completes before this phase, and addBinding is\n  reachable only from it, so a scope's bindings no longer change.\n- directInitializerPosition, directMutationPosition and\n  referenceInitializerPosition are pure functions of a node and the analysis\n  parent map, but were recomputed for every mutation and initializer.\n- markValue re-encoded the same capture tuple with JSON.stringify and built a\n  fresh long key for every Set/Map lookup, so each lookup re-hashed the whole\n  key. The capture key is now cached per binding, origin and owner, and the\n  lifetime key is derived from it.\n\nOn pdfjs-dist 5.3.93 wasm/openjpeg_nowasm_fallback.js (462316 bytes, sha256\n53c228428a8861035a34738966af263fc9d4cee6df25a0ad942af947469a0bd9) the semantic\nphase takes 177.8 s instead of 272.9 s in-process, with a byte-identical\nsemantic IR. With --max-heap-mb 3072 and the default heap the base revision\nexhausts the worker; with the default 300 s per-source deadline raised, the\ncompleted CLI run takes 240.6 s instead of 396.7 s and its output is identical\napart from volatile identifiers.\n\nRefs #2498\n\nCo-authored-by: gongfpp <22683417+gongfpp@users.noreply.github.com>",
