      "sha": "20b802f165b572cc067d14d3011563cad4508285",
      "subject": "fix(analysis-view): bound limitations and unknowns per view (#2794)",
      "body": "fix(analysis-view): bound limitations and unknowns per view (#2794)\n\n* fix(analysis-view): bound limitations and unknowns per view\n\nViews of a JavaScript application or binary layout copied every parent\nlimitation into both limitations and unknowns, so a parent with tens of\nthousands of limitations produced views as large as the complete record\nand exceeded the MCP response budget even for a one-item page. Each view\nnow carries at most 64 distinct messages per field plus one line naming\nthe omitted count and the parent Evidence that retains the full list.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(analysis-view): assert exact bounded message notices\n\nSource inspection and targeted formatting only. Tests, builds, lint, typechecks and provider workloads were not run at the user's explicit request.\n\n* fix(analysis-view): preserve coverage facts in bounded messages\n\nReserve JavaScript completeness and unknown-count facts before bulk limitations. Direct omission recovery to the source parent without assuming session retention. Preserve exact threshold assertions and add unrun exhausted-page/item and unretained-inline MCP regressions. Source inspection and targeted formatting only; tests/checks/builds/provider workloads/CI reruns skipped by explicit user request.\n\n* fix(analysis-view): bound repeated message serialization bytes\n\n* fix(analysis-view): let byte budget bound messages\n\n* test(analysis-view): exercise byte-based message omissions\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: morluto <76467478+morluto@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>",
