      "body": "fix(reverse): reconcile cleanup ownership and mutation diagnostics (#2799)\n\n* feat(process): add owned debugger shutdown lifecycle\n\n* feat(reverse): add local inspection commands\n\n* feat(gdb): add persistent debugger integration\n\n* feat(cutter): add Cutter bridge integration\n\n* test(reverse): enforce complete integration coverage\n\n* fix(process): preserve debugger shutdown ownership\n\n* fix(reverse): retain evidence across interrupted commands\n\n* fix(gdb): honor captured provider environment\n\n* test(process): cover debugger shutdown retries\n\n* fix(reverse): retain evidence for interrupted providers\n\n* test(process): cover debugger shutdown retries\n\n* fix(reverse): retain evidence for interrupted providers\n\n* fix(server): snapshot provider environment at creation\n\n* fix(reverse): close review gaps with complete coverage\n\n* fix(reverse): address inspection review findings\n\n* fix(gdb): bound sessions and retain cleanup ownership\n\n* fix(ci): require reverse-tools quality lane\n\n* fix(process): unref inherited debugger output pipes\n\n* fix(reverse): address remaining PR 1960 findings\n\n* fix(gdb): address remaining PR 1961 findings\n\n* fix(reverse): account for unrestricted provider execution\n\n* fix(process): retain debugger ownership until safe shutdown\n\n* fix(process): preserve replacement debugger sessions\n\n* fix(reverse): preserve admission and output provenance\n\n* fix(process): retain exited debugger until output settles\n\n* fix(mcp): bound provider admission and debugger cleanup\n\n* fix(reverse): preserve failure provenance and classify E2BIG\n\n* fix(gdb): preserve startup cleanup and detach safety\n\n* fix(process): retain debugger ownership after detach failure\n\n* fix(reverse): preserve mutation and failure provenance\n\n* fix(gdb): address debugger review findings\n\n* fix(reverse): rebind sessions after external mutation\n\n* fix(process): cap debugger output after exit\n\n* fix(gdb): protect one-shot detach verification\n\n* feat(debugger): add reverse tool coverage gate\n\n* test(debugger): cover integrated failure paths\n\n* fix(gdb): bound and preserve session observations\n\n* fix(gdb): address review regressions\n\n* style: format merged integration files\n\n* fix(reverse): preserve session and output evidence\n\n* refactor(gdb): share repeated test and partial result setup\n\n* fix(gdb): invalidate TTY proof for Python aliases\n\n* fix(reverse): retain failure output byte counts\n\n* test(process): synchronize late debugger output\n\n* fix(gdb): invalidate TTY proof for wrapped commands\n\n* fix(gdb): recognize wit command abbreviation\n\n* test(reverse): wait for cancelled descendant readiness\n\n* test(reverse): bound descendant cancellation cleanup\n\n* style(reverse): format integration tests and adapters\n\n* style: format reverse engineering integration files\n\n* test(reverse): remove duplicate environment harness\n\n* test(gdb): share session startup assertions\n\n* fix(gdb): invalidate output proof for command abbreviations\n\n* test(reverse): share composition edge case scenarios\n\n* fix(ci): recognize verification and mutation tool entries\n\n* test(rizin): cover successful fake inferior detach\n\n* test(cli): align full output failure envelope\n\n* test(cli): isolate reverse command lifecycle service\n\n* test(process): share debugger output fixture setup\n\n* fix(binary): preserve high-bit Windows signature bytes\n\n* style(binary): format Windows signature parser\n\n* test(mcp): preserve call coverage in unchanged comparison\n\n* fix(ci): include reverse tools Vitest configs in lint cache\n\n* fix(mcp): preserve target content on delivery errors\n\n* ci: align duplication ceiling with expanded suite\n\n* test(reverse): allow signal admission mutants\n\n* fix(reverse): bound retained cleanup failures to process owners\n\n* fix(test): replace drifting mutation ranges with owned selectors\n\n* fix(reverse): admit persistent commands and retain cleanup ownership\n\n* fix(cutter): recover timed-out commands from exact receipts\n\n* fix(cutter): reject unsupported bridge request kinds\n\n* fix(ci): repair client format and shared verification fixtures\n\n* fix(native): preserve debugger cleanup ownership and bridge authentication\n\n* test(native): retain diagnostics without perfect coverage requirements\n\n* chore(licenses): refresh locked dependency inventory and notices\n\n* fix(test): exclude transient command locks from mutation sandboxes\n\n* fix(gdb): admit only platforms with safe detach verification\n\n* fix(cutter): retain bounded completion receipts until acknowledgement\n\n* fix(cutter): acknowledge commands rejected before UI dispatch\n\n* test(reverse): fail cancellation checks before fixture teardown\n\n* test(gdb): clean up the retained broken-stdin fixture owner\n\n* docs(test): clarify focused provider verification scope\n\n* fix(rizin): retain close cleanup failures\n\n* fix(gdb): wait for inferior stop and bound MI buffering\n\n* fix(cutter): retain failed receipt acknowledgements\n\n* fix(rizin): return retained session identity on rebind failure\n\n* fix(gdb): preserve startup cancellation and lossy status\n\n* fix(rizin): retain launch provenance and assemble frames once\n\n* fix(cutter): recover receipts across callers and bound discovery\n\n* docs: describe debugger evidence and bridge recovery\n\n* fix(process): keep cleanup incomplete while writers remain\n\nStopping a debugger no longer reports success when inherited output\nstreams stay open, so BinarySession cannot reopen a binary a child is\nstill changing. Concurrent Cutter cleanup retries share one receipt\nacknowledgement instead of treating a consumed receipt as failure.\n\n* fix(debuggers): recover cleanup with captured process identities\n\n* fix(analysis): retire sessions after unrestricted commands\n\n* fix(cli): preserve completed evidence after cleanup recovery\n\n* fix(cutter): bound frame collection and coalesce cleanup\n\n* fix(windows): resolve selected provider paths absolutely\n\n* fix(gdb): report decoding loss in failed startup evidence\n\n* fix(rizin): scope decoding loss to collected command frames\n\n* test(mcp): cover snapshot retirement in reverse tools CI\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Daniel Gonçalves Araujo <47118053+dandgabr@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: REA Maintainers <noreply@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: OpenAI Codex <codex@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>",
