    {
      "sha": "aa6f74af04c06d3d09ef69d2292f05f74e93cf1b",
      "subject": "fix(setup): configure a comment-only Hermes config.yaml (#2096)",
      "body": "fix(setup): configure a comment-only Hermes config.yaml (#2096)\n\n* fix(setup): configure a comment-only Hermes config.yaml\n\ncomments, or only a `---` marker, also parses to a null YAML document.\nSetup still rejected it as malformed (\"expected record, received null\")\nand reported Hermes as invalid.\n\nTreat a null Hermes document as holding no settings, as #1983 does for\nan empty file. The serializer already edits a comment-only document in\nplace. A bare `---` document holds a null scalar that takes no keys, so\nreplace it with a map and keep the comments written after the marker.\n\n* fix(setup): keep rejecting an explicit null Hermes root\n\nOnly a document with no root, or a bare --- marker whose null scalar has\nno source text, holds no settings. An explicit null or ~ is a value, so\nsetup and uninstall reject it as before, the same as any other non-map\nroot.\n\n* test(setup): split the Hermes empty-configuration tests under the function length limit\n\nThe Hermes YAML registration block reached 159 lines, past oxlint's\nmax-lines-per-function limit of 150. Move the empty-document cases and\nthe multiple-document rejection into their own block.\n\n* fix(setup): type the Hermes edit document as a plain Document\n\nparseDocument with options returns a Document.Parsed, whose contents\naccept only parsed nodes, so assigning the new map for a bare --- root\nfailed typecheck (TS2322). Annotate the edited document as Document, as\nthe code did before it moved into HermesConfigurationYaml.ts.\n\n* fix(ci): isolate Linux Hopper process fixture inventory\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: morluto <76467478+morluto@users.noreply.github.com>",
