    {
      "sha": "c86b09a1095ffd360cd8851ff20a7b6aeb19b198",
      "subject": "feat(ghidra): admit 32-bit big-endian PowerPC ELF (#1747)",
      "body": "feat(ghidra): admit 32-bit big-endian PowerPC ELF (#1747)\n\n* feat(ghidra): admit 32-bit big-endian PowerPC ELF\n\nRecognize EM_PPC as a provider-neutral `powerpc` family that keeps its ELF\nclass, byte order, type and flags, and admit ELF32 big-endian ET_EXEC through\na bounded Ghidra lane. ELF64, little-endian, relocatable/shared objects and\nEF_PPC_EMB are refused with a specific reason; Hopper and IDA do not gain\nPowerPC support, and Windows Ghidra P0 is unchanged.\n\nGhidra's ELF loader selects PowerPC:BE:32:e500:default for a plain EM_PPC\nheader, which misreads 750-family code. The lane binds\nPowerPC:BE:32:default/default in the profile (language_selection\n\"admitted-lane-v1\"), imports with it and checks the reported language. A\nlanguage set through REA_GHIDRA_LANGUAGE_ID still replaces the lane default.\n\nAdd a source-owned fixture, fixed-encoding probe, GNU readelf cross-check and\nthe optional `verify:ghidra:ppc` real-provider lane, plus docs/ghidra-ppc.md.\n\nRefs #1741\n\n* style(ghidra): format shared PowerPC profile integration\n\n* fix(ghidra): preserve caller-selected PowerPC languages\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: morluto <76467478+morluto@users.noreply.github.com>",
