    {
      "sha": "1ebbc3b3714a83f10950eaa09bee5d4490bd572e",
      "subject": "fix(managed): pair members by declared identity before name-free remaps (#2116)",
      "body": "fix(managed): pair members by declared identity before name-free remaps (#2116)\n\n* fix(managed): pair members by declared identity before name-free remaps\n\nThe first matching round keyed methods on signature and normalized CIL,\nand fields on signature, without the declared type or name. Identical\nmembers of different types fell into one ambiguous group, so a file\ncompared with itself reported unknowns, and a lone match across types\nwas reported as an unchanged exact pair while the member's own\ncounterpart went unpaired.\n\nPair by declared type, name, and exact CIL/signature first, then by\ndeclared type, name, and raw signature. The name-free CIL/signature,\nfield-signature, and structural rounds now run last, as remaps, and\nskip a pair across declared identities while either member's own type\nand name remain unpaired on the other side.\n\nNested types that share a bare name still share one declared identity,\nso their identical members stay ambiguous in a self-comparison.\n\n* fix(managed): keep members with kept identities out of remap rounds\n\nThe cross-identity check applied only to one-to-one groups. A member\nwhose own declared type and name were still unpaired on the other side\ncould fall into a larger remap group and be reported ambiguous, and a\nblocked candidate could make an otherwise unique remap ambiguous.\n\nA remap round now drops such members before grouping, along with\nmembers whose declaring type is unresolved. Same-identity structural\npairs get their own round before the remaps. Each member's declared\nidentity is computed once.\n\nAmbiguity limitations now name the evidence a group shares, which\nstays true whether the round keyed on names or not.\n\n* fix(managed): keep names in unresolved identities and hold ambiguous ones\n\nA member of an unresolved declaring type had no declared identity, so\nthe declared-identity rounds keyed it by CIL or signature alone. Two\nunresolved members with different names paired as an exact match, and\na file compared with itself reported unresolved members ambiguous.\n\nThe declared identity now always includes the name, with a null type\nfor an unresolved one. Remap rounds still leave such members out.\n\nA remap round now also leaves out a member whose own identity sits in\nan ambiguous group on the other side, not only one left one-sided.\n\nThe undecoded-counterpart check uses the same declared identity.\n\n* fix(managed): keep remap groups with unresolved owners ambiguous\n\nRemap rounds dropped members of an unresolved declaring type before\ngrouping. Such a member can be another member's own counterpart, so a\nresolved member could remap to a copy in another type while its\nunresolved counterpart was reported added.\n\nUnresolved members now join remap grouping, and a group that contains\none stays ambiguous instead of pairing.\n\nThe undecoded-counterpart set reuses each member's computed identity.\n\n* fix(managed): keep ownerless members out of declared rounds when shared\n\nA member whose declaring type did not resolve has a declared identity\nof a null type and its name. The declared rounds paired two such\nsame-named members even when the other side also held a resolved\nmember with the same CIL and signature, which could be the owner. The\nold name-free first round reported that group as ambiguous.\n\nAn ownerless member now enters the declared rounds only when no other\nmember on either side shares its exact CIL/signature key, and never\nthe declared structural round. Otherwise it reaches the remap rounds,\nwhich keep any group with an unresolved member ambiguous.\n\n* fix(managed): keep competitors of an ownerless member out of the declared round\n\nWhen an ownerless member shares its exact CIL/signature key with another\nmember on the same side, its owner may be that member. The resolved\nmembers holding the key now stay out of the declared round too, so they\ncannot pair and consume the candidate the ownerless member may own, and\nthe remap round keeps the whole group ambiguous as main does. A lone\nownerless member still pairs with its lone counterpart.\n\n* test(managed): split the ownerless comparison tests under the function length limit\n\nThe ownerless describe block reached 181 lines, past oxlint's\nmax-lines-per-function limit of 150. Move the structural-competitor\ncase into its own block.\n\n* fix(managed): contest signatures and remap only open candidates\n\n* fix(managed): retain blocked raw-signature choices as unknown\n\n* fix(managed): keep member names in signature contention\n\n* fix(managed): scope residual signature contention by name once\n\nownerlessContested applies competitionIdentityKey itself, but\nunresolvedSignatureAmbiguities passed it keys that were already\nname-scoped, so the contested set never matched the groups and the\nsame-signature, different-body case reported additions and removals\ninstead of one unknown group. Pass the raw signature key.\n\n* fix(managed): constrain matchObserved to declared members\n\nmatchObserved passes its items to matchByKeys, which needs Declared, so\nits looser { declaring_type } bound failed typecheck (TS2344, TS2322).\n\n* fix(managed): retain held ownership contention for residual matches\n\n* fix(test): bind workspace fixture in Hopper launch cases\n\n* fix(ci): prepare worker tests and preserve Hopper cleanup ordering\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: morluto <76467478+morluto@users.noreply.github.com>",
