      "subject": "fix(browser): read expression-free template literals as module specifiers (#2842)",
      "body": "fix(browser): read expression-free template literals as module specifiers (#2842)\n\nCaptured-bundle chunk edges and source-map original module edges only\naccepted quoted string literals as import()/require() specifiers. Bundlers\nsuch as rolldown emit plain constants as expression-free template literals\n(import(`./chunk.js`)), so statically known dependencies were dropped while\ncompleteness stayed complete. Read both sites through the shared exact-literal\nreader (stringValue); template literals with substitutions stay unrecognized.\n\nOn OWASP Juice Shop v20.3.0 this recovers 8 lazy chunk edges (previously 0).\n\nFixes #2841\nFixes #2599\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: morluto <17176810+morluto@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: morluto <76467478+morluto@users.noreply.github.com>",
