      "sha": "97aff282018907e7e48dc67fc12043e1237e2c99",
      "subject": "fix(electron): reject non-executable paths and contain launch rejections (#2705)",
      "body": "fix(electron): reject non-executable paths and contain launch rejections (#2705)\n\n* fix(electron): reject non-executable paths and contain launch rejections\n\nAn executable_path that runs but never prints the inspector line made\nPlaywright's electron.launch() leave three waits unawaited. They rejected\nunhandled and Node ended the CLI or the MCP server (#2269).\n\nCheck the resolved executable_path is a regular file, and on non-Windows\nhosts that it passes X_OK, before any launch. Wrap only the launch call\nin a scoped unhandledRejection listener that absorbs rejections whose\nstack is in playwright-core/lib and re-throws anything else.\n\nTested on Linux with Node 22.23.1, 24.18.0 and 26.11.1.\n\nRefs #2269\n\n🤖 Generated with Claude Code (Sonnet 5.5, verified by Opus 5.5) 🦊\n\n* fix(electron): absorb only this launch's orphaned rejections\n\nThe listener around the launch dropped every rejection with a\nplaywright-core stack, so an unrelated Playwright failure during the\nlaunch window would vanish. Hold those rejections instead. When the\nlaunch settles, drop only the ones whose message is part of the launch's\nown error (the orphans of a failed launch). Raise every other one again\nthrough the unhandledRejection path, so the process still fails. A launch\nthat succeeds raises all of them. Rejections without a Playwright stack\nstill fail at once.\n\nOne setImmediate turn before the decision lets rejections queued by the\nsettling tick arrive first. It is a single turn, not a timer. A shared\nset of absorbed errors stops overlapping launches from raising each\nother's orphans. The listener is removed on every path.\n\nAdd child-process tests that drive the built provider through its launch\nseam, since Vitest's worker has its own unhandledRejection listener.\n\n🤖 Generated with Claude Code (Sonnet 5.5, verified by Opus 5.5) 🦊\n\n* test(electron): distinguish launch success from capture ownership\n\n* test(electron): assert cleanup ownership failures around overlapping launches\n\n* fix(comparison): recheck historical calls-only changes (#2223)\n\n* fix(comparison): preserve incomplete function call evidence\n\nKeep missing, unknown, partial and unresolved call relationships unknown in function comparisons and reconstruction claims. Aggregate IDA caller and callee coverage without overwriting uncertainty.\n\nValidate with 144 focused tests, typecheck/lint, docs checks and test discovery. Real providers were not verified; the full headless IDA session suite requires unavailable Windows native controls.\n\n* fix(comparison): recheck historical calls-only changes\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: morluto <76467478+morluto@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix(android): make DEX descriptor pattern portable\n\n* fix(ci): isolate Linux Hopper process fixture inventory\n\n* fix(browser): avoid replaying observed launch rejections\n\n* style: format comparison and IDA sources\n\n* test(electron): allow cold macOS ownership setup\n\n* test(electron): allow cold macOS setup in the early-exit path test\n\nThe test that runs an executable which exits at once builds the Swift\nownership helper twice on macOS: in the CLI process, and again in the\nMCP server process on its first tool call that prepares. A cold Swift\ncache can spend up to 120 seconds on a build. The test had only the\n30 second default.\n\nGive the test 180 seconds, as e1579ec31 did for\nelectronLaunchRejections.test.ts and 65a809a0d did for\nwebSourceLocationCli.test.ts. cli.run has no deadline of its own, so\nit needs no timeoutMs.\n\n🤖 Generated with Claude Code (Sonnet 5.5, verified by Opus 5.5) 🦊\n\n* test(ci): isolate report fixtures and declare PowerPC Java bounds\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <opus@fox.invalid>\nCo-authored-by: morluto <76467478+morluto@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Lucien <164857476+dakjdakd@users.noreply.github.com>",
