      "sha": "20e4f83097511090205c9f867c62bca0152e6676",
      "subject": "fix(ghidra): fail doctor when the JVM os.arch selects an unvalidated decompiler directory (#2792)",
      "body": "fix(ghidra): fail doctor when the JVM os.arch selects an unvalidated decompiler directory (#2792)\n\n* fix(ghidra): fail doctor when the JVM os.arch selects an unvalidated decompiler directory\n\nprobeJava now also reads the JVM os.arch property. When it maps to a\ndifferent native decompiler directory than the one validated from the\nhost architecture (for example an x86_64 JDK under Rosetta on Apple\nsilicon selecting os/mac_x86_64 while only mac_arm_64 was built), the\nnative_decompiler check fails with a remediation pointing at a\nmatching-arch JDK instead of reporting a healthy installation that\nfails every analysis. Unknown os.arch values keep the previous\nbehavior.\n\n* fix(ghidra): tighten JVM arch remediation and cover os.arch extraction\n\nAddress review findings on the JVM os.arch decompiler-directory check:\n- The remediation no longer suggests building the decompiler for the\n  JVM-selected directory, which could never clear the check; it only\n  advises pointing JAVA_HOME at a matching-architecture JDK.\n- Add a test running the real Java probe against captured\n  -XshowSettings:properties output, asserting os.arch reaches the\n  installation diagnostics.\n- Document the JDK-architecture prerequisite in the Ghidra setup guide.\n\n* fix(ghidra): refuse unrecognized JVM native architectures\n\n* docs(ghidra): align doctor prerequisites with JVM architecture admission\n\n* fix(ghidra): reject unreported JVM architecture\n\n* test(ghidra): separate JVM and executable admission cases\n\n* fix(ghidra): defer decompiler arch validation when Java is absent\n\n* fix(ghidra): reject JVM native architecture override\n\n* fix(ghidra): validate JVM platform overrides\n\n* fix(ghidra): validate JVM os.name and helper-environment platform overrides\n\n* test(ci): isolate report fixtures and declare PowerPC Java bounds\n\n* test(ghidra): provide observed JVM platform in PowerPC fixture\n\n* fix(ghidra): parse quoted JVM environment options before admission\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: morluto <76467478+morluto@users.noreply.github.com>",
