      "sha": "ec271121e4996f89f666a5a2ed1cd2f3229411b4",
      "subject": "fix(artifacts): preserve path identity and exclusion applicability",
      "body": "fix(artifacts): preserve path identity and exclusion applicability\n\nNormalize path facts once at the owning filesystem boundary, preserve caller spelling and unavailable inventory members, and retain typed read failures. Record exclusion entry kinds so only proven directories can establish descendant symlink targets; omitted legacy kinds stay unknown.\n\nReviewed fixes include #1969, #2642, #2759, and #2994.\n\nValidation: 26 reference graph source tests passed; prior artifact checks passed 275 tests with one Windows-only skip. Updated compiled import workflows are included in final validation after regeneration.\n",
      "parents": ["55dd21a5e2172187dfe7167df684f85ecb536f5e"],
      "authors": [
