      "subject": "fix(ghidra): preserve function facet and call coverage (#3002)",
      "body": "fix(ghidra): preserve function facet and call coverage (#3002)\n\n* fix(ghidra): preserve observed function facet and call coverage\n\nDeclare successful query availability in the Java producer, including explicit unavailable pseudocode reasons. Carry observed static call-set coverage through the parsed provider result and Evidence without inventing facts for legacy omissions. Use Ghidra indexed comment addresses over the function body and entry, retaining cancellation checks and sparse collection.\n\nCloses #2951\n\nCo-authored-by: Kaoru0822 <208281322+kaoru0822-kitauji@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix(ghidra): retain unresolved call coverage in observations\n\nShare decoded unresolved-call facts between dossiers, callee coverage and reference observations. Combine terminal and unresolved observations in one instruction traversal and retain site records only when requested. Keep missing procedure identities incomplete and validate unresolved locations at the provider boundary.\n\nBind snapshots to the corrected call coverage profile so older complete claims cannot replay under the new semantics. Add real public MCP callback trace/comparison regressions.\n\nCo-authored-by: Kaoru0822 <208281322+kaoru0822-kitauji@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix(ghidra): separate reference targets from callee coverage\n\nReuse containing-function ownership for resolved reference identities and independently compare those identities with the actual returned callee set. Keep known interior routes out of unresolved site records while retaining partial inventory coverage.\n\nAdvance the coverage profile to v3 and reject interim v2 cache bindings. Add a real Ghidra producer regression with restored reference metadata; the previous bridge fails the known-route assertion.\n\nCo-authored-by: Kaoru0822 <208281322+kaoru0822-kitauji@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix(ghidra): measure incoming call coverage across function bodies\n\nCompare incoming reference source identities across the owned function body and entry with the actual returned caller set. Stream caller-only checks and reuse dossier reference observations. Combine caller/callee coverage from observed counts without reinterpreting serialized metadata, and share the body scope owner with comments and references.\n\nBind snapshots to function-body coverage semantics v4 and preserve the real off-entry caller regression.\n\nCo-authored-by: Kaoru0822 <208281322+kaoru0822-kitauji@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix(ghidra): preserve whole-scope directional call coverage\n\nCheck body-and-entry call references independently of decoded instruction flow. Reuse collected dossier references and stream inventory-only coverage checks. Keep caller-only gaps distinct from incomplete outgoing coverage in offline path reconstruction, and invalidate prior snapshot profiles.\n\nCo-authored-by: Kaoru0822 <208281322+kaoru0822-kitauji@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix(mcp): retain compact Evidence field types\n\nShare optional diagnostics across the three tagged relationship coverage states instead of advertising duplicate branches. Preserve coverage validation while keeping compact Evidence properties within the existing reference expansion budget. Verify invalid direction cardinalities against the actual SDK-advertised schema.\n\nCo-authored-by: Kaoru0822 <208281322+kaoru0822-kitauji@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Kaoru0822 <208281322+kaoru0822-kitauji@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: morluto <76467478+morluto@users.noreply.github.com>",
