      "sha": "679658b28748729c9b881497e680c811a708f5f3",
      "subject": "fix(reference): report entries beyond the path limit as I/O failures (#2716)",
      "body": "fix(reference): report entries beyond the path limit as I/O failures (#2716)\n\n* fix(reference): report entries beyond the path limit as I/O failures\n\nReference-source traversal joins each child onto the root path. A valid\ntree whose nested entries exceed the platform's absolute path limit\n(PATH_MAX 1024 on macOS) makes lstat fail with ENAMETOOLONG. The\nreader's filesystem error allow-list lacked that code, so\nfilesystemFailureDetail returned undefined and the native rejection\nescaped both readReferenceSource and importReferenceSource instead of\nbecoming the existing failed `io` entry.\n\nAdd ENAMETOOLONG to the allow-list, matching the JavaScript application\nreader's list. Readable siblings stay in the graph and the unreachable\nentry is recorded with its OS message.\n\nFixes #2652\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(reference): assert the imported graph keeps readable and failed entries\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(process): report no remaining time after a provider deadline fires\n\nNode timers can fire while performance.now() is still a fraction of a\nmillisecond short of the monotonic deadline. ProviderStartupDeadline then\nreported interruption \"timeout\" and an aborted signal while remainingMs()\nreturned ceil(0.x) = 1, so polling loops guarded by remainingMs() > 0\n(Hopper and Ghidra startup) could run past an elapsed deadline, and the\nreal-timer test \"aborts a bounded wait when its real monotonic deadline\nexpires\" failed intermittently in CI (expected 1 to be 0).\n\nOnce the deadline's own timer has classified a timeout, report zero\nremaining time. A deterministic regression test fires the timer with the\nmonotonic clock 0.4 ms short of the deadline.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(reference): preserve path limit entry uncertainty\n\n* fix(reference): preserve unknown entry failures and identity\n\n* fix(reference): type unknown-kind exclusions and keep them out of symlink counts\n\nThe metadata-failure path offers \"unknown\" to exclusion predicates, but\nthe predicate type only admitted concrete kinds, which broke the build.\nDirectory-only secret and ignore rules now also match an unknown-kind\nentry (it may be a directory), and the summary counts unknown entries\nseparately instead of as symlinks.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: morluto <76467478+morluto@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Codex <codex@users.noreply.github.com>",
