    {
      "sha": "04672f2b917d7ae3d71424a6abbcc2da0f24fa0b",
      "subject": "fix(javascript): preserve builtin identity and share alias traversal",
      "body": "fix(javascript): preserve builtin identity and share alias traversal\n\nTrack module writes and escapes at their owner, preserve capture and reassignment ordering, and share CommonJS/default namespace identity without erasing parent-slot changes. Carry write sites into ambient alias resolution and use parsed write targets across consumers. Deduplicate returned-reference work with cycle context; retain unchanged temporal selection identity so provenance memoization stays effective.\n\nReviewed fixes include #2041, #2465, #2830, #2881, and #2948. Remove superseded mutation representations and the ineffective per-markValue dedup layer.\n\nValidation: 380 focused JavaScript tests passed under a 384 MiB heap cap, including the previously aborting 30-level/128-call alias regression. Six public CLI/MCP builtin tests passed. Exact pdf.js completed-workflow performance remains unmeasured.\n",
      "parents": ["0f4c484be552a4d5e8e1d0fa072441bfa900c815"],
      "authors": [
