      "subject": "fix(native): classify every Swift mangling prefix as invalid when undecodable (#3089)",
      "body": "fix(native): classify every Swift mangling prefix as invalid when undecodable (#3089)\n\n* fix(native): classify every Swift mangling prefix as invalid when undecodable\n\ndemangle_swift reported \"invalid\" only for $s and _$s inputs that\nswift-demangle left unchanged. Undecodable symbols carrying the other\nprefixes the Swift demangler accepts (_T0, $S, _$S, @__swiftmacro_, $e,\n_$e) were reported as \"unchanged\", i.e. as non-Swift names. Legacy _T\nstays \"unchanged\" because it is also an ordinary C symbol spelling.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(native): expect only toolchain-portable Swift manglings to demangle\n\nThe macOS 15 runner's swift-demangle predates Embedded Swift, so valid\n$e symbols stay unchanged there. Keep $e and _$e in the undecodable\nhalf only.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
