    {
      "sha": "74844016018dfdb171132c0d1d2c937905b16d1f",
      "subject": "perf(managed): add retained member summary and pages (#3061)",
      "body": "perf(managed): add retained member summary and pages (#3061)\n\n* perf(managed): add retained member summary and pages\n\ninspect_managed_members always returned the assembly-wide member_refs, so\none selected or unmatched type produced megabytes, and an unselected\nordinary assembly exceeded the MCP response budget. Add opt-in\ndetail: \"summary\" that retains the complete Evidence and returns identity,\nselection with unmatched names, coverage, user-string coverage, limitations\nand per-collection counts. Page original rows through inspect_analysis_view\nwith kind managed-members; each page names its collection so no row schema\nis chosen by union order. Complete delivery stays the default.\n\nRefs #3010\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* perf(managed): validate a sealed member parent once across pages\n\nEach managed-members page reparsed the whole parent report, about 35 ms\nfor an 18 MB assembly result regardless of the page size. The analysis\nview service now reports whether the parent Evidence is a sealed\nsnapshot, and the member view reuses the validated report for that\nsealed result through a weak reference. Unsealed input is still\nvalidated on every call.\n\nThe round-trip test fixture now carries an exported type, an ldstr\nliteral, a field access and a call edge, and requires every collection\nto be nonempty so a row schema that drops facts cannot pass on empty\narrays.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(managed): keep delivery detail out of retained Evidence identity\n\nSummary, omitted and complete delivery of the same managed inspection\nnow retain one parent record, as inspect_macho already does.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
      "parents": ["7375ab6e34e511095a74d5a67e57cec28d56fd10"],
      "authors": [
        {
