    {
      "sha": "e5791229f3d64e3b3ccc9d839b8e4c567e97cc98",
      "subject": "perf(native): skip llvm-nm's dyld-info pass when the symbol table names every export (#3200)",
      "body": "perf(native): skip llvm-nm's dyld-info pass when the symbol table names every export (#3200)\n\n* perf(native): skip llvm-nm's dyld-info pass when the symbol table names every export\n\ninspect_macho ran `nm -gjU`, whose default dyld-info pass takes seconds on\nlarge apps (Keynote arm64 5.8 s, x86_64 10.2 s) yet under -gU can only add\nexport-trie names that dyld_info -exports already reports. Run\n`nm -gjU --no-dyldinfo` and rerun the default pass only when dyld_info\nreports an export the symbol table lacks (e.g. strip -T), so its exact\nnames still disambiguate dyld_info rows.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(native): fall back to nm's dyld-info pass for unreadable export rows\n\nAccount for every dyld_info export line instead of only the rows the\nparser returns, so an unfamiliar row format reruns the default nm pass.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
