    {
      "sha": "bdacd4140ef68d6860b70867d058939d0b4d37d1",
      "subject": "fix(sqlite): keep a retained worker owner after a failed worker exit (#3242)",
      "body": "fix(sqlite): keep a retained worker owner after a failed worker exit (#3242)\n\n* fix: abort invalid JSON parses and keep retained worker owners\n\nMain (7375ab6e3) fails four boundary tests from its latest batch.\n\n- f79fd59e9 moved JSON value validation into a non-aborting superRefine, so\n  authenticated Evidence still computed its recursive identity digest over\n  a 10,000-level `parameters` value and overflowed the stack. The process\n  comparison CLI then reported \"Maximum call stack size exceeded\" instead of\n  the depth limit. Abort the parse on a JSON validation issue so enclosing\n  refinements never walk invalid data.\n- runOwnedCommand retains an incomplete cleanup through retainCleanup and\n  then rethrows the command failure without a cleanupOwner. The EVM and SQLite\n  providers replaced their retained owner with that undefined value, so an\n  output-limit failure with unresolved cleanup lost cleanupIncomplete and its\n  owner. Keep the retained owner unless the failure carries one.\n- The EVM malformed-reply test expected a nonexistent `output_failure` code;\n  AnalysisOutputError projects to `unreadable_output`. The pcap capinfos stub\n  prints its report with a trailing newline, which retained output preserves.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(sqlite): keep a retained worker owner after a failed worker exit\n\nCover the path the existing worker-cleanup test bypasses: a real owned worker\nexits nonzero, runOwnedCommand retains its incomplete cleanup and rethrows the\nfailure without a cleanupOwner. The provider must still report\ncleanupIncomplete and block a new worker until the retained cleanup succeeds.\nFails on the previous owner assignment.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(evm): retain the compact worker failure beside retained cleanup\n\nWhen the worker command fails and its cleanup is retained, the cleanup error\nnow reports the primary failure in the same compact form as an unretained\ncommand cleanup failure: failure kind, message, exit code and signal. Its\noutput is already retained once as captured_output, so the previous error no\nlonger repeats up to a megabyte of diagnostics, and failure_kind stays at the\ntop level that the provider test reads. Both paths share\nownedCommandPreviousError.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
      "parents": ["307af044bc0bdc15bc836c549e774220af8f459e"],
