    {
      "sha": "cf6ea097116bdf3578b1e02e35c772d8aa92db00",
      "subject": "fix(setup): refuse linked skill installation directories (#3108)",
      "body": "fix(setup): refuse linked skill installation directories (#3108)\n\nValidate final selected skill roots and references before preview, approval,\nand client/Hopper changes, with a repeated installation-boundary check.\nPreserve interactive unselected-client choices and registration-only setup.\n\nShare typed directory/read observations across setup, doctor, and update;\nreport unmanaged paths and unknown reads with actionable paths/reasons.\nRetain uninstall child outcomes and ownership manifests when cleanup remains.\n\nShared single-pass inspection retains all unreadable paths after stale or\nmissing files and keeps observed metadata, without duplicate manifest reads.\nAbsent installed files do not depend on generated bundled bytes.\n\nValidation: 217 related tests, 41 final CLI/MCP and filesystem checks, and all\n7,446 source tests in 508 files pass (eight platform/condition skips).\nStatic/docs checks pass. Normal four-call\ninstall/rerun/repair/uninstall tasks preserve results and output token counts.\nNo native Windows follow-up or arbitrary concurrent swap containment claim.\n\nFixes #3057.\n\nCo-authored-by: geekwolf <3125615+geekwolf@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: N0zoM1z0 <161784452+N0zoM1z0@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Kaoru0822 <208281322+kaoru0822-kitauji@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: akushonkamen <74654766+akushonkamen@users.noreply.github.com>",
      "parents": ["90d4098a01b62d0e00dd79376465c2243aff800d"],
      "authors": [
