    {
      "sha": "e5828596c50029e48feb7f56d6f5fe7b5580a561",
      "subject": "fix(artifacts): inventory universal slices REA cannot structurally index (#3283)",
      "body": "fix(artifacts): inventory universal slices REA cannot structurally index (#3283)\n\n* fix(artifacts): inventory universal slices REA cannot structurally index\n\ninspect_artifact and extract_artifact rejected a valid universal Mach-O\nwhen one slice was outside the structural index, such as XLD's\nbig-endian PowerPC slice. The whole inventory failed with \"Artifact is\ninvalid or has changed. Get a fresh copy and try again.\"\n\nWhen lipo reports every slice's range, the slices are now inventoried\nfrom those ranges with a limitation naming the unsupported structure,\nas the reader already does for files without structural facts. When\nlipo omits a range, the failure is reported as unavailable support\nrather than a corrupt artifact.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(artifacts): validate every FAT slice past an unsupported one\n\nreadFatSlices returned at the first unsupported slice, so a later\nmalformed slice went unchecked: with lipo's ranges now inventoried for\nunsupported structure, a malformed little-endian slice after a\nbig-endian one was accepted while the reverse order was rejected.\nUnsupported slices are now remembered and the remaining slices are\nstill validated, so malformed structure wins in either order.\n\nAdds portable fake-lipo coverage for complete ranges, missing ranges\n(unavailable) and malformed slices on both sides of a big-endian slice.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
